#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0350_000_0
#. timeline 19379..19853
#: codec/1/175/0xaf200/18
msgid ""
"Now wouldn't that be something...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/0
msgid ""
"Enemies that steal your items will try and escape\n"
"the area.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/1
msgid ""
"Make it a priority to take them out first.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/2
msgid ""
"Don't let them make off with your stuff.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/3
msgid ""
"We're seeing multiple hostiles in this area.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/4
msgid ""
"It's not going to be easy going it alone.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xaf8f0/5
msgid ""
"I'd recommend taking this one on as a two-man cell\n"
"in CO-OPS.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xafb40/0
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you could try planting Claymores\n"
"along the routes they walk.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xafb40/1
msgid ""
"We need you to stop that nuke, Boss.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xafb40/2
msgid ""
"We'll keep you safe, no matter what it takes!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xafca0/0
msgid ""
"It's going to take more than small arms fire to take\n"
"down a truck.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xafca0/1
msgid ""
"Some kind of rocket's your best bet.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xafca0/2
msgid ""
"Another tactic to try would be setting off an\n"
"explosion from afar.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xafca0/3
msgid ""
"You could also call in a support strike,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/175/0xafca0/4
msgid ""
"if you can manage to tag them with a marker...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/176/0xb00d0/0
msgid ""
"You'll be using C4 for demolition.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/176/0xb00d0/1
msgid ""
"As you might imagine, it's gonna make a big noise\n"
"when it detonates.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/176/0xb00d0/2
msgid ""
"For your own safety, make sure you put plenty of\n"
"distance\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/176/0xb00d0/3
msgid ""
"between yourself and the C4 before detonating it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/176/0xb0290/0
msgid ""
"Boss, we're not sure where your gear is being\n"
"stored.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/176/0xb0350/0
msgid ""
"Amanda and her crew tell me they've managed to\n"
"identify several different categories\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/176/0xb0350/1
msgid ""
"of mercenaries employed by the CIA.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/176/0xb0350/2
msgid ""
"Give me a rundown. Sounds like info I could use.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/176/0xb0350/3
msgid ""
"No problem. I'll go through them in order.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 445..1058
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/0
msgid ""
"The type of enemy you'll be seeing most\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 1058..2368
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/1
msgid ""
"is the type that patrols and guards a specific\n"
"operational area.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 2396..3775
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/2
msgid ""
"For the sake of convenience, Amanda's crew calls\n"
"the outdoor ones \"patrolmen,\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 3775..4374
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/3
msgid ""
"and the indoor ones \"guards.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 4388..5043
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/4
msgid ""
"They might look like they're just out for a stroll,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 5043..5907
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/5
msgid ""
"but don't be fooled - they're sharper than they\n"
"look.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 5948..6757
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/6
msgid ""
"All of their senses are finely honed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 6812..7592
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/7
msgid ""
"Normally they'll patrol along fixed routes,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 7592..8818
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/8
msgid ""
"but when the alert level is raised they'll assume a\n"
"more efficient alert posture\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 8818..10156
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/9
msgid ""
"and focus on defending specific points. That's bad\n"
"for you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 10253..10978
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/10
msgid ""
"Obviously they can hold their own in combat,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 10978..12051
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/11
msgid ""
"and with body armor it'll be even harder to take\n"
"them down.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 12106..12692
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/12
msgid ""
"If they're wearing a bulletproof helmet,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 12705..13876
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/13
msgid ""
"you can forget about one-shot kills. Just a heads\n"
"up.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 13945..15116
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/14
msgid ""
"You'll need to be smart about using camo and pick\n"
"your routes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0520_000_0
#. timeline 15144..16063
#: codec/1/176/0xb0510/15
msgid ""
"The most important thing is to avoid detection.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 445..1852
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/0
msgid ""
"When the enemy spots you and goes on alert, they\n"
"may call in a backup strike team.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 1866..3120
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/1
msgid ""
"These assault teams are heavily armed, well\n"
"trained, and highly dangerous.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 3134..3873
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/2
msgid ""
"Amanda's crew calls them \"commandos.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 3900..5670
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/3
msgid ""
"Unlike the patrolmen, these guys will actively,\n"
"relentlessly track and hunt you down - like hounds.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 6032..7216
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/4
msgid ""
"Hounds to hunt a former FOXHOUND... Bring it on.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 7244..8080
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/5
msgid ""
"They won't give up easily even if they lose sight of\n"
"you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 8080..9083
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/6
msgid ""
"They'll clear out any likely hiding places they come\n"
"across.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 9097..10267
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/7
msgid ""
"So don't get too comfy in one spot or you might\n"
"get caught again.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 10281..11173
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/8
msgid ""
"Keep your eyes fixed on them and what they're\n"
"doing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 11229..12329
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/9
msgid ""
"Also, be aware that commando gear includes body\n"
"armor.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 12329..13305
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/10
msgid ""
"So don't think you can deal with them by going in\n"
"guns blazing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 13305..14405
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/11
msgid ""
"All I've got to do is find an exposed weak point\n"
"and...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0530_000_0
#. timeline 14405..14767
#: codec/1/176/0xb0af0/12
msgid ""
"Exactly.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/0
msgid ""
"There's one type of commando you really need to\n"
"watch out for,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/1
msgid ""
"and that's the kind toting shotguns.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/2
msgid ""
"They can take a few hits and still keep charging\n"
"you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/3
msgid ""
"And believe me, you don't want them closing in\n"
"between those shotgun blasts.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/4
msgid ""
"When they start charging, you need to stop them\n"
"immediately.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1000/5
msgid ""
"Use something with serious stopping power.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 459..1643
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/0
msgid ""
"We've also confirmed that some of the enemies\n"
"specialize in ambushes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 1657..2424
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/1
msgid ""
"Amanda's crew calls them \"scouts.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 2479..3510
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/2
msgid ""
"They'll blend themselves in with the terrain and the\n"
"vegetation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 3538..4263
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/3
msgid ""
"Then, when they see you, they'll swoop in.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 4318..4876
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/4
msgid ""
"They fight pretty much like commandos\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 4876..5670
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/5
msgid ""
"and will use clearing techniques to flush you out.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 5726..7049
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/6
msgid ""
"In addition to wielding normal weapons, the scouts\n"
"also carry wires.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 7077..8178
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/7
msgid ""
"Hm... Sounds like these guys know their CQC.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 8192..9640
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/8
msgid ""
"Could be. We've been getting reports of CQC\n"
"attacks being blocked by wires.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0550_000_0
#. timeline 9668..10031
#: codec/1/177/0xb1290/9
msgid ""
"Stay alert.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/0
msgid ""
"Scouts are outfitted with camouflage to help them\n"
"hide.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/1
msgid ""
"Some of them look kind of weird, like they've got\n"
"seaweed growing all over them.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/2
msgid ""
"Ah, ghillie suits.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/3
msgid ""
"Not much difference between them and any other\n"
"scout in terms of combat ability,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/4
msgid ""
"but it does make them harder to spot.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/5
msgid ""
"I'm sure it does.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/6
msgid ""
"You've come across these before?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/7
msgid ""
"Yeah. The Soviet Union...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/8
msgid ""
"The first time, it took me a full hour to find the\n"
"guy and take him out...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/9
msgid ""
"Kaz, do you know if they shine?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/10
msgid ""
"...Shine. Like how?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/11
msgid ""
"Like from their heads.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/12
msgid ""
"Their heads?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/13
msgid ""
"How about their hair? Do they have a lot of it?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/14
msgid ""
"What are you talking about? How the hell would I\n"
"know?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/15
msgid ""
"How about a parrot? Did anybody hear a parrot\n"
"squawk?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/16
msgid ""
"A parrot? Look, Snake, you're talking to the wrong\n"
"guy.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/17
msgid ""
"I mean, Cecile's the bird expert...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/18
msgid ""
"Wait a second, what am I saying? You're not\n"
"making any sense to begin with!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/19
msgid ""
"Never mind. It's... a long story. I'll figure out another\n"
"way. Forget about it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/20
msgid ""
"Yeah, I'll do that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/21
msgid ""
"Anyway, we've already lost too many good people\n"
"to these surprise encounters.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1640/22
msgid ""
"Make sure you don't end up like one of them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0570_000_0
#. timeline 445..1128
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/0
msgid ""
"There are areas out there where enemy soldiers\n"
"are\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0570_000_0
#. timeline 1128..2048
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/1
msgid ""
"deployed in multiple layers for extra coverage.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0570_000_0
#. timeline 2075..2995
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/2
msgid ""
"More than a few of those will be attacking you\n"
"from a distance\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0570_000_0
#. timeline 60749..11426
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/3
msgid ""
"- rooftops and far-off vantage points.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/4
msgid ""
"Try not to get too distracted by nearby enemies,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/5
msgid ""
"because you could be leaving yourself wide open\n"
"to longer-range attacks.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 7356..7787
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0140_000_0
#. timeline 5517..5921
#: codec/1/177/0xb1db0/6
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/8
#: codec/1/205/0xcd600/5
msgid ""
"I'll be careful.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 445..1030
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/0
msgid ""
"Enemy tanks, armored vehicles,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 1030..2173
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/1
msgid ""
"and attack choppers are always accompanied by a\n"
"combat squad.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 2229..3051
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/2
msgid ""
"The soldiers aren't particularly tough on their own.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 3078..4263
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/3
msgid ""
"What makes them formidable is how well they work\n"
"together as a team.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 4291..5126
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/4
msgid ""
"As if you didn't have enough to worry about with\n"
"the machine.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 5140..5795
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/5
msgid ""
"Good. I like a challenge.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 5809..7035
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/6
msgid ""
"Yeah, well, see how you feel when you actually\n"
"have to face them in battle.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 7091..8052
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/7
msgid ""
"Snake, whatever you do, don't let them surround\n"
"you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 8066..9097
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/8
msgid ""
"The last thing you need is to get pushed into the\n"
"vehicle's kill zone.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 9153..10086
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/9
msgid ""
"And pay attention to what your enemies say to\n"
"each other.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 10114..11201
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/10
msgid ""
"You can improve your chances by figuring out\n"
"what they're planning\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 11215..11939
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/11
msgid ""
"and using it to preempt their movements.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 11967..12845
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/12
msgid ""
"You don't always have to go toe to toe to win a\n"
"fight.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 12873..13500
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/13
msgid ""
"Think like a guerrilla.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 459..1476
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/0
msgid ""
"Enemies carrying shields can be a real pain in the\n"
"ass.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 1532..2424
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/1
msgid ""
"To hear Amanda tell it, trying to fight those\n"
"bastards\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 2424..3371
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/2
msgid ""
"while they sit behind their shields taking pistol\n"
"shots at you\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 3385..4109
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/3
msgid ""
"is enough to make you want to rip your hair out.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 4165..4778
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/4
msgid ""
"Get around and flank them if you can.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 4820..5976
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/5
msgid ""
"You might want to try blinding them with smoke or\n"
"stun grenades first.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 6046..7509
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/6
msgid ""
"Also, armor-piercing rounds should make it a little\n"
"easier to punch through their shields.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0590_000_0
#. timeline 7551..8066
#: codec/1/178/0xb25a0/7
msgid ""
"Use 'em if you've got 'em.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 459..1769
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/0
msgid ""
"We know there are variations in the kinds of gear\n"
"patrolmen and commandos wear,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 1769..2284
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/1
msgid ""
"especially the body armor.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 2326..3510
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/2
msgid ""
"Our scouts report that an enemy's defense and\n"
"firing accuracy\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 3510..4472
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/3
msgid ""
"are directly proportional to how heavy their gear is.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 4750..5628
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/4
msgid ""
"Those must be the guys with the highest combat\n"
"skills.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 5656..6659
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/5
msgid ""
"They can fight in heavier gear without their\n"
"performance suffering.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 6673..7857
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/6
msgid ""
"Supposedly it's pretty easy to tell the difference in\n"
"gear just by looking.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 7927..8233
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/7
msgid ""
"So remember:\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0640_000_0
#. timeline 8233..9334
#: codec/1/178/0xb28e0/8
msgid ""
"use extra caution when dealing with enemies\n"
"wearing heavy gear.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/178/0xb2c50/0
msgid ""
"Enemies will try to fight you from different\n"
"distances\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/178/0xb2c50/1
msgid ""
"based on the weapon they've got equipped.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/178/0xb2c50/2
msgid ""
"When you meet an enemy, get a good look at what\n"
"they're carrying\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/178/0xb2c50/3
msgid ""
"- it can make or break your chances in battle.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/178/0xb2e10/0
msgid ""
"Enemies carrying handguns and shotguns will try\n"
"and get in close.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/178/0xb2e10/1
msgid ""
"That makes them dangerous, but at the same time\n"
"easier to hit.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/178/0xb2e10/2
msgid ""
"Keep you wits about you and you can turn a threat\n"
"into an opportunity.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/0
msgid ""
"Don't expect enemies carrying sniper rifles\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/1
msgid ""
"or rocket launchers to get up close and personal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/2
msgid ""
"They'll be constantly moving from place to place\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/3
msgid ""
"looking for an opening to snipe at you. Tricky\n"
"bastards.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/4
msgid ""
"Eye for an eye, tooth for a tooth, - go with the\n"
"sniper rifle.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/5
msgid ""
"Make sure you stay out of their line of sight,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/179/0xb3140/6
msgid ""
"and when they expose themselves, take 'em down!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/179/0xb33f0/0
#: codec/1/179/0xb3490/0
#: codec/1/179/0xb3530/0
#: codec/1/179/0xb35d0/0
#: codec/1/179/0xb3670/0
msgid ""
"(dummy. not used)\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 473..1226
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/0
msgid ""
"Costa Rica means \"rich coast\" in Spanish.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 1267..2089
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/1
msgid ""
"Is it true that Columbus was the one who came up\n"
"with the name?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 2173..3092
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/2
msgid ""
"Your guess is as good as mine. But it is true\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 3092..4388
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/3
msgid ""
"that Columbus landed his ships near Limón back in\n"
"the Age of Exploration.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 4458..5154
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/4
msgid ""
"He wrote in his diary that when he landed,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 5224..6352
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/5
msgid ""
"the indígena showered him with gifts of gold.\n"
"Hence the name.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 6394..6938
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/6
msgid ""
"It sounds a little strange to me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 7007..7955
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/7
msgid ""
"There is no way they could find that much gold in\n"
"Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 7983..9153
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/8
msgid ""
"Columbus originally set sail in search of the\n"
"legendary land of gold.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 9320..9961
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/9
msgid ""
"Maybe he was just nuts about the stuff.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 9975..10644
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/10
msgid ""
"Costa Rica is rich enough without it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 10727..11800
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/11
msgid ""
"Look at the forests and the animals, and the\n"
"peace-loving people...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 11814..12329
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/12
msgid ""
"That is what I want to protect.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0010_000_0
#. timeline 12357..12914
#: codec/1/179/0xb3710/13
msgid ""
"...I know how you feel.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 473..1825
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/0
msgid ""
"Democracy took root in Costa Rica before\n"
"anywhere else in Central America.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 1894..3162
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/1
msgid ""
"Sure, we had coups and dictators and all, but\n"
"never a total meltdown.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 3287..4026
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/2
msgid ""
"That is, until 26 years ago...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 4082..5726
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/3
msgid ""
"The civil war. Yeah, I understand you lost your\n"
"grandparents.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 5753..6868
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/4
msgid ""
"It started with a dispute over alleged fraud in the\n"
"presidential election.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 6993..8108
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/5
msgid ""
"What I don't understand is why friend turned\n"
"against friend\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 8192..8735
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/6
msgid ""
"when they could have talked it out instead.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0020_000_0
#. timeline 8832..9613
#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/7
msgid ""
"Yeah, that... would have been nice.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/8
msgid ""
"Even today, some buildings still have bullet holes\n"
"from the civil war.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/9
msgid ""
"A quarter century later, and it is a tragedy we\n"
"ticos cannot forget... Must not forget.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/179/0xb3be0/10
msgid ""
"It was the year after the civil war that the army\n"
"was constitutionally abolished.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/0
msgid ""
"A new president was elected this year - President\n"
"Oduber.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/1
msgid ""
"He seems to be distancing himself from the United\n"
"States.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/2
msgid ""
"He's limited the privileges granted to American\n"
"banks, lifted the sanctions on Cuba...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/3
msgid ""
"Our last president was so pro-U.S., people\n"
"suspected he was in bed with the CIA.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/4
msgid ""
"You think the CIA's doing this because it feels\n"
"threatened by the president's shift in policy...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/5
msgid ""
"It is possible. But would they really bring in such a\n"
"huge army just because of that?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/6
msgid ""
"Part of our job is finding out.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb4050/7
msgid ""
"Exactly. Thanks, Snake. Peace.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 487..1755
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/0
msgid ""
"So are you a student at the University for Peace,\n"
"Paz?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 1797..2410
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/1
msgid ""
"No, I am still in high school.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 2479..3761
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/2
msgid ""
"But Professor Gálvez lets me visit his office and\n"
"study with him every now and then.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 3817..5419
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/3
msgid ""
"International law, security, conflict resolution,\n"
"human rights...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 5489..6729
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/4
msgid ""
"We study all these subjects and then use them to\n"
"build the foundations of peace.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 6798..8373
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/5
msgid ""
"Yeah, I get it... I'd just never heard the UN had a\n"
"University for Peace before.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 8387..10685
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/6
msgid ""
"Oh, that. Well, to be precise, it is still being set up.\n"
"They have started conducting research, but\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 10741..11563
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/7
msgid ""
"the UN has not passed the necessary resolution\n"
"yet.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 11633..12260
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/8
msgid ""
"Professor Gálvez couldn't wait that long...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 12274..12928
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/9
msgid ""
"Oh, uh, right.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 12942..13514
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/10
msgid ""
"Costa Rica abolished its army,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 13555..14586
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/11
msgid ""
"and has also hosted the Central American Court of\n"
"Justice.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 14614..15993
#: codec/1/180/0xb43c0/12
msgid ""
"It is the perfect place to build a university like\n"
"ours, don't you think?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/0
msgid ""
"Professor Gálvez was a KGB spy...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/1
msgid ""
"I thought he helped me out of genuine concern for\n"
"Costa Rica's future...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/2
msgid ""
"You didn't know?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/3
msgid ""
"How could I?! Believe me, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/4
msgid ""
"He introduced himself as a peace researcher at\n"
"the university.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/5
msgid ""
"He had an office and credentials and everything...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/6
msgid ""
"They're masters at creating cover personas. They\n"
"think of everything\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/7
msgid ""
"- ID papers, jobs, sometimes even families.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/8
msgid ""
"Don't feel bad you didn't see through it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/9
msgid ""
"But you did?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/10
msgid ""
"From the first time we met.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/11
msgid ""
"I wish you'd told me...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/12
msgid ""
"Sorry. I didn't know if it'd be right.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/13
msgid ""
"You might have gotten mixed up in things you\n"
"shouldn't.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/14
msgid ""
"That is impressive, though. Sizing him up him at a\n"
"single glance.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/15
msgid ""
"He reeked.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/16
msgid ""
"Reeked?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/17
msgid ""
"He had this unmistakable air about him...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/18
msgid ""
"The air of someone who's been given a mission\n"
"and will see it through no matter what.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/19
msgid ""
"Like me. I could just smell it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/20
msgid ""
"That is amazing, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/21
msgid ""
"Nah, I'm just kidding. It was his prosthetic hand.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/22
msgid ""
"Why would a professor from a peace university\n"
"need a tool for assassination?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/180/0xb48c0/23
msgid ""
"...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 473..1365
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/0
msgid ""
"Are there any large-scale ruins in Costa Rica, Paz?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 1407..2410
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/1
msgid ""
"There's a place east of Cartago called Guayabo.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 2493..3232
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/2
msgid ""
"They have ruins there, but they're not especially\n"
"big.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 3650..4486
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/3
msgid ""
"Not the place I'm thinking of... Any others?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 4527..5935
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/4
msgid ""
"Well, if you go a little way across the border into\n"
"Nicaragua,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 6004..8219
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/5
msgid ""
"there's a place called La Fortaleza de la\n"
"Inmaculada Concepción. That's the only famous one.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 8261..9195
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/6
msgid ""
"Then what were those ruins I saw from up on\n"
"Irazu...?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 9250..10783
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/7
msgid ""
"There are a lot of things we still do not know\n"
"about Costa Rica's ancient civilizations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 10839..11730
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/8
msgid ""
"There are giant stone spheres throughout the\n"
"country.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0070_000_1
#. timeline 11814..12719
#: codec/1/181/0xb54b0/9
msgid ""
"What they were used for is still a mystery.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/0
msgid ""
"Paz, you said Costa Rica has no army, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/1
msgid ""
"Correct. Article 12 of the constitution declared\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/2
msgid ""
"that the army as a permanent institution is\n"
"abolished.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/3
msgid ""
"It does permit us to organize armed forces for\n"
"national defense\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/4
msgid ""
"based on inter-American treaties.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/5
msgid ""
"Only temporarily, then.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/6
msgid ""
"In effect, yes. But in the years since the\n"
"constitution took effect,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/181/0xb58a0/7
msgid ""
"Costa Rica has not once raised an army.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 473..1783
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/0
msgid ""
"The army was abolished 25 years ago, the year\n"
"after the civil war.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 1894..2869
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/1
msgid ""
"I learned about the sorrow of civil war from a very\n"
"young age.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 2995..4165
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/2
msgid ""
"The futility of countrymen fighting each other, and\n"
"the tragedy...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 4291..5377
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/3
msgid ""
"Costa Rica learned the hard way. That is why it\n"
"abolished its army.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 5489..6394
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/4
msgid ""
"It decided to pour its efforts into education\n"
"instead.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 6548..7272
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/5
msgid ""
"\"More teachers than soldiers\" was the slogan.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 7314..8080
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/6
msgid ""
"Education is essential, no question.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 8247..9334
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/7
msgid ""
"Even Che used to teach reading and writing in\n"
"between guerrilla campaigns.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 9418..10644
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/8
msgid ""
"Costa Rica was poor at the time. We didn't have\n"
"many resources.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 10811..12246
#: codec/1/182/0xb62e0/9
msgid ""
"I suppose we had to pick one or the other - the\n"
"military or the schools.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/0
msgid ""
"Kaz was telling me Japan has a peace constitution,\n"
"too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/1
msgid ""
"That is right. Apparently when Costa Rica was\n"
"drafting its constitution,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/2
msgid ""
"they looked to the Japanese as a model.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/3
msgid ""
"Only Japan's constitution renounces war itself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/4
msgid ""
"Unlike Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/5
msgid ""
"But... Japan has a Self-Defense Force, right? That I\n"
"do not get.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/6
msgid ""
"I think I will ask Mr. Miller about it next time I see\n"
"him. He said he used to be in the JSDF.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb66e0/7
msgid ""
"You're a curious one, aren't you? Don't study too\n"
"hard.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/0
msgid ""
"What was that you were saying... \"peace is not the\n"
"natural state of men\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/1
msgid ""
"You said you learned it in school.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/2
msgid ""
"That's right. They're the words of the German\n"
"philosopher Immanuel Kant.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/3
msgid ""
"In 1795 he wrote a book titled \"Perpetual Peace.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/4
msgid ""
"Kant argued that it's precisely because peace is\n"
"unnatural\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/5
msgid ""
"that we have to make it ourselves.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/6
msgid ""
"How?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/7
msgid ""
"That's what his book is about. Is the concept\n"
"starting to sound interesting now?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/8
msgid ""
"Not really... I belong in a more natural world.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/9
msgid ""
"Is that so...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/10
msgid ""
"...My grandparents died in the civil war.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/11
msgid ""
"If only we'd been at peace, they wouldn't have lost\n"
"their lives.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/12
msgid ""
"You actually wish for war?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/13
msgid ""
"It's not like I want to hurt innocent civilians.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/14
msgid ""
"But if someone attacks you, what are you\n"
"supposed to do?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/15
msgid ""
"A country needs the strength to defend itself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/16
msgid ""
"Otherwise it faces invasion, oppression, political\n"
"subjugation.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/17
msgid ""
"If they'd simply stop using force to tangle with\n"
"each other,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/18
msgid ""
"countries wouldn't need force to defend themselves.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/19
msgid ""
"And how would you guarantee that?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/20
msgid ""
"I...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/21
msgid ""
"...Sorry. But you have to understand how the world\n"
"works\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/22
msgid ""
"in order to protect the ones you love.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/23
msgid ""
"That's not to say ideals aren't important, too. They\n"
"are.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/182/0xb6a00/24
msgid ""
"You are right, Snake... Thanks. Peace!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/0
msgid ""
"Costa Rica's forests are more diverse than you\n"
"might expect.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/1
msgid ""
"Not all of them are tropical rain forests.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/2
msgid ""
"Costa Rica is close to the Equator, it is true, but it\n"
"is also very mountainous.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/3
msgid ""
"I see what you mean.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/4
msgid ""
"Go up 4,000 feet in elevation and the temperature\n"
"drops more than seven degrees.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/5
msgid ""
"There are basically three types of forests.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/6
msgid ""
"The lowlands are covered in tropical rain forests,\n"
"the highlands by tropical cloud forests.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb71f0/7
msgid ""
"And areas where there is a dry season have\n"
"tropical dry forests.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 473..2034
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/0
msgid ""
"The lowlands along the Caribbean coast are mostly\n"
"covered by hot, humid tropical rain forests.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 2131..2897
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/1
msgid ""
"What most people envision when they think of\n"
"\"jungle.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 3009..4374
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/2
msgid ""
"The closely packed trees spread their branches\n"
"out at great heights to soak up the sun.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 4527..5530
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/3
msgid ""
"Their shade makes it dark near the ground, so be\n"
"careful.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 5600..6757
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/4
msgid ""
"Of course, with so little light few plants can grow\n"
"on the ground,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 6812..7439
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/5
msgid ""
"so it might actually be easier to walk.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 7481..8791
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/6
msgid ""
"So even if you could photosynthesize, it wouldn't\n"
"do you any good.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 8860..9738
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/7
msgid ""
"Photosynthesize? People cannot do that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0120_010_0
#. timeline 10128..10602
#: codec/1/183/0xb7530/8
msgid ""
"Most people, anyway.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/0
msgid ""
"Areas with a distinct dry season, like the Pacific\n"
"coast, have tropical dry forests.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/1
msgid ""
"During the dry season, the trees drop their leaves.\n"
"It gives you a clearer view,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/2
msgid ""
"but at the same time there are fewer places to\n"
"hide, so be careful.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/3
msgid ""
"Sounds dull.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/4
msgid ""
"It is not, really. A lot of trees flower during the dry\n"
"season.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/5
msgid ""
"Including my favorite, the tabebuia.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb78c0/6
msgid ""
"It has these amazingly vivid yellow flowers.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/0
msgid ""
"The cloud forests cover the central mountainous\n"
"region of the country.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/1
msgid ""
"They're perpetually shrouded in fog. You get wet\n"
"just standing there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/2
msgid ""
"It is as if the entire forest is inside a cloud.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/3
msgid ""
"Must make for poor visibility.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/4
msgid ""
"It does. But beauty, too. It is like being lost in some\n"
"mystical, green labyrinth.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/5
msgid ""
"...I'd rather not get lost if that's OK.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/6
msgid ""
"The forests are also home to lots of rare animals.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/183/0xb7b80/7
msgid ""
"Especially brightly colored frogs. They like the\n"
"humidity.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 473..1825
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/0
msgid ""
"Costa Rica is said to have about 87,000 species\n"
"of living things.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 1922..2925
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/1
#, c-format
msgid ""
"That's about 5% of all the known species in the\n"
"world.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 2967..4235
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/2
msgid ""
"A tiny place like this? I'll be damned.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 4263..5057
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/3
msgid ""
"I want to protect that biological diversity.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 5154..6102
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/4
msgid ""
"When diversity is lost, the environment weakens.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 6185..6729
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/5
msgid ""
"Just look at the plantations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 6784..8192
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/6
msgid ""
"I think I know what you mean. It's like trying to\n"
"assemble a unit from similar guys\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 8331..8958
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/7
msgid ""
"- it usually doesn't work out.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 8986..10017
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/8
msgid ""
"Throw a few square pegs in there and everything\n"
"falls into place.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 10058..11243
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/9
msgid ""
"There are so many species here that a lot of them\n"
"have not even been classified yet.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 11312..12678
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/10
msgid ""
"I'm hoping I can help do that someday. Kind of like\n"
"a parataxonomist.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 12692..13527
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/11
msgid ""
"Para... say that again?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 13555..14503
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/12
msgid ""
"Parataxonomist. Someone who helps a taxonomist.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 14517..16147
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/13
msgid ""
"Oh. Huh. I thought you were going to say it had\n"
"something to do with parachutes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 16551..16913
#: codec/1/184/0xb8540/14
msgid ""
"You're weird...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 473..2131
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/0
msgid ""
"The Development Corporation of Costa Rica, or\n"
"CODESA, was established two years ago.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 2215..3023
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/1
msgid ""
"Since President Oduber was elected this year,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 3092..3914
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/2
msgid ""
"the state has been putting a lot more effort into\n"
"development.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 4012..4736
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/3
msgid ""
"The corporate state, so to speak.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 4778..5767
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/4
msgid ""
"Growth is good and all, but there's one thing that\n"
"bugs me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 5767..5976
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/5
#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/37
msgid ""
"What's that?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 6004..7258
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/6
msgid ""
"I cannot help but wonder whether CODESA is not\n"
"just a front for la CIA.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 7286..7843
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/7
msgid ""
"You mean what the \"professor\" was saying\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 7843..8721
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/8
msgid ""
"about the CIA mercenaries posing as security\n"
"guards?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 8763..9404
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/9
msgid ""
"They were using CODESA as camouflage...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 9431..10295
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/10
msgid ""
"I'm worried that development is going to destroy\n"
"the forests...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 10435..11257
#: codec/1/184/0xb8a90/11
msgid ""
"but I do not suppose it has anything to do with this.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 473..975
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/0
msgid ""
"You like the peace sign, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 1003..2340
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/1
msgid ""
"Sí. As a gesture it connects every peace-loving\n"
"person.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 2452..3441
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/2
msgid ""
"Here, you try it, Snake. Peace!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 3496..4388
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/3
msgid ""
"...No thanks. It... doesn't suit me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 4444..4862
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/4
msgid ""
"Too bad for you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 4945..6032
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/5
msgid ""
"You know, the \"V\" in the peace sign comes from\n"
"the \"V\" in \"Victory.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 6199..6882
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/6
msgid ""
"When did it start standing for peace?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 6952..7648
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/7
msgid ""
"I am not completely sure... but\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 7774..8832
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/8
msgid ""
"I guess it came out of the protest movement\n"
"against the Vietnam War.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 8888..9724
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/9
msgid ""
"Oh, and don't turn your hand around when you do\n"
"it,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 9766..10699
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/10
msgid ""
"especially around British people. It is insulting.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 487..1072
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/0
msgid ""
"So you live alone now?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 1086..2605
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/1
msgid ""
"No, not alone. I've been living in school dormitories\n"
"since I started junior high.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 2688..4304
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/2
msgid ""
"After my mother died, my relatives took me in,\n"
"but... they were not my real family.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 4332..4709
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/3
msgid ""
"You didn't fit in there?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 4722..5544
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/4
msgid ""
"In a way... My aunts were kind to me and all...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 5698..7077
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/5
msgid ""
"But I know how difficult it must have been to\n"
"suddenly have a child thrust into their lives.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 7133..7927
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/6
msgid ""
"When you live with someone, there are no secrets.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 8108..8832
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/7
msgid ""
"I could tell my being there was a burden on them...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 9209..9724
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/8
msgid ""
"Sounds like a rough childhood.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 9766..10922
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/9
msgid ""
"I would not say that. I was lucky just to have\n"
"people to take me in.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 10964..12162
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/10
msgid ""
"There are huérfanos living out in the streets\n"
"because their mothers died.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 12246..13165
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/11
msgid ""
"It is even worse in countries with frequent civil\n"
"wars.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 13221..14113
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/12
msgid ""
"So who am I to complain about my childhood?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 14154..14628
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/13
msgid ""
"You're a pretty tough kid, you know?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 14656..15562
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/14
msgid ""
"...Not at all. I am not strong at all.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 473..1003
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/0
msgid ""
"I have a favor to ask you, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 1044..1226
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/1
msgid ""
"Name it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 1267..2215
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/2
msgid ""
"I want to you to give me a job here. I want to help\n"
"out.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 2243..3148
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/3
msgid ""
"You sure? You just went through a hell of a time.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 3287..3970
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/4
msgid ""
"You should probably take it easy until you're\n"
"settled.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 4012..4904
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/5
msgid ""
"Thank you. But there must be something I can do.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 4945..6116
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/6
msgid ""
"You would not want me near a gun, but I am a\n"
"decent cook.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 6171..6826
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/7
msgid ""
"Now there's a skill we can use.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 6854..7885
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/8
msgid ""
"Put me on the mess hall team - I think I can handle\n"
"it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 8010..9250
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/9
msgid ""
"Once I get used to it, I'll even add in some Costa\n"
"Rican recipes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 9292..9780
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/10
msgid ""
"Sounds like a plan.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/0
msgid ""
"Bosque del Alba means \"forest of dawn.\" Naturally,\n"
"it is situated on the east coast.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/1
msgid ""
"It is your standard tropical rainforest, everything\n"
"you'd imagine in a jungle.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/2
msgid ""
"No sign of morning sun here.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/3
msgid ""
"The foliage is too thick for direct sunlight to hit\n"
"the floor.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/4
msgid ""
"I do not know how easy it will be making your way\n"
"through here.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/5
msgid ""
"I'll be fine. This isn't my first trip to a jungle.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 473..1727
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/0
msgid ""
"The mercenaries' supply base is situated on\n"
"elevated ground by the coast.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 1825..2981
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/1
msgid ""
"I heard them call it \"Puerto del Alba\" - \"Port of\n"
"Dawn.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 3051..3845
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/2
msgid ""
"They have perfect visibility of the area from up\n"
"there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 3928..4709
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/3
msgid ""
"We did our best to sneak in undetected, but...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 4959..5544
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/4
msgid ""
"one of the guards spotted us, and we...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 5572..5823
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/5
msgid ""
"What is it?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 5837..6840
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/6
msgid ""
"...I'm sorry, you'll have to ask Professor Gálvez the\n"
"rest.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 6868..7718
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/7
msgid ""
"...It's OK. You've been through a lot.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 7732..8735
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/8
msgid ""
"I am sorry, I... I just cannot...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 8749..10031
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/9
msgid ""
"You did great, Paz. I won't let your efforts go\n"
"wasted.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/0
msgid ""
"This is a tropical rainforest, just like Bosque del\n"
"Alba.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/1
msgid ""
"The temperature and humidity can be brutal. El\n"
"Cenegal means \"Place of Mud.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/2
msgid ""
"Mud. Great. I'll watch my step.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/3
msgid ""
"This area often gets flooded by the river.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/4
msgid ""
"There are canals here and there carved out by the\n"
"water.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/5
msgid ""
"Good places to hide.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/6
msgid ""
"But they'll also make it harder for you to see. Be\n"
"careful, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 445..1212
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/0
msgid ""
"There should be a suspension bridge around there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 1239..1713
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/1
msgid ""
"In lowlands like this?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 1769..2633
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/2
msgid ""
"The ground nearby is harder and higher than usual.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 2716..3594
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/3
msgid ""
"The river cut through it, eventually creating a\n"
"valley.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 3636..4597
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/4
msgid ""
"There might be another way to get across the\n"
"river somewhere.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 4597..5349
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/5
msgid ""
"I wouldn't want to run into someone on the bridge.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 5391..6687
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/6
msgid ""
"The valley tends to be misty, so you might not be\n"
"able to see the water from up there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 6770..7314
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/7
msgid ""
"Fall and it'll leave more than a bump.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xbae80/0
msgid ""
"When a river floods an area, the banks can\n"
"collapse, creating a marsh.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xbae80/1
msgid ""
"You see a lot of them around here.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xbae80/2
msgid ""
"I'll need to watch the noise my feet make in el\n"
"cenegal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xbae80/3
msgid ""
"There's a marsh on the other side of the river, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/186/0xbae80/4
msgid ""
"The suspension bridge will take you there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 445..1630
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/0
msgid ""
"The river running through here is Río del Jade, or\n"
"\"the Jade River.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 1657..2438
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/1
msgid ""
"Jade? Are there minerals around here?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 2452..3287
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/2
msgid ""
"No, it refers to the color of the water.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 3357..4040
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/3
msgid ""
"You'll have to go to Guatemala for jade.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 4096..5475
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/4
msgid ""
"Hmm... Doesn't look all that pretty from where I'm\n"
"standing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 5517..6673
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/5
msgid ""
"We're still in the rainy season, so the river's a little\n"
"muddy.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 6715..7606
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/6
msgid ""
"It'll return to normal once the dry season starts.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 7648..8554
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/7
msgid ""
"Rivers are an important means of transport around\n"
"here.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 8609..9822
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/8
msgid ""
"They're relatively calm, and there are plenty of\n"
"canals along the coast, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 9863..10978
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/9
msgid ""
"A boat'd be more than enough to transport some\n"
"good-sized cargo.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 10978..11619
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/10
msgid ""
"Like... a nuclear weapon?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 11967..12887
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/11
msgid ""
"We don't know enough yet. I'll keep looking.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 12914..13221
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/12
#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/29
msgid ""
"Thank you, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 445..1727
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/0
msgid ""
"There's a lot of banana cultivation along Costa\n"
"Rica's Caribbean coast.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 1839..2702
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/1
msgid ""
"The area's dotted with banana plantations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 2772..3524
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/2
msgid ""
"Bananas have been Costa Rica's main crop\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 3538..4611
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/3
msgid ""
"since they were introduced from Panama in the\n"
"19th century.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 4695..5447
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/4
msgid ""
"They bring in a fair amount of foreign currency.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 5503..6227
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/5
msgid ""
"A real fruta de oro, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 6241..7453
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/6
msgid ""
"Si. But exporting all those bananas requires a ton\n"
"of land.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 7537..8219
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/7
msgid ""
"Hence all the plantations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 8261..9543
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/8
msgid ""
"Clearing all that forest just to grow bananas robs\n"
"animals of their habitats.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 9654..10546
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/9
msgid ""
"I do not know how good that is for Costa Rica in\n"
"the end.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 459..1267
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/0
msgid ""
"Panama disease was rampant here about 20 years\n"
"ago,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 1393..2284
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/1
msgid ""
"putting a lot of banana plantations out of business.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 2354..2716
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/2
msgid ""
"Panama disease?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 2786..3413
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/3
msgid ""
"It is caused by a type of fungus.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 3524..4695
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/4
msgid ""
"Apparently it killed off almost all the banana\n"
"species that used to grow here.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 4736..5154
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/5
msgid ""
"How could that happen?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 5224..5893
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/6
msgid ""
"Cultivated bananas do not produce seeds.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 5948..7481
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/7
msgid ""
"You have to remove and transplant part of the\n"
"stem yourself. You plant them in the fields.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 7523..8233
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/8
msgid ""
"So you've got acres of identical plants?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 8275..9487
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/9
msgid ""
"Si. When one plant is infected, the disease spreads\n"
"quickly.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 9599..10407
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/10
msgid ""
"Species lacking genetic diversity become weak.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 10504..11075
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/11
msgid ""
"They grow different bananas today,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 11103..11981
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/12
msgid ""
"ones said to be resistant to Panama disease.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/0
msgid ""
"Costa Rica has several active volcanoes, Irazú\n"
"being one of them.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/1
msgid ""
"That's where \"Camino de Lava\" comes from, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/2
msgid ""
"The tropical dry forests around here are quite\n"
"different from our rainforests.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/3
msgid ""
"They lose their leaves in the dry season.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/4
msgid ""
"Tropical forests are not all thick jungles. A few of\n"
"them even have cacti.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/5
msgid ""
"Some of Costa Rica's greatest assets are its\n"
"diverse forests and natural landscapes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 445..1588
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/0
msgid ""
"Aldea de los Despiertos means \"Village of the\n"
"Awake.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 1936..2229
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/1
msgid ""
"Weird name.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 2270..3510
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/2
msgid ""
"The area's littered with coffee fields and there's a\n"
"factory nearby.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 3608..4569
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/3
msgid ""
"The villagers are fans of coffee, so...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 4806..6185
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/4
msgid ""
"They don't get much sleep, huh? They've got a\n"
"sense of humor all right.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 6283..7397
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/5
msgid ""
"I cannot believe they would take over a place like\n"
"this and use it as a prison.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 7481..8763
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/6
msgid ""
"It is unforgiveable. For both la CIA and the thugs\n"
"they employ.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 8832..9557
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/7
msgid ""
"All the villagers wanted was to live in peace.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 9654..10490
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/8
msgid ""
"What gives la CIA the right to crush them like\n"
"that?!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 10560..11438
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/9
msgid ""
"They don't care about anyone's rights but their\n"
"own.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 11674..12204
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/10
msgid ""
"It's just the way some people are.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 12260..12705
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/11
msgid ""
"You really think so?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 12747..14015
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/12
msgid ""
"Don't worry. It just gives me the right to teach\n"
"them a lesson.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 445..2159
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/0
msgid ""
"La CIA has taken control of this coffee factory,\n"
"too. All to produce its drugs...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 2215..3204
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/1
msgid ""
"It was famous once, for its fine beans.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 3482..4722
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/2
msgid ""
"Cafetal Aroma Encantado... \"Enchanting Aroma,\"\n"
"huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 4764..5823
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/3
msgid ""
"Si. Once we've thrown the mercenaries out of\n"
"Costa Rica,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 5935..6701
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/4
msgid ""
"I know it will make wonderful coffee again.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 6743..7370
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/5
msgid ""
"And then you must come and try some, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 7370..9306
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/6
msgid ""
"Sounds great. I wouldn't mind a cuppa joe after all\n"
"this is over. Oh, wait...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 9334..9557
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/7
msgid ""
"What is wrong?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 9599..11215
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/8
msgid ""
"No, I... just remembered this guy I knew who wasn't\n"
"big on coffee. English.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 11354..12552
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/9
msgid ""
"\"Get rid of that muddy water and get a cup of\n"
"black tea down your gob,\" he'd say.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 12552..13918
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/10
msgid ""
"Ha! That's too bad for him - it is delicious.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 445..1727
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/0
msgid ""
"As I said before, building railroads in Costa Rica\n"
"was a dangerous job.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 1839..2883
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/1
msgid ""
"A lot of men died, and sometimes they stopped\n"
"work altogether.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 2967..4193
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/2
msgid ""
"This is one of those places. They had to cut\n"
"through steep terrain,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 4207..5405
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/3
msgid ""
"so when they finally made it through they just built\n"
"the rail terminal right there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 5447..5921
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/4
msgid ""
"And that's why they named it...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 46138..64136
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/5
msgid ""
"El Cadalso... the Gallows. Charming.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/6
msgid ""
"I'm surprised the construction money didn't dry up\n"
"the way things were going.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/7
msgid ""
"Actually, it did. But the bananas helped complete it,\n"
"so they say.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/8
msgid ""
"You mean... the energy the workers got from\n"
"eating bananas?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/9
msgid ""
"I suppose they do have plenty of vitamins and...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/10
msgid ""
"No, no, no, I meant the money they got to finish it\n"
"came from exporting bananas.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/11
#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/5
msgid ""
"Oh...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/12
msgid ""
"But one thing is for certain!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/13
msgid ""
"The owners of the railroads expanded into the\n"
"banana trade\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/14
msgid ""
"after construction was completed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/15
msgid ""
"That was the start of banana cultivation in Costa\n"
"Rica.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 459..1741
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/0
msgid ""
"Snake, to the north of the village is a bridge that\n"
"crosses a hydraulic pipe,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 1783..2549
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/1
msgid ""
"though normally the bridge is not used by people.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 2577..3942
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/2
msgid ""
"If you slip you'll fall straight to the bottom of the\n"
"valley. Be careful.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 4012..4500
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/3
msgid ""
"What's a channel doing here?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 4527..5642
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/4
msgid ""
"It is not for irrigation - they're hydroelectric pipes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 5767..6534
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/5
msgid ""
"I wonder if they run into Irazú's crater lake.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 6617..7509
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/6
msgid ""
"Normally they would build a reservoir at the\n"
"bottom of the valley,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 7551..8247
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/7
msgid ""
"but it was probably too dangerous.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 8373..9292
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/8
msgid ""
"Los Cantos means \"Sword Peak.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 445..1476
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/0
msgid ""
"You should be able to see across the Irazú\n"
"mountain range from there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 1532..3078
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/1
msgid ""
"There are not as many big trees at that elevation,\n"
"and you'll probably be well above the mist.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 3622..4193
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/2
msgid ""
"It'll be tough to hide up there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 4221..5099
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/3
msgid ""
"You're not thinking about the scenery right now,\n"
"are you?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 5154..5893
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/4
msgid ""
"Not while I'm surrounded by bad guys.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 5907..6617
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/5
msgid ""
"You should have seen it when the country was at\n"
"peace.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 6729..7258
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/6
msgid ""
"I know you'd have been impressed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 7314..8874
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/7
msgid ""
"Well, that'll be our reward for a successful mission.\n"
"Sound good?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 8902..9668
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/8
msgid ""
"Wonderful. Thank you, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 445..1309
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/0
msgid ""
"...There is... an old fort around there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 1309..2201
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/1
msgid ""
"What is it, Paz? You sound... upset.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 2201..3705
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/2
msgid ""
"Well... You see, it was built during the civil war.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 3733..5015
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/3
msgid ""
"Let me guess: disputes between Costa Rica's\n"
"political parties\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 5015..5656
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/4
msgid ""
"escalated into all-out conflict.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 5656..6812
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/5
msgid ""
"Sí. Conflict that cost my grandparents their lives.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 6924..8303
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/6
msgid ""
"The most senseless sort of war - countrymen\n"
"mindlessly slaughtering their own.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 8345..9181
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/7
msgid ""
"That fort is a reminder of that senselessness.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 9445..10518
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/8
msgid ""
"Sadly ironic, given who's occupying it now.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 10560..11479
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/9
msgid ""
"That war was the reason Costa Rica abolished the\n"
"army.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 11549..12371
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/10
msgid ""
"Please, Snake! Get them out of our country!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 12385..12928
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/11
msgid ""
"I intend to.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 445..2410
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/0
msgid ""
"This area is a tropical cloud forest, continually\n"
"covered in a thick mist.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 2465..3162
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/1
msgid ""
"It is quite a mystical place.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 3204..4987
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/2
msgid ""
"Selba de la Leche... \"Forest of Milk.\" I can barely\n"
"see in front of me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 5015..6269
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/3
msgid ""
"There you go again. The forest is basically sitting\n"
"in a cloud,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 6283..7021
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/4
msgid ""
"so of course it's going to be hard to see.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 7049..8623
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/5
msgid ""
"But you know, the cloud forest is the only place\n"
"many exotic creatures can live.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 8637..9849
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/6
msgid ""
"Well, if they're not edible, I'm not interested.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 9905..10964
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/7
msgid ""
"Snake! I'll have you know people travel from all\n"
"around the world\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 10964..11772
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/8
msgid ""
"to witness Costa Rica's unique fauna!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 445..1170
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/0
msgid ""
"Snake, watch out for the frogs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 1239..2883
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/1
msgid ""
"Why, they bite? Relax, no frog's ever eaten a snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 3009..4179
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/2
msgid ""
"Although I've feasted on a few frogs' legs myself...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 4193..5029
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/3
msgid ""
"But, they're dangerous! They're poisonous!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 5071..5335
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/4
msgid ""
"Poisonous?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 5335..6311
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/5
msgid ""
"Poison dart frogs live up to their name, I assure\n"
"you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 6380..7829
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/6
msgid ""
"Their poison is so strong the indígena use them to\n"
"make poison-tipped arrows.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 7857..9292
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/7
msgid ""
"Some secrete poison through their skin - even\n"
"touching them can be dangerous.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 9292..9961
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/8
msgid ""
"So don't go petting them or anything.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 10212..10978
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/9
msgid ""
"So... I can't eat one?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 10978..11424
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/10
msgid ""
"I'm warning you!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/0
msgid ""
"Catarata de la Muerte means \"Waterfall of Death.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/1
msgid ""
"How cheerful.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/2
msgid ""
"I am sure it will be no problem for you, Snake,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/3
msgid ""
"especially compared to all the dire situations\n"
"you've faced in the past.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/4
msgid ""
"Easy to say now. We'll see what really happens.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/5
msgid ""
"Sorry. Still, you have surprised me. Everything they\n"
"say about the legend is true.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/6
msgid ""
"I'm neither hero nor legend. But for some reason, I\n"
"don't mind you calling me that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/7
msgid ""
"Thanks. Be careful, Snake. Peace!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 445..1309
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/0
msgid ""
"La Ruinas de Xochiquetzal will be around there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 1337..2619
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/1
msgid ""
"They have not been restored at all, so they may\n"
"well be covered in plants.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 2702..3106
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/2
msgid ""
"Xochiquetzal?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 3134..3970
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/3
msgid ""
"An Aztec goddess of fertility and beauty.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 4068..5154
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/4
msgid ""
"They say she was always accompanied by birds\n"
"and butterflies.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 5210..6506
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/5
msgid ""
"One theory states she was the mother of the god\n"
"known as Quetzalcoatl.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 6575..6993
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/6
msgid ""
"Quetzalcoatl...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 7035..8400
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/7
msgid ""
"The quetzal is said to be an incarnation of\n"
"Quetzalcoatl, hence its name.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 8442..10309
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/8
msgid ""
"I get it. Well, this place definitely matches the\n"
"atmosphere of a cloud forest.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 10323..11535
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/9
msgid ""
"Now, it may have seen better days, but that is still\n"
"a temple.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 11591..12399
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/10
msgid ""
"So, be sure to show respect when you're inside.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 12427..12901
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/11
msgid ""
"If the mood strikes me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 12956..14001
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/12
msgid ""
"Hmph! Well, you've got no one to blame but yourself\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 14043..14698
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/13
msgid ""
"if Xochiquetzal strikes you down.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 445..1434
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/0
msgid ""
"I do not know if I recall such large ruins being\n"
"there...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 1630..2897
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/1
msgid ""
"Well, didn't you say there's a lot we don't know\n"
"about Costa Rica's ancient civilizations?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 2925..4193
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/2
msgid ""
"You talked about some giant stone balls, too. What\n"
"are those?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 4235..5154
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/3
msgid ""
"Oh, the Stone Spheres of Costa Rica?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 5266..6074
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/4
msgid ""
"They're an assortment of giant spheres carved\n"
"from stone\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 6074..7383
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/5
msgid ""
"that were discovered in the jungles of Costa Rica\n"
"about 50 years ago.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 7411..7941
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/6
msgid ""
"What's so special about that?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 7983..9041
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/7
msgid ""
"What if I told you some of them are nearly perfect\n"
"spheres?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 9167..10407
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/8
msgid ""
"And that they were carved out of granite, which is\n"
"quite a hard substance.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 10448..11493
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/9
msgid ""
"Hmm, could be good for laying a trap.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 11605..12483
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/10
msgid ""
"And if they're spherical, they'd roll easily, too...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 12496..12845
#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice 
#. timeline 1017..1281
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/11
#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/8
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/1
#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/0
#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/0
#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/0
#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/14
msgid ""
"Snake...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0250_000_0
#. timeline 445..1365
#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/0
msgid ""
"So tell me, what do they mine around here?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0250_000_0
#. timeline 1393..1936
#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/1
msgid ""
"Gold, if I am not mistaken.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0250_000_0
#. timeline 1978..3733
#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/2
msgid ""
"Gold?! No kidding. I wonder what'd be the fastest\n"
"way to...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/3
msgid ""
"I do not know how much success they've had.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/4
msgid ""
"You do not hear of anyone still operating mines\n"
"around here.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/6
msgid ""
"Generally speaking, people here are not too thrilled\n"
"with outside capital\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/7
msgid ""
"coming in and taking away the country's natural\n"
"resources.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/8
msgid ""
"Four years ago, a group of protestors hurled\n"
"stones at the parliament building\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/9
msgid ""
"when people found out the country had been\n"
"bestowing mining rights to foreign companies.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 445..1783
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/0
msgid ""
"They must have had to clear a considerable\n"
"amount of forest to open up that mine.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 2020..3092
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/1
msgid ""
"No doubt. So much for any hiding places, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 3120..4207
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/2
msgid ""
"And it is not just the forest. Without the proper\n"
"precautions,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 4277..5113
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/3
msgid ""
"the mine's waste water could pollute the\n"
"groundwater.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 5182..6339
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/4
msgid ""
"And to top it all off, they're developing nuclear\n"
"weapons there, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 6450..7328
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/5
msgid ""
"How can people care so little about their own\n"
"country?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 7370..8038
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/6
msgid ""
"...I'm not the one to ask about that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 8038..8930
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/7
msgid ""
"Well, you may have abandoned your country,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 9055..9752
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/8
msgid ""
"but you still treasure where you came from.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 10198..10504
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/9
#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/10
#: codec/2/914/0x392460/23
msgid ""
"You think so?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 10518..11312
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/10
msgid ""
"Sure. I know you do.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 11424..13931
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/11
msgid ""
"Paz, you... I... Whatever you do, never stop loving\n"
"your country.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/0
msgid ""
"Since it was founded, my country has not once\n"
"been able to choose its own path.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/1
msgid ""
"First Spain, then America. Over one hundred years\n"
"of this...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/2
#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/11
msgid ""
"I know.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/3
msgid ""
"In the 19th century,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/4
msgid ""
"an American mercenary named William Walker\n"
"seized power in Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/5
msgid ""
"I'd heard he exploited rivalries between the political\n"
"parties.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/6
msgid ""
"Even after we expelled him,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/7
msgid ""
"the Americans sent in their Marines under the\n"
"pretext of quelling political unrest.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/8
msgid ""
"And the real reason?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/9
msgid ""
"To intimidate the government and thwart the\n"
"construction of the Nicaragua Canal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/0
msgid ""
"I thought the U.S. already has the rights to build a\n"
"canal in Nicaragua...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/1
msgid ""
"They never intended to build a canal there. They\n"
"had already started digging in Panama.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/2
msgid ""
"A canal in Nicaragua would break up the Panama\n"
"Canal's monopoly,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/3
msgid ""
"reason enough for America to stick its nose into\n"
"our affairs.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/4
msgid ""
"They snagged the rights so nobody else could\n"
"build there...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/5
msgid ""
"It was General Sandino who finally stood up to los\n"
"yanquis.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/0
msgid ""
"General Sandino waged a guerrilla war against the\n"
"Marines,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/1
msgid ""
"at last driving them out. He was a true hero, and -\n"
"to us Sandinistas - like a father.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/2
msgid ""
"But when they pulled out, the Americans left us\n"
"something to remember them by.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/3
msgid ""
"The National Guard.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/4
msgid ""
"Yes, la Guardia. In name, a peacekeeping force.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/5
msgid ""
"But in reality, Commander Somoza's personal army,\n"
"answering to no one else.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/6
msgid ""
"Unable to stay silent, General Sandino went to\n"
"protest...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/7
msgid ""
"and was assassinated by Somoza as he made his\n"
"way home.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/8
msgid ""
"It was then that Somoza and los sapos\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/9
msgid ""
"began to eat our country alive, from the inside.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/0
msgid ""
"The first Somoza was originally no more than the\n"
"commander of la Guardia.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/1
msgid ""
"Ordinarily, a man of his station could never hope to\n"
"become president.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/2
msgid ""
"But the president at the time had no power to\n"
"back him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/3
msgid ""
"The only one with the strength to oppose him was\n"
"General Sandino.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/4
msgid ""
"....No. Better to say the General was the only one\n"
"who dared oppose him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/5
msgid ""
"There was nothing special about him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/6
msgid ""
"Above all, it takes a strong will to see justice done.\n"
"That is what he taught us.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/7
msgid ""
"It's also what motivated Somoza to have him killed...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/8
msgid ""
"Yes. The rest was easy. He got rid of the\n"
"president, taking office in a sham election.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/9
msgid ""
"And once he had power, he never gave it up.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/10
msgid ""
"Talk about heavy-handed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/11
msgid ""
"He had the Americans backing him, that's why.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/12
msgid ""
"They didn't want to hand over power to a\n"
"rebellious general.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/13
msgid ""
"Even so, it's hard to believe Washington would give\n"
"its blessing to a guy like that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/14
msgid ""
"The American President at the time put it this way:\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/15
msgid ""
"\"Somoza may be a son of a bitch, but he's our son\n"
"of a bitch.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/16
msgid ""
"In other words, better a dog or los sapos (Somoza\n"
"and counter-revolutionaries)\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/17
msgid ""
"than an anti-US regime.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/0
msgid ""
"The river that flows between Nicaragua and Costa\n"
"Rica is el Río San Juan.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/1
msgid ""
"It connects Lago Cocibolca to el Mar Caribe.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/2
msgid ""
"It is a gentle river, safe even for small boats. You\n"
"have to watch out for the sharks, though.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/3
msgid ""
"Sharks? In a river?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/4
msgid ""
"El tiburón toro live in the river. But there's nothing\n"
"to fear. San Juan will protect you always.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/5
msgid ""
"Juan?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/6
msgid ""
"The Rio San Juan takes its name from San Juan,\n"
"the man who baptized Jesús.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/7
msgid ""
"The man you call John the Baptist in your country.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/8
msgid ""
"John, huh... I'll be careful anyway. I'd hate to drown\n"
"- end up a John Doe.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/0
msgid ""
"There is a volcanic island in Lago Cocibolca called\n"
"Ometepe.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/1
msgid ""
"It's formed from two connected volcanoes, shaped\n"
"like a porongo (gourd).\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/2
msgid ""
"The one with smoke coming out of it?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/3
msgid ""
"That's the one. The smoking volcano is\n"
"Concepción. It erupts once in a while.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/4
msgid ""
"The other one is Maderas.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/5
msgid ""
"It's never erupted in recorded history. There's a\n"
"lake in the caldera at the top.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/6
msgid ""
"A crater lake... Let's hope there's not another\n"
"underground factory inside...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/7
msgid ""
"Don't say that!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/8
msgid ""
"If Peace Walker's nukes detonated there, it would\n"
"destabilize the magma underneath.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/9
msgid ""
"It could cause the volcano to erupt again.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/10
msgid ""
"If that happens, my country is doomed. Snake, you\n"
"must stop Peace Walker!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/0
msgid ""
"We are Sandinistas, the heirs of General Sandino's\n"
"will.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/1
msgid ""
"Sandino... the father of modern guerrilla warfare.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/2
msgid ""
"To you, maybe. To us, he's more like a real father.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/3
msgid ""
"That why you named yourselves after him?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/4
msgid ""
"Of course. La Frente Sandinista de Liberación\n"
"Nacional...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/5
msgid ""
"the Sandinista National Liberation Front is named\n"
"in his honor.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/6
msgid ""
"We share the General's goal - to take back our\n"
"country's freedom.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/7
msgid ""
"In his day, from America. In ours, from the despot\n"
"Somoza.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/8
msgid ""
"Times have changed, but the song remains the\n"
"same.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/9
msgid ""
"\"Patria Libre o Morir\"... That is our slogan.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/10
msgid ""
"El Che used to say the same thing, you know?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/11
msgid ""
"\"Patria o Muerte\"... the slogan of the Cuban\n"
"Revolution.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/12
msgid ""
"So you're fighting for a socialist revolution, too,\n"
"then?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/13
msgid ""
"No. It's not about ideology. We only want to live\n"
"normal lives.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/14
msgid ""
"We are sick of living in a country where you can\n"
"be beaten for walking down the street.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/15
msgid ""
"Where you never know if your neighbor is snitching\n"
"on you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/16
msgid ""
"Our goal is to give back the country to its people.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/17
msgid ""
"Yeah. The Cuban Revolution started out like that,\n"
"too...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/18
msgid ""
"We are few in number, but we will win.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/19
msgid ""
"Victoria o muerte. For a revolutionary, there is no\n"
"other fate.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/0
msgid ""
"Augusto César Sandino... general and hero of\n"
"Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/1
msgid ""
"Fifty years ago, conflict broke out between the\n"
"political parties of Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/2
msgid ""
"The U.S. Marines intervened in the name of\n"
"restoring order.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/3
msgid ""
"The only one who refused to listen to their call for\n"
"reconciliation was General Sandino.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/4
msgid ""
"One man against the Marines... That takes guts.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/5
msgid ""
"The General wasn't a professional soldier. Neither\n"
"were his compadres.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/6
msgid ""
"And they certainly could not match the Marines'\n"
"equipment.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/7
msgid ""
"But he used the land to his advantage, lurking in\n"
"the fields and hills of Nicaragua,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/8
msgid ""
"and using surprise attacks to harass the Marines.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/9
msgid ""
"I know. I've read plenty of textbooks on guerrilla\n"
"warfare.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/10
msgid ""
"In the end, he drove them out. He was truly a role\n"
"model for us.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/11
msgid ""
"Yeah, but that was the '30s - didn't the Depression\n"
"have something to do with it?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/12
msgid ""
"It takes cash to wage war.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/13
msgid ""
"Perhaps. But there is no denying what the General\n"
"accomplished.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/14
msgid ""
"The people hailed him as the \"General de Hombres\n"
"Libres\" - the general of free men.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/15
msgid ""
"They loved him. And then...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/16
msgid ""
"He was assassinated - by Anastasio Somoza\n"
"Garcia, commander of la Guardia.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/17
msgid ""
"The father of the current Somoza.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/18
msgid ""
"Somoza had the Americans' backing. That is the\n"
"way things were.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/19
msgid ""
"The General may be dead, and the times may have\n"
"changed,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/20
msgid ""
"but his will lives on inside each of us.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/21
msgid ""
"We are the sons and daughters of General Sandino.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/0
msgid ""
"Hey. How's the watermelon business these days?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/1
msgid ""
"Not bad. I hear the compas back home are hanging\n"
"in there, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/2
msgid ""
"Good to hear.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/3
msgid ""
"...You know our nickname. I'm impressed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/4
msgid ""
"No wonder they call you Boss.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/5
msgid ""
"You used to hide your weapons in hollowed-out\n"
"watermelons,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/6
msgid ""
"smuggle 'em right past the National Guard.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/7
msgid ""
"You even transported pineapple grenades that\n"
"way.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/8
msgid ""
"The name caught on among sympathizers in the\n"
"region and...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/9
#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/39
#: codec/2/914/0x392460/18
msgid ""
"What are you talking about?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/11
msgid ""
"They call us watermelon sellers because the\n"
"General's name\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/12
msgid ""
"sounds like the word for watermelon, sandía.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/13
#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/9
msgid ""
"...Really?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/14
msgid ""
"Si.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/15
msgid ""
"Dammit, Kaz...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/0
msgid ""
"I noticed you call Che Guevara \"El Che.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/1
msgid ""
"Not just us. Everyone in these parts does.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/2
msgid ""
"\"Che\" was always his nickname. It does not feel\n"
"right to call him by his last name.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/3
msgid ""
"...I was shocked the first time I saw you. You look\n"
"so much like him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/4
msgid ""
"I look like \"El Che\", huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/5
msgid ""
"Sort of. Not in the face. It's more... the way you\n"
"carry yourself...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 7397..8136
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/6
msgid ""
"I guess Che's a hero to the Sandinistas, too?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 8164..10156
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/7
msgid ""
"Of course. The FSLN was formed in the spirit of\n"
"the ideologies championed by El Che and Fidel.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 10421..12775
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/8
msgid ""
"Fidel... Fidel Castro. So you're trying to bring the\n"
"Cuban Revolution to Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 12845..14642
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/9
msgid ""
"Well, we were. But Cuba isn't what it once was...\n"
"Not since El Che left.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 14740..16314
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/10
msgid ""
"El Che was a true revolutionary. He fought - and\n"
"died - for the people.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 16370..17387
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/11
msgid ""
"He worked harder than anybody, and he was a\n"
"righteous man.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 17442..19045
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/12
msgid ""
"Even as a minister of Cuba, he gave up his\n"
"weekends to work on the farms and public works.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 19100..19560
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/13
msgid ""
"As a volunteer, no less.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 19644..20271
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/14
msgid ""
"Yeah, I've heard the stories.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 20326..21441
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/15
msgid ""
"But when you think about it, wasn't it that\n"
"obsession that did him in?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 21483..21831
#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 2048..2326
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/16
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/1
msgid ""
"How do you mean?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 21887..23517
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/17
msgid ""
"We can't all be supermen. He thought the ideals he\n"
"applied in Cuba would work in Bolivia.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 23558..25077
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/18
msgid ""
"But, he failed to win converts and the support of\n"
"the peasants, and it cost him his life.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 25175..25927
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/19
msgid ""
"Maybe... maybe you're right.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 26010..27278
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/20
msgid ""
"But at least he did not steal from those peasants,\n"
"no matter how hard things got.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 27320..27473
#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 1309..1476
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/21
#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/14
#: codec/1/206/0xce040/7
#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/2
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/1
#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/12
#: codec/2/913/0x391bb0/1
msgid ""
"Yeah.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 27515..28017
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/22
msgid ""
"I can sympathize with that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 28100..29312
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/23
msgid ""
"There's plenty of guerrillas out there who'd rob\n"
"their own people to feed their revolutions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 29354..31249
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/24
msgid ""
"If we had a comandante like him, the Sandinistas\n"
"would find the will to fight.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 501..1407
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/0
msgid ""
"You called that giant chopper an \"hombre nuevo\"...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 1407..2201
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/1
msgid ""
"Si. It means \"new man.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 2229..2563
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/2
msgid ""
"\"New man\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 2605..3789
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/3
msgid ""
"There was nobody piloting that thing. It must be\n"
"controlled by machine.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 3817..5391
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/4
msgid ""
"Yeah, it seems that way. No human being could pull\n"
"off those crazy maneuvers.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 5433..6561
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/5
msgid ""
"But it's not crazy - it's smart. It sings, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 6603..8038
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/6
msgid ""
"When we first saw it, one of my men said, \"Pilot\n"
"must be an hombre nuevo.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 8080..8721
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/7
msgid ""
"Me, I do not like the name.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 8735..8986
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/8
#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/2
msgid ""
"Why?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 9000..10017
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/9
msgid ""
"\"Hombre nuevo\" was what El Che was striving to\n"
"become.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0110_000_1
#. timeline 10058..57662
#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/10
msgid ""
"What all of us who joined the Sandinistas strive to\n"
"become. That's why!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/11
msgid ""
"An hombre nuevo is one who finds joy in virtue\n"
"and voluntary labor...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/12
msgid ""
"It makes me furious to see the name given to such\n"
"a monster.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/196/0xc4bb0/13
msgid ""
"I'll bet.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 459..1198
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/0
msgid ""
"Chico called that helicopter el colibri...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 1253..2229
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/1
msgid ""
"Our name for the hummingbird. You saw how that\n"
"chopper moved...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 2270..2856
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/2
msgid ""
"how it hovered in midair like a hummingbird.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 2911..3650
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/3
msgid ""
"Hell've a lot bigger than a bird, though.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 3691..4500
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/4
msgid ""
"True. But better than hombre nuevo, don't you\n"
"think?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 4555..5419
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/5
msgid ""
"When you get kidnapped by el colibri, it's all over.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 5503..6673
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/6
msgid ""
"They take you to a prison camp, and torture you\n"
"until you snitch on your compas.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 6715..7202
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/7
msgid ""
"That's what took Chico...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 7244..8484
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/8
msgid ""
"They have no mercy. Once you've talked, they toss\n"
"you out like trash...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 8582..9459
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/9
msgid ""
"I knew this, and still I could not save Chico.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 9613..10616
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/10
msgid ""
"If he cannot be saved, I'll do what must be done...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 10671..11187
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/11
msgid ""
"Don't write him off like that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 11270..12538
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/12
msgid ""
"Sometimes you have to survive, even if it means\n"
"sacrificing your honor.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0120_000_1
#. timeline 12594..13486
#: codec/1/197/0xc5060/13
msgid ""
"I'll get him back. I promise.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/0
msgid ""
"Snake, I need your opinion. How strong are the\n"
"enemy's mercenaries?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/1
msgid ""
"They're well trained. They've got more than enough\n"
"men...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/2
msgid ""
"Seasoned, too - a lot of them probably saw action\n"
"in Vietnam. They're a tough bunch.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/3
msgid ""
"And armed to the teeth.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/4
msgid ""
"I don't think I've ever seen a mercenary force field\n"
"that many tanks and attack choppers.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/5
msgid ""
"It shows how much cash they have to throw\n"
"around.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/6
msgid ""
"And connections - how did they get access to\n"
"such weapons?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/7
msgid ""
"How do you think? They're backed by the one and\n"
"only CIA.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/8
msgid ""
"And here we are, half of us farmers and the other\n"
"half students. Children, even!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/9
msgid ""
"And weapons... We're so short on guns we have to\n"
"steal them from the enemy.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/10
msgid ""
"As much as I hate to say it, we're always going to\n"
"be on the defensive.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/12
msgid ""
"And mi viejo... Without him, we...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice 
#. timeline 16258..16690
#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/13
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/15
msgid ""
"Yeah, I know.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/14
msgid ""
"...I don't know if we can win.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/15
msgid ""
"Can we, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/16
msgid ""
"Stop feeling sorry for yourself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/17
#: codec/2/905/0x389770/4
#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/48
msgid ""
"But...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/18
msgid ""
"Amanda!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 4959..5099
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 3761..3914
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_myo_rad_0190_000_0
#. timeline 417..557
#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/19
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/3
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/3
#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/17
#: codec/1/255/0xff000/8
#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/21
#: codec/2/904/0x388570/13
#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/46
#: codec/2/914/0x392460/12
#: codec/2/919/0x3971e0/1
msgid ""
"What?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/20
msgid ""
"Listen to me. Don't ever let your men hear you talk\n"
"like that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/21
msgid ""
"...I...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/22
msgid ""
"You're their leader, and a leader has to stand tall.\n"
"Even when times get tough.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/23
msgid ""
"When it feels like the fear and uncertainty could\n"
"crush you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/24
msgid ""
"You're the one your comrades look to for\n"
"reassurance. That's what a leader is. Don't forget it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/25
msgid ""
"...Snake...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/26
msgid ""
"If you're looking for comfort, go find a church.\n"
"That's all I've got to say.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/27
msgid ""
"You are right. I am sorry. I need to pull myself\n"
"together.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/28
msgid ""
"You'll be fine. I know you have it in you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/0
msgid ""
"The land in our country belongs to us, and yet it\n"
"doesn't belong to us.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/2
msgid ""
"Along the coast, it is all banana groves. And in the\n"
"mountains, it is coffee.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/3
msgid ""
"I guess in that way it's not so different from here.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/4
msgid ""
"Plantations...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/5
msgid ""
"Almost all the bananas and coffee are sold as\n"
"exports.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/6
msgid ""
"The landlords keep the money for themselves,\n"
"leaving precious little to the farmers.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/7
msgid ""
"Worse, the biggest landowners in the country are\n"
"Somoza and his family.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/8
msgid ""
"But it does bring in foreign currency...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/9
msgid ""
"I doubt even that, at least for bananas. The\n"
"plantations are owned by American corporations.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/10
msgid ""
"The bananas are processed in factories on the\n"
"plantations and exported to America from private\n"
"ports...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/11
msgid ""
"It's like having little American enclaves along the\n"
"coast of Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/12
msgid ""
"But the farmers have no choice but to go work\n"
"there...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/13
msgid ""
"Es ridículo! The people have to take their land\n"
"back.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/14
msgid ""
"It is one of the things we're fighting for.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/0
msgid ""
"Tell me... when exactly did you realize your dad\n"
"was working with the KGB?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/1
msgid ""
"About six months ago. Up until then, we only had\n"
"beans to eat.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/2
msgid ""
"And then suddenly we started to get eggs and\n"
"flour. Our bullet shortage simply disappeared.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/3
msgid ""
"How'd he get the cocaine?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/4
msgid ""
"Ask the KGB. All we did here was process it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/5
msgid ""
"Coca plants grow here, too,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/6
msgid ""
"but to my knowledge almost all of the stuff we\n"
"used came from Colombia and Bolivia.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/7
msgid ""
"It's processed in a factory and then shipped to\n"
"ports on the Caribbean Sea.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/8
msgid ""
"Where does it go after that?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/9
msgid ""
"I never thought about it.... I mean, I did not want to\n"
"think about it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/10
msgid ""
"The biggest cocaine consumer in the world is the\n"
"United States.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/11
msgid ""
"I'm guessing they smuggle it in on vessels\n"
"disguised as fishing boats.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/12
msgid ""
"Wait. La CIA uses that route, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/13
msgid ""
"Are you telling me they're selling cocaine to their\n"
"own country?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/14
msgid ""
"Looks that way.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/15
msgid ""
"Those bastards are turning their own children into\n"
"junkies? Are they insane?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/198/0xc6890/16
msgid ""
"No, just afraid. Afraid of a communist Central\n"
"America.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/0
msgid ""
"Amanda! When did you join up with the Sandinistas?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/1
msgid ""
"About a year ago, when I went into the mountains\n"
"with mi viejo and his group.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/2
msgid ""
"I thought your dad was with the FSLN from the\n"
"start.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 3719..5419
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/3
msgid ""
"No. He fought alongside General Sandino, but after\n"
"that he retired for a while.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 5489..6617
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/4
msgid ""
"He found a job, got a wife and a house, and raised\n"
"us kids.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 6715..7453
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/5
msgid ""
"Then one day some Sandinista students came by...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 7481..8345
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/6
msgid ""
"And he felt the old fire in his belly?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 8373..9654
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/7
msgid ""
"Something like that. All he did was help them\n"
"escape from la Guardia, though.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 9710..10295
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/8
msgid ""
"But then la Guardia showed up.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 10407..11549
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/9
msgid ""
"They broke into our house and began pushing him\n"
"around, shouting questions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 11591..12301
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/10
msgid ""
"I'm guessing he kept his mouth shut.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 12343..13681
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/11
msgid ""
"No matter how hard they hit him. Our house was\n"
"trashed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 13778..14935
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/12
msgid ""
"After that, he was on their list - they harassed him\n"
"day and night.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 15032..15966
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/13
msgid ""
"It was only then that he gave himself over to the\n"
"Sandinistas.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 16063..17010
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/14
msgid ""
"He kept it hidden from us at first, so we would not\n"
"get hurt.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 17387..17916
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/15
msgid ""
"He sounds like a good father.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0160_000_0
#. timeline 18000..19964
#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/16
msgid ""
"He was... But my mother got fed up with it. She left\n"
"us. I don't blame her.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/17
msgid ""
"Why didn't you go with her?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/18
msgid ""
"It was a hard decision, for sure.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/19
msgid ""
"But like my father, I couldn't let Somoza get away\n"
"with his crimes. But most of all...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/20
#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/0
msgid ""
"Chico.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/21
msgid ""
"...He is too much like his papá. One way or the\n"
"other he was going to stay.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/22
msgid ""
"And I could not leave him behind.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/23
msgid ""
"Soon enough la Guardia drove us out, and we\n"
"found ourselves in the mountains...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/24
msgid ""
"It just kind of happened\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/25
msgid ""
"For an accidental revolutionary, you sure put up a\n"
"hell of a fight.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/26
msgid ""
"The mountains make men into warriors. The\n"
"training is harsh,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/27
msgid ""
"but it brings us that much closer to being hombres\n"
"nuevos.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/28
msgid ""
"Chico couldn't ask for a better sister.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/199/0xc76f0/29
msgid ""
"I can see why they picked you to be comandante.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/0
msgid ""
"When I was little, I came down with malaria.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/1
msgid ""
"Unlucky for me, it was the bad kind. I was in a\n"
"daze the whole time,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/2
msgid ""
"and at one point they said I was not going to make\n"
"it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/3
msgid ""
"Malarial encephalopathy. I hear it's pretty common\n"
"in tropical malaria cases.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/4
msgid ""
"Even today, my memory sometimes gets a little\n"
"fuzzy.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/5
msgid ""
"Since then I've had this fear of mosquitoes... When\n"
"I hear them buzzing nearby, I get jumpy.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/6
msgid ""
"That explains the chain-smoking?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/7
msgid ""
"Si. I thought it might help keep the mosquitoes\n"
"away, just a little.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/8
msgid ""
"Maybe it's all in my head. You're the same way,\n"
"right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/9
msgid ""
"I will say this - I prefer a cigar over mosquitoes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/10
msgid ""
"Me, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/11
msgid ""
"I've gotta hand it to you. It takes guts to conquer\n"
"your fear like that\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/12
msgid ""
"and live a guerrilla's life in the wild.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/13
msgid ""
"It is nothing. El Che did not let asthma stop him\n"
"from leading the revolution.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8150/14
msgid ""
"Compared to him, I am no hero.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/0
msgid ""
"I'm sorry to hear about your dad.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/1
msgid ""
"Thank you for saying that... Mi viejo was the leader\n"
"of the frente.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/2
msgid ""
"He was the last of the generation that knew\n"
"General Sandino...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/3
msgid ""
"He saw the General's exploits first-hand as a boy.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/4
msgid ""
"He would tell us stories about it all the time... and\n"
"about how the General was assassinated.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/5
msgid ""
"Did you know he was getting money from the KGB?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/6
msgid ""
"I had some idea... But I did not have the courage to\n"
"confront him about it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/7
msgid ""
"I know it was a painful decision for him to make.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/8
#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/9
msgid ""
"I can imagine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/9
msgid ""
"Yes, my father was a good man. I loved him as a\n"
"daughter. And his soldiers believed in him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/10
msgid ""
"Thanks to him, la Frente held together even in the\n"
"worst of times.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc86c0/11
msgid ""
"I don't know if I can ever fill his shoes...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/0
msgid ""
"Chico's 12, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/2
msgid ""
"Isn't he a little... short for his age?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/3
msgid ""
"...Malnourishment. Food is hard to come by when\n"
"you're running around in the jungle...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/4
msgid ""
"He's got quite an appetite.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/5
msgid ""
"I know!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/6
msgid ""
"I didn't want him to come in the first place.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/7
msgid ""
"But there was no one to take him in. I had no\n"
"choice but to look after him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/8
msgid ""
"Don't be so hard on yourself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/9
msgid ""
"Sometimes it's better for a kid to be with his family\n"
"than far away, in a safe place.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/10
msgid ""
"Thank you...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/11
msgid ""
"Promise me this, though. When your fight is over,\n"
"make sure he gets a proper education.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/12
msgid ""
"Give him a chance to be something other than a\n"
"guerrilla.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/13
msgid ""
"It's not too late to teach him something other than\n"
"fighting.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/14
msgid ""
"OK. I promise.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/15
msgid ""
"...You know what book Chico really likes?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/16
msgid ""
"The \"World Encyclopedia of Mysterious Creatures.\"\n"
"The Loch Ness Monster, the Yeti...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/17
msgid ""
"UMAs. Yeah, I know.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/18
msgid ""
"He's still so much like a boy... I worry about him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/19
msgid ""
"He'll be fine. I know plenty of grown men who still\n"
"go crazy over UMAs.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/20
msgid ""
"Are... are you serious?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/0
msgid ""
"You've taken such good care of me since you\n"
"saved me from el colibri.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/1
msgid ""
"I want to return the favor.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/2
msgid ""
"Just wait until you're healed up. Then we'll talk.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/3
msgid ""
"I appreciate that. But you need all the help you\n"
"can get.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/4
msgid ""
"It might take a while for me to heal completely,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/5
msgid ""
"but I'll be fine once I'm on my feet. Put me in a\n"
"combat unit - I'll pull my weight.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/6
msgid ""
"I wouldn't expect any less from a Sandinista\n"
"comandante.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/7
msgid ""
"Enough flattery.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/8
msgid ""
"But seriously, it does not feel right for me to be\n"
"sitting here while my compas are out risking their\n"
"lives.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/9
msgid ""
"One thing's for sure. Having you out in the field\n"
"would be a big boost to Sandinista morale.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/10
msgid ""
"Of course, our ultimate goal is still the overthrow\n"
"of Somoza.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/11
msgid ""
"But until we get ourselves back in order, we will\n"
"follow your lead, wherever it takes us.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc91f0/12
msgid ""
"Glad to have you on board.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/0
msgid ""
"Amanda, you getting used to Mother Base?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/1
msgid ""
"Yes, it is Heaven compared to living in the\n"
"mountains.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/2
msgid ""
"We're no longer constantly on the run from la\n"
"Guardia or mercenaries.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/3
msgid ""
"Some of the new guys we've recruited used to be\n"
"mercenaries...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/4
msgid ""
"We're getting along. It was difficult at first,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/5
msgid ""
"but once you talk to them you realize we've got\n"
"plenty in common.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/6
msgid ""
"I see. Good to hear.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/7
msgid ""
"We may be enemies, but we're all still human\n"
"beings...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/8
msgid ""
"La CIA's soldiers, la Guardia... The same goes for\n"
"the people of America.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/9
msgid ""
"What's gotten into you?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/10
msgid ""
"Mi viejo got involved with drugs in order to scrape\n"
"together money for la revolución.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/11
msgid ""
"He did whatever the KGB said.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/12
msgid ""
"All for Nicaragua... or so he told himself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/13
msgid ""
"But I realize now... In the end all he did was help\n"
"poison young people of America.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/15
msgid ""
"...I've made up my mind. Even when I leave Mother\n"
"Base and return to la revolución,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/16
msgid ""
"I will never turn to drugs. Nor will I look to the KGB\n"
"for help.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/17
msgid ""
"If we topple Somoza using the KGB and drug\n"
"money, we will lose the people's hearts.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/18
msgid ""
"So you're choosing a different path from your\n"
"father.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/19
msgid ""
"I still respect him. But I will not do things the way\n"
"he did.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/20
msgid ""
"Well, I'm sure Chico will be glad to hear that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/21
msgid ""
"Chico is a grown soldier now. I could not face him\n"
"otherwise.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/22
msgid ""
"Well said, Amanda. Those are the words of a true\n"
"comandante.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/23
msgid ""
"Stop... I was inspired by the greatest comandante I\n"
"have ever known, Boss.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/0
msgid ""
"Amanda, how do I get to the prison camp?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/1
msgid ""
"First head up the narrow mountain path.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/2
msgid ""
"The path will gradually open up, and you'll come to\n"
"a fork in the road.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/3
msgid ""
"Watch yourself up there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/4
msgid ""
"You'll be lower than the surrounding terrain,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/5
msgid ""
"so if you head down the middle you'll make for an\n"
"easy target.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/6
msgid ""
"Thanks for the heads-up.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca000/7
msgid ""
"Take the leftward path to reach the prison camp.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 431..1030
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/0
msgid ""
"What can you tell me about the prison camp?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 1058..2117
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/1
msgid ""
"Well, it used to be a village - until they took control\n"
"of it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 2145..3065
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/2
msgid ""
"It is a maze of paths, so watch out for soldiers on\n"
"patrol.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 3301..3956
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/3
msgid ""
"I'll be sure not to stop and say \"hi.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 3984..4931
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/4
msgid ""
"Use the paths carefully and you should be able to\n"
"stay out of view.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 4959..5489
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/5
msgid ""
"Where are they holding Chico?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 5530..6645
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/6
msgid ""
"One of the houses, most likely. You can peek\n"
"through the doors.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 6659..7523
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/7
msgid ""
"Just press <I=ACT> when the Icon appears.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 7718..8735
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/8
msgid ""
"You could also listen to any sounds inside for clues.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 8749..9013
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/9
msgid ""
"Good idea.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 9041..10198
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/10
msgid ""
"Guards will still be on the move while you're looking\n"
"inside. Make sure you don't get caught.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 10212..10407
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/11
msgid ""
"And Snake...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 10421..11187
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/12
msgid ""
"I know. I'll bring him back.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0020_010_0
#. timeline 11201..12051
#: codec/1/202/0xca2d0/13
msgid ""
"Thank you. I know I can count on you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/0
msgid ""
"Amanda, do you know the way to the rail terminal?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/1
msgid ""
"Remember the locomotive? By the fork in the road\n"
"before the village?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/2
msgid ""
"Yeah, back in the jungle.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/3
msgid ""
"Follow the train tracks from there and you'll come\n"
"to the terminal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/4
msgid ""
"But there's a plant along the way.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/5
msgid ""
"Disguised as a coffee factory?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/6
msgid ""
"...Yes, it is their drug refining plant. La CIA controls\n"
"it now.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/7
msgid ""
"Cutting through there is the shortest way, but it'll\n"
"be crawling with soldiers.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/8
msgid ""
"If you want go around...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/9
msgid ""
"No, forget it. If that's the shortest way, that's the\n"
"way I'll take.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/10
msgid ""
"Besides, it's one of their bases. It'll be good intel.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/11
msgid ""
"Very good. A number of the guards at the plant\n"
"are positioned on high walkways.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/12
msgid ""
"Be sure to study their movements before you\n"
"advance.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/13
msgid ""
"Or I could just snipe them first...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/14
msgid ""
"The plant's layout is another maze, I'm afraid. Stay\n"
"cool.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/15
msgid ""
"Make your way out of the plant and you'll arrive at\n"
"the terminal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/16
msgid ""
"You know a lot about this place...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/17
msgid ""
"What are you saying? I've been there before -\n"
"when the KGB ran it - yes,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/18
msgid ""
"but it is not as if I enjoyed it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/19
msgid ""
"No, I just meant you know a lot about how the\n"
"enemy works.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/20
msgid ""
"I hope so.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/21
msgid ""
"Anyway, did you talk to Chico about the terminal?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/22
msgid ""
"He said it's where they transfer the cargo onto\n"
"trucks.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/23
msgid ""
"Meaning the facility is of considerable importance\n"
"to them. Don't get careless.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/24
msgid ""
"I won't.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/25
msgid ""
"By the way,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/26
msgid ""
"I've heard of a shortcut that cuts straight to the\n"
"coffee factory to the east of the village,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/27
msgid ""
"but I've never used it myself. Check it out if you're\n"
"interested.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/202/0xca770/28
msgid ""
"Thanks for the tip.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 445..1226
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/0
msgid ""
"An enemy tank! Is there somewhere you can hide,\n"
"Boss?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 1253..2215
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/1
msgid ""
"There are train cars, but they won't hold up\n"
"against a gun like that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 2243..2869
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/2
msgid ""
"Even a freight train? Incredible!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 3009..3887
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/3
msgid ""
"But they'd keep me out of sight - temporarily.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 3914..5196
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/4
msgid ""
"Use them to look for an opportunity to hit its\n"
"treads or the fuel tank at the back, but...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 5196..5781
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/5
msgid ""
"Don't forget about that gun, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 5795..6506
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/6
msgid ""
"Or the soldiers. They may try to flank you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 6645..8219
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/8
msgid ""
"You can also stop it by taking out all the soldiers.\n"
"You can do it, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 445..1657
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/0
msgid ""
"Amanda, do I have to take the fork in the road\n"
"back to the village?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 1685..2925
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/1
msgid ""
"People say there is a shortcut. Go back to the\n"
"coffee factory entrance,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 2939..3469
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/2
msgid ""
"then follow the path on the right.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 3496..4082
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/3
msgid ""
"That will take you straight to the village.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 4109..4820
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/4
msgid ""
"They may have increased security in that area,\n"
"though.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 5015..6534
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/5
msgid ""
"Not surprising, after what happened with the tank.\n"
"What do I do once I'm back at the village?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 6561..8010
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/6
msgid ""
"Destroy the barricade at the north side. From\n"
"there you can reconnect with the transport route.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 8024..8874
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/7
msgid ""
"Hmm... I'll need C4 for that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 8888..9738
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/8
msgid ""
"The explosion will bring everyone running too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 9766..10727
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/9
msgid ""
"There's probably going to be a fight - one way or\n"
"the other.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 10755..11730
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/10
msgid ""
"They might not see you if you stick to the\n"
"narrower pathways.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 11800..12552
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/11
msgid ""
"Then just climb over any obstacles.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0050_000_0
#. timeline 12566..13583
#: codec/1/203/0xcb450/12
msgid ""
"Don't let your guard down after taking out the\n"
"barricade, either.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 445..1226
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/0
msgid ""
"Chico says there's a bridge north of the village.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 1253..2020
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/1
msgid ""
"Yes, a narrow one - for crossing the pipe.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 2159..2981
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/2
msgid ""
"On the other side of that is the road the trucks\n"
"use,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 3023..3482
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/3
msgid ""
"though it's collapsed in places.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 3622..4249
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/4
msgid ""
"I'll have nowhere to run if they spot me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 4263..4792
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/5
msgid ""
"They could be blocking the road, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 4820..5182
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/6
msgid ""
"Is there another way?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 5196..5851
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/7
msgid ""
"There is a path along the cliff.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 5879..6993
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/8
msgid ""
"After you cross the bridge, there are ruins of a\n"
"fort on the mountain.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 7049..7704
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/9
msgid ""
"Going through there would be a little easier.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_000_0
#. timeline 7746..8888
#: codec/1/203/0xcb950/10
msgid ""
"Once you come to the end of the mountain path,\n"
"you'll be at the fort.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0
#. timeline 431..1950
#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/0
msgid ""
"That fort was built during the civil war. It seems la\n"
"CIA's troops are occupying it, now.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0
#. timeline 2187..2856
#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/1
msgid ""
"This just gets better and better.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0
#. timeline 2883..3859
#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/2
msgid ""
"They've got gun turrets set up all around, from the\n"
"looks of it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0
#. timeline 3887..4959
#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/3
msgid ""
"Attract too much attention and you'll really stir up\n"
"the hornet's nest.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0
#. timeline 4973..5558
#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/4
msgid ""
"Maybe I'll try and find a way around.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0060_010_0
#. timeline 5600..6854
#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/5
msgid ""
"You could always commandeer one of the turrets -\n"
"a little target practice, perhaps?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/6
msgid ""
"Just like Krasnogorje.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/7
msgid ""
"Krasno-what?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/203/0xcbd00/8
msgid ""
"Sorry, just... thinking about old times.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/0
msgid ""
"Watch out! It's el galápago!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/1
msgid ""
"It reduces its body weight by blasting air\n"
"underneath it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/2
msgid ""
"That makes it a lot faster than any tank. It also\n"
"has a tight turning radius.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/3
msgid ""
"Any weak points?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/4
msgid ""
"Taking out its boosters could reduce its\n"
"acceleration...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/5
msgid ""
"You could also try destroying its machine guns.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/6
msgid ""
"I'll give it a shot.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/204/0xcc050/7
msgid ""
"We've lost many compas to that thing. Send it to\n"
"the scrapyard!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 459..1894
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/0
msgid ""
"From here on in you'll be in a cloud forest. The\n"
"ground is covered in vegetation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 1922..2897
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/1
msgid ""
"You'll have plenty of hiding places, but so will the\n"
"enemy.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 2925..3496
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/2
msgid ""
"I'll keep an eye out for scouts.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 3524..4360
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/3
msgid ""
"Trying to force your way through would be suicide.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 4388..5377
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/4
msgid ""
"Know the enemy's location before making any\n"
"moves.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 5405..6004
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/5
msgid ""
"Too bad you don't have some sort of radar.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 6227..6715
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/6
msgid ""
"I could try night vision.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 6729..7843
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/7
msgid ""
"Once you know where an enemy is, decide how you\n"
"want to handle him.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 7871..8373
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/8
msgid ""
"You could get into his blindspots...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 8414..9626
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/9
msgid ""
"Or drop him from a distance before he even has a\n"
"clue someone's around.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0080_000_0
#. timeline 9640..10267
#: codec/1/204/0xcc320/10
msgid ""
"An eye for an eye, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 431..1323
#: codec/1/204/0xcc700/0
msgid ""
"Don't even think about facing a chopper head-on.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 1351..2145
#: codec/1/204/0xcc700/1
msgid ""
"Guerilla tactics would work well in a place like that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 2159..3357
#: codec/1/204/0xcc700/2
msgid ""
"Moving from tree to tree will make it hard to get a\n"
"fix on you from the air.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 3385..3747
#: codec/1/204/0xcc700/3
msgid ""
