#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 9557..10407
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/8
msgid ""
"\"a metal gear linking infantry and artillery...\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 10421..10741
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/9
msgid ""
"Metal gear...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 11201..11828
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/10
msgid ""
"I've got a bad feeling about this.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 11981..12859
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/11
msgid ""
"Like maybe it's connected to everything that's\n"
"happening here somehow.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 12901..13806
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/12
msgid ""
"The nukes? You don't think...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 13834..15353
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/13
msgid ""
"...What else could it be? If it is up there, I'll just\n"
"have to improvise.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 15422..16202
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/14
msgid ""
"Either way, I won't know until I get there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 16244..16676
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/15
msgid ""
"Watch your back, Snake...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 445..1184
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/0
msgid ""
"So there's a real basilisco that lives in the river?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 1184..2326
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/1
msgid ""
"I'm only saying I heard stories from people who\n"
"said they saw it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 2410..3650
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/2
msgid ""
"But I know lots of places to find it in Nicaragua.\n"
"You wanna go have a look?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 3678..4263
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/3
msgid ""
"I don't have time for sightseeing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 4611..4987
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/4
msgid ""
"You don't like lizards?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 5015..5962
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/5
msgid ""
"It's not that. I just think snakes taste better.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 5976..6422
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/6
msgid ""
"...Who said anything about taste?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 6492..7007
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/7
msgid ""
"How about you? You like 'em?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 7007..8791
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/8
msgid ""
"Not that way... they do look kinda like dinosaurs,\n"
"though. You don't think that's cool?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 8944..10170
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/9
msgid ""
"They're both reptiles, yeah. But there's a big\n"
"difference size-wise.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 10170..11006
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/10
msgid ""
"I'll bet there are still big ones around somewhere.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 11089..12385
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/11
msgid ""
"They say mammals multiplied and ate up their\n"
"eggs, but they can't all be gone.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 12469..13026
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/12
msgid ""
"They've gotta exist somewhere out there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 13625..14001
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/13
msgid ""
"Dinosaur eggs, huh...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 14029..14586
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/14
msgid ""
"And animals are always evolving, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 14698..15757
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/15
msgid ""
"Maybe they evolved so much they don't even look\n"
"like dinosaurs anymore.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 15770..16592
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/16
msgid ""
"Then you can't really call them dinosaurs, can you?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 16620..18362
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/17
msgid ""
"I guess not... Yeah, you're right, dinosaurs've gotta\n"
"be big!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_000_0
#. timeline 431..1630
#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/0
msgid ""
"Irazú has more than one crater, 'cause it's erupted\n"
"so many times.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_000_0
#. timeline 1671..2758
#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/1
msgid ""
"I heard most of them filled up with rainwater and\n"
"became lakes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_000_0
#. timeline 27439..44878
#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/2
msgid ""
"Calderas, huh.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/3
msgid ""
"Calderas? Yeah, something like that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/4
msgid ""
"...Hey, I got an idea.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/5
msgid ""
"When you get to the lake, can you keep an eye out\n"
"for weird animals for me?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/6
msgid ""
"People all over the world tell stories about giant\n"
"monsters living in lakes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/7
msgid ""
"Nessie in Loch Ness, Nahuelito in Argentina,\n"
"Ogopogo in Canada...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/8
msgid ""
"I can hardly keep track of them all.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/9
msgid ""
"They say that all these sightings prove dinosaurs\n"
"do still exist.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/10
msgid ""
"But crater lakes are isolated. They're not\n"
"connected to rivers.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/11
msgid ""
"Yeah, but... you know Mokèlé-mbèmbé? In the\n"
"Congo River? He can walk on land.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/12
msgid ""
"So maybe they moved there from some other lake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/13
msgid ""
"You sure know a lot about UMAs.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/14
msgid ""
"There used to be a guy in el Frente who was a\n"
"hunter. He taught me lots of things.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/15
msgid ""
"He even said he once went to a place called Isla\n"
"del Monstruo.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/16
msgid ""
"A hunter on Isla del Monstruo...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/17
msgid ""
"Someday, I'm gonna be a hunter and catch some\n"
"rare animals.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/18
msgid ""
"Right after we restore peace to our land, of course.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 459..1030
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/0
msgid ""
"You ever hear of the Loch Ness Monster?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 1044..2187
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/1
msgid ""
"Now that one I know. Pretty much everyone's\n"
"heard of ol' Nessie.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 2215..3859
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/2
msgid ""
"Great, so I don't have to explain. I think she's a\n"
"long-lost dinosaur, don't you?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 3887..4611
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/3
msgid ""
"Uh, sure, why not.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 4625..5503
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/4
msgid ""
"One of the compas gave me a book about it - with\n"
"photos.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 5558..6199
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/5
msgid ""
"It looks exactly like the plesiosaur.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 6227..6840
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/6
msgid ""
"...Then why does it only live in Loch Ness?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 6854..7509
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/7
msgid ""
"Well it probably got cut off from the ocean.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 7592..8178
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/8
msgid ""
"Back when Loch Ness was part of the ocean,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 8219..9111
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/9
msgid ""
"some plesiosaurs became trapped there when the\n"
"climate changed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 9195..10086
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/10
msgid ""
"There weren't any mammals there, so no natural\n"
"predators.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 10156..11048
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/11
msgid ""
"Today's Nessie is descended from those\n"
"plesiosaurs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 11048..12594
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/12
msgid ""
"Then... wouldn't it make sense for there to be\n"
"monsters in other lakes with similar climates?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 12608..13987
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/13
msgid ""
"Exactly! That's why there's been giant monster\n"
"sightings in a bunch of other places\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 14029..14879
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/14
msgid ""
"- like Nahuelito and Ogopogo.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 14949..15575
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/15
msgid ""
"I don't know if there's one in Irazú, too...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 15617..16620
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/16
msgid ""
"But I know there's definitely something living in\n"
"Lago Cocibolca.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 445..1365
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/0
msgid ""
"You mentioned the Nahuelito... What is it?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 1365..3204
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/1
msgid ""
"It's a plesiosaur that lives in Lago Nahuel Huapi in\n"
"Argentina. It's described a little differently,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 3232..4931
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/2
msgid ""
"but I'm sure it's basically the same creature as\n"
"Nessie. Except for one thing...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 5099..6784
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/4
msgid ""
"Well, according to one theory, it's the result of a\n"
"nuclear test back in the '50s...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 6826..7969
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/5
msgid ""
"What? There's no record of a nuclear test in\n"
"Argentina in the '50s.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 8024..8860
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/6
msgid ""
"At the time the president, General Juan Peron,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 8874..9585
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/7
msgid ""
"was pushing hard to industrialize the country.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 9696..10630
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/8
msgid ""
"I wouldn't be surprised if he conducted a\n"
"top-secret nuclear test\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 10685..11187
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/9
msgid ""
"before he was overthrown in a coup.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 11521..12190
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/10
msgid ""
"Sounds a little far-fetched to me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 12204..13555
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/11
msgid ""
"You think? Then maybe Nahuelito really is a\n"
"dinosaur.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 13583..14043
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/12
msgid ""
"No, I didn't say...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 14071..14795
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/13
msgid ""
"I mean, it's really pretty obvious...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 14837..15018
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/14
msgid ""
"Wait a...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 15130..15631
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/15
msgid ""
"Thanks for clearing that up, Boss!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 15659..16272
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/16
msgid ""
"... dinosaur...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 445..2048
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/0
msgid ""
"Mokèlé-mbèmbé lives in the Congo River. There's\n"
"nothing mysterious about it, though\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 2089..3051
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/1
msgid ""
"- it's already been confirmed as a real, living\n"
"dinosaur.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 3120..4402
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/2
msgid ""
"The local people know all about it, and when they\n"
"were shown a drawing of a brontosaurus,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 4458..5280
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/3
msgid ""
"every one of them said it was Mokèlé-mbèmbé.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 5405..6534
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/4
msgid ""
"When peace returns to Nicaragua, I wanna go to\n"
"the Congo myself...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 6798..7746
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/5
msgid ""
"...The revolutionary movement in the Congo ended\n"
"in failure, you know.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 7760..9348
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/6
msgid ""
"Yeah, I know. I wish we could do something to help,\n"
"but Africa's awfully far away.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 9376..9585
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/7
msgid ""
"Africa...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 9626..10421
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/8
msgid ""
"I wonder if El Che ever saw Mokèlé-mbèmbé...?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 10476..10853
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/9
msgid ""
"I wonder if I will...?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 11173..12106
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/10
msgid ""
"Best to take care of business here before\n"
"daydreaming about Africa.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 12134..12775
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/11
msgid ""
"Yeah, I guess you're right...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/1
msgid ""
"You know much about cloud forests?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/2
msgid ""
"Not that much... All I know is\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/3
msgid ""
"there's a world of difference between a rainy rain\n"
"forest and a foggy cloud forest.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/4
msgid ""
"But they have some things in common...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/5
msgid ""
"Like for instance you gotta watch out for poison\n"
"dart frogs.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/6
msgid ""
"Both rain and cloud forests have high humidity,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/7
msgid ""
"so they're perfect environments for frogs and\n"
"other amphibians.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/8
msgid ""
"I mean, it's not like just touching a strawberry\n"
"poison dart frog or\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/9
msgid ""
"a dyeing dart frog is going to kill you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/10
msgid ""
"But don't eat 'em, no matter how hungry you get.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/11
msgid ""
"I can get all the rations I need from Mother Base.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/12
msgid ""
"No jungle food for me this time.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/13
msgid ""
"Seriously? You're not disappointed you don't get to\n"
"eat wild animals?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/14
msgid ""
"...What do you think I am?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/15
msgid ""
"Ha ha ha. Just kidding. In Colombia, though, there's\n"
"a frog\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/16
msgid ""
"- the golden dart frog - that's lethal to the touch.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/17
msgid ""
"How do you know all this?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/18
msgid ""
"C'mon, don't you think poisonous animals are cool?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/19
msgid ""
"Not if you get poisoned by one.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/20
msgid ""
"Well, obviously. One more thing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/21
msgid ""
"When you get to the forest, be on the lookout for\n"
"Bigfoot.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/22
msgid ""
"I... think I'll be OK there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 459..1393
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/0
msgid ""
"Gotta admit, I've never heard of Mono Grande.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 1407..2814
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/1
msgid ""
"Yeah, he's not as famous as Bigfoot. He's similar,\n"
"but he lives in Venezuela.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 2856..3622
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/2
msgid ""
"He's not that big - less than two vara (5.5 ft)\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 3678..4374
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/3
msgid ""
"- but he's way more ferocious than Bigfoot.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 4820..6199
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/4
msgid ""
"I wonder just how mean he is? Like when he\n"
"catches his prey, does he punch it to death...?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 6213..7941
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/5
msgid ""
"That's the law of the wild: you catch your prey,\n"
"you kill it, and you eat it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 7955..8888
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/6
msgid ""
"Yeah! Yeah! But punching is way more ferocious\n"
"than biting.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 9083..10017
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/7
msgid ""
"Maybe it seems that way because that's what\n"
"humans do.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 10044..10783
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/8
msgid ""
"...You really love UMAs, don't you, Chico?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 10811..11953
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/9
msgid ""
"You know what I think? I think UMAs should be\n"
"dangerous.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 12037..12775
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/10
msgid ""
"Otherwise where's the fun in hunting them?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/0
msgid ""
"Did you see a quetzal, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/1
msgid ""
"Yep.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/2
msgid ""
"What do you think? Did it look like a snake?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/3
msgid ""
"Huh? No, it didn't look like a snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/4
msgid ""
"Oh, really? ...Must be different from the\n"
"quetzalcoatl, then.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/5
msgid ""
"Quetzalcoatl?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/6
msgid ""
"A winged snake from Mayan and Aztec legend.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/7
msgid ""
"A winged snake...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/8
msgid ""
"Weird, right? I bet it's a UMA.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/9
msgid ""
"Amanda and everybody says Quetzalcoatl is a\n"
"quetzal in the form of a god.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/10
msgid ""
"But there's no way anybody'd mistake a snake for\n"
"a bird,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/11
msgid ""
"I think the legend of Quetzalcoatl came first.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/12
msgid ""
"Somebody saw it and adopted it as their god,\n"
"before they saw the quetzal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/13
msgid ""
"After that, somebody saw a bird that looked like\n"
"the image of the god,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/14
msgid ""
"and so they named it \"quetzal.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/15
msgid ""
"You mean it happened the other way around?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/16
msgid ""
"If you ask me, the quetzalcoatl was probably a\n"
"pterosaur that survived.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/17
msgid ""
"I mean, it's got wings, and it's a reptile, so it\n"
"probably looks kind of like a snake, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/18
msgid ""
"Pterosaurs live on in Africa even today. They're\n"
"called the Kongamato and the Olitiau.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/19
msgid ""
"So it makes sense that there'd be pterosaurs on\n"
"the American continent, too,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/20
msgid ""
"and that they survived until the Mayan and Aztec\n"
"eras.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/21
msgid ""
"Lucky for us they're not still around today.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/22
msgid ""
"Who says they aren't? The dinosaurs supposedly\n"
"died out 65 million years ago,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/23
msgid ""
"and the Aztec civilization only arose about 600\n"
"years ago.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/24
msgid ""
"If they managed to survive 65 million years, surely\n"
"they couldn't be wiped out in 600.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 445..1922
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/0
msgid ""
"A base disguised as a mine? We never made it\n"
"that far.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 1964..3162
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/1
msgid ""
"I don't know what kind of place it is, but you'd\n"
"better be careful - just in case.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 3190..3496
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/2
msgid ""
"I plan to.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 3510..5196
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/3
msgid ""
"I've heard that the American army keeps dead alien\n"
"bodies and UFOs in secret bases.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 5461..5726
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/4
msgid ""
"Aliens?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 5726..6325
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/5
msgid ""
"There are billions of stars in space.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 6394..7523
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/6
msgid ""
"You've gotta think that at least a few have\n"
"civilizations more advanced than ours.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 7648..8526
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/7
msgid ""
"I'll bet they visit Earth in UFOs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 8596..9055
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/8
msgid ""
"In 1947,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 9083..10602
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/9
msgid ""
"the army actually announced they'd caught a flying,\n"
"disc-shaped object near Roswell, New Mexico.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 10699..11828
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/10
msgid ""
"Maybe you don't know about it, but those army\n"
"guys, they all know!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 12176..12455
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/11
msgid ""
"You don't say...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 12455..13736
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/12
msgid ""
"Anyway, there's no telling what kind of mystery\n"
"weapons they might have stashed up there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 13848..14182
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/13
msgid ""
"Watch your back.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/0
msgid ""
"Apparently, UFOs are connected to cattle\n"
"mutilations.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/1
msgid ""
"Cattle mutations?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/2
msgid ""
"Not mutations. Mutilations... It's a word I'd never\n"
"heard before.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/3
msgid ""
"People have been reporting their livestock dying\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/4
msgid ""
"in mysterious ways near the same places where\n"
"UFOs have been sighted.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/5
msgid ""
"They say\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/6
msgid ""
"the bodies are drained of blood and the eyeballs\n"
"and sexual organs are gouged out.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/7
msgid ""
"When you leave a corpse cut open in a field\n"
"somewhere, the ground soaks up the blood.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/8
msgid ""
"Yeah, but supposedly these cows weren't cut up\n"
"by any man-made means.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/9
msgid ""
"Maybe maggots got to 'em?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/10
msgid ""
"In some cases they detected radiation.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/11
msgid ""
"Radiation...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/12
msgid ""
"Even in our own town we had goats that died in\n"
"strange ways.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/13
msgid ""
"Some said they saw a monster\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/14
msgid ""
"- a lizard on two legs, covered in spines from its\n"
"head all the way down its back.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/15
msgid ""
"I wonder if that's what the aliens look like,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/16
msgid ""
"or if it was some pet they brought with them...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/17
msgid ""
"...Either way, it doesn't sound like a very advanced\n"
"civilization to me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/18
msgid ""
"If you see one, tell it I said \"hi!\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/19
msgid ""
"Sure... if it speaks human.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 459..1532
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/0
msgid ""
"You wanna know something? I once met an alien\n"
"cat.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 1546..2229
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/1
msgid ""
"An alien... cat?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 2243..3051
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/2
msgid ""
"Yep. It was dark out so I couldn't see too well,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 3120..3956
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/3
msgid ""
"but it was a cat with a huge long tail.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 3998..4500
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/4
msgid ""
"Its eyes shined in the dark, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 4513..4987
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/5
msgid ""
"Most cats' eyes do...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 5001..6854
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/6
msgid ""
"At first I thought it was a regular cat. But then it\n"
"started talking to me - inside my head.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 6868..7230
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/7
msgid ""
"...Inside your head?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 7230..8345
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/8
msgid ""
"He said his name was Altargozo Elbakki Munyudar.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 8400..9682
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/9
msgid ""
"He'd come to Earth from the Andromeda Galaxy to\n"
"check out Earth's nuclear weapons...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 9724..10992
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/10
msgid ""
"The Andromeda Galaxy... Mankind's barely made it\n"
"to the moon.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 11089..11702
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/11
msgid ""
"We couldn't possibly launch nukes that far.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 11716..13054
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/12
msgid ""
"Elbakki said he was watching over us - to make\n"
"sure we don't destroy ourselves with nukes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 13123..14113
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/13
msgid ""
"Until the day we humans are ready to join the\n"
"Space Federation...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 14489..15659
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/14
msgid ""
"...It's a shame. This is supposed to be the era of\n"
"Détente,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 15729..16899
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/15
msgid ""
"and still we've got people pulling stunts like\n"
"bringing nukes into peaceful countries.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 16941..18111
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/16
msgid ""
"If something ever went wrong and set off a chain\n"
"reaction of retaliation...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 18111..19379
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/17
msgid ""
"I know. This planet could destroy itself at anytime.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 459..1393
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/0
msgid ""
"Snake, is it true you took a picture of el colibri?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 1393..1964
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/1
msgid ""
"Yep. Got it right here.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 1978..4026
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/2
msgid ""
"Whoa! It's like an actual UFO! I knew it - los\n"
"yanquis are working with the aliens!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 4221..4973
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/3
msgid ""
"I know it kind of looks that way, but...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 4987..5684
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/4
msgid ""
"Hey Snake, can you make me a copy of that?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 5698..6506
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/5
msgid ""
"I don't see why not. What for?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 6520..7871
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/6
msgid ""
"People pay good money for this stuff. We can use\n"
"it to raise money for MSF.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 7927..9181
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/7
msgid ""
"Ha, sure, kid. You go out and get us a good price\n"
"for it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 9195..10518
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/8
msgid ""
"You don't believe me, do you? I'll get the money.\n"
"You'll see!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/0
msgid ""
"Chico. I, uh... I met that talking cat.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/1
msgid ""
"The legendary Trenya? Really?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/2
msgid ""
"Trenya? Yeah, that's what it called itself. Is it\n"
"famous?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/3
msgid ""
"In certain circles, yeah.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/4
msgid ""
"I'm still having trouble believing it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/5
msgid ""
"I never thought I'd be talking to an animal one day.\n"
"What a world.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/6
msgid ""
"Amazing you could understand its language.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/7
msgid ""
"Picking up the local lingo is one of the basics of\n"
"intelligence work.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/8
msgid ""
"That's what makes you the Boss, Boss! Hey, say\n"
"something in Trenya's language, will you?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/9
msgid ""
"Meow? Meow... Meow meow meow...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/10
msgid ""
"Wow! I have no idea what you're saying!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/11
msgid ""
"...Of course you wouldn't.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/12
msgid ""
"So what did Trenya say?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/13
msgid ""
"It said it would take me to that island you talked\n"
"about.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/14
msgid ""
"Really?! Take me too, Boss! Please, please!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/15
msgid ""
"I know you must be excited, but we don't know\n"
"what's out there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/16
msgid ""
"It could be dangerous. I'll scout it out first.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/17
msgid ""
"No fair!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/18
msgid ""
"Come on, Chico. This isn't as cut and dry as you\n"
"think.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/19
msgid ""
"You can come next time, depending on what I find.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/20
msgid ""
"I'll take some photos if I get the chance. Sorry,\n"
"kid, but that's life.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/0
msgid ""
"Apparently there are other cats that talk besides\n"
"Trenya on Isla del Monstruo.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/1
msgid ""
"There's more of them?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/2
msgid ""
"Yep. They're called the Felynes, but supposedly\n"
"they don't ever come to Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/3
msgid ""
"You should try talking to them if you spot them.\n"
"Who knows what kinda stuff they have to say.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/4
msgid ""
"Yeah. Just when you think things can't get any\n"
"crazier...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/5
msgid ""
"Also, the Felynes are nice to humans, so you be\n"
"sure and be nice back.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/6
msgid ""
"Don't you go attacking them or anything.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/7
msgid ""
"I would never hurt a defenseless little kitty.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/0
msgid ""
"Tigrex is a wyvern just like Rathalos.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/1
msgid ""
"But it's good at moving around on land, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/2
msgid ""
"It can blast you with rocks from a distance, or\n"
"rush at you with incredible speed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/3
msgid ""
"People have seen it on land?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/4
msgid ""
"Sí.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/5
msgid ""
"It's said that these two lady pirates, Anne and\n"
"Mary, visited Isla del Monstruo.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/6
msgid ""
"It was there that they did battle with Tigrex.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/7
msgid ""
"Anne was quite a marksman, wasn't she?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/8
msgid ""
"Must've been a heck of a battle. I wish I'd been\n"
"there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/9
msgid ""
"You know, I'm not so bad with guns myself...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/10
msgid ""
"I've already seen how good you are.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/0
msgid ""
"Anne and Mary also saw little dinosaurs running\n"
"around the island.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/1
msgid ""
"Velocipreys?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/2
msgid ""
"Yup. As you'd expect they're very nimble - but no\n"
"match for a firearm.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/3
msgid ""
"You wouldn't want to get surrounded by them,\n"
"though.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/4
msgid ""
"I'll bet. Nobody wants to be outnumbered in battle.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/5
msgid ""
"Right. Your best move would be to make sure they\n"
"cannot encircle you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/6
msgid ""
"Well, stealth is the basis of all solo sneaking\n"
"missions...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/7
msgid ""
"While it makes battle tougher,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/8
msgid ""
"working alone has its advantages when it comes to\n"
"infiltration.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/9
msgid ""
"That's what makes you the boss, Boss! You don't\n"
"need any advice from me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/10
msgid ""
"Not bad for an old-timer, eh Chico?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/11
msgid ""
"Nope. Still, be careful.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/0
msgid ""
"Have you heard the legend about the dinosaur that\n"
"came back to life as a zombie\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/1
msgid ""
"and attacked people?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/2
msgid ""
"Zombie?! You mean the living dead?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/3
msgid ""
"Yeah. Dinosaurs may be extinct,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/4
msgid ""
"but technically it would be possible for one to\n"
"come back to life as a zombie.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/5
msgid ""
"Not so fast. Dinosaurs were real, zombies... not so\n"
"much.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/6
msgid ""
"What are you talking about, Boss!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/7
msgid ""
"Zombies have been used as slaves on Haitian\n"
"plantations for years.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/8
msgid ""
"In Haiti they've handed down a secret zombie\n"
"powder for generations.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/10
msgid ""
"People from long ago must have used that same\n"
"stuff on dinosaur remains.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/11
msgid ""
"But dinosaurs had been extinct for millions of\n"
"years before the first humans-\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/12
msgid ""
"That hypothesis has to be wrong.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/13
msgid ""
"...In any case, this zombie was incredibly powerful.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/14
msgid ""
"Its name was Gear REX. They say nothing could kill\n"
"it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/15
msgid ""
"Some say its bodily fluids would burn right through\n"
"your flesh.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/16
msgid ""
"Then the spines that fell off its back would impale\n"
"you,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/17
msgid ""
"the pain made even worse by the deafening roar\n"
"rattling every bone in your body.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/18
msgid ""
"...You sure it wasn't just some really strong\n"
"monster?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/19
msgid ""
"Who knows what kind of dinosaurs were out there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/20
msgid ""
"We could be talking about something strong\n"
"enough to resist small arms fire.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/21
msgid ""
"Are you afraid of zombies, Boss?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/22
msgid ""
"...No. I just find the whole thing hard to believe.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/0
msgid ""
"A fantasma is an espiritu that wanders this plane\n"
"instead of going to el Cielo.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/1
msgid ""
"There are different interpretations, of course, but\n"
"that's what I think.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/2
msgid ""
"See, the fantasma has a reason for remaining in\n"
"this world.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/3
msgid ""
"And if that were, say, a deep hatred for someone,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/4
msgid ""
"they just might be capable of inflicting harm on\n"
"that person.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/5
msgid ""
"You probably realize this, but your weapons or\n"
"CQC won't work on fantasma.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/6
msgid ""
"And since they're not physical beings, they can\n"
"pass right through solid objects.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/7
msgid ""
"But, if you can eliminate their reason for remaining\n"
"here,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/8
msgid ""
"you should be able to help them reach el Cielo.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/9
msgid ""
"People say words can work wonders on fantasma.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/10
msgid ""
"You could try talking to them through CO-OPS\n"
"communication.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 459..1504
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/0
msgid ""
"You can't always see fantasma with your naked eye.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 1518..2967
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/1
msgid ""
"If some unseen presence is making a noise, you\n"
"can be sure one is around.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 2967..3956
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/2
msgid ""
"When that happens, try taking photos in the area.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 3970..4583
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/3
msgid ""
"You should be able to see what's causing it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 4597..5126
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/4
msgid ""
"Why do they show up on photos?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 5168..5739
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/5
msgid ""
"I'm not the one to ask about that, but...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 5753..7537
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/6
msgid ""
"Maybe fantasma are somehow able to deceive our\n"
"minds - on a subconscious level.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 7551..9153
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/7
msgid ""
"They're right there in front of us, but they whisper,\n"
"\"Hey, we're not really here!\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 9153..10616
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/8
msgid ""
"But a camera is a machine, so they can't do\n"
"anything to it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 10616..11466
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/9
msgid ""
"Yeah, that's it! That's gotta be it!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 445..1337
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/0
msgid ""
"That's a rangefinder camera you have, right, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 1337..2020
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/1
msgid ""
"Mi viejo used to talk about rangefinder cameras,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 2020..3274
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/2
msgid ""
"and how they can focus just as well as any other\n"
"camera, despite their size.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 3315..4193
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/3
msgid ""
"He also said they don't have much picture blur,\n"
"either.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 4207..4834
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/4
msgid ""
"To bring an object into focus,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 4834..5893
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/5
msgid ""
"make sure the two images overlap before taking\n"
"the picture.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 5907..6631
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/6
msgid ""
"But you could probably do that in your sleep,\n"
"couldn't you?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 6631..7871
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/7
msgid ""
"All you need to worry about is making sure your\n"
"subject is in the frame.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 7899..9181
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/8
msgid ""
"Remember, Snake, photography is all about timing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 459..891
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/0
msgid ""
"Sorry to hear about your dad.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 905..2229
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/1
msgid ""
"Don't be. He was... He is a guerrilla warrior.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 2326..3134
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/2
msgid ""
"We pledge our lives to our country and its people...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 3190..3705
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/3
msgid ""
"I'm ready to die, too, if I have to.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 3733..3984
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/4
msgid ""
"You sure?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 4054..5600
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/5
msgid ""
"You'd better believe it! Like mi viejo used to say,\n"
"\"Patria o Muerte.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 5948..6325
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/6
msgid ""
"Che said it first.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 6339..6924
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/7
msgid ""
"My dad used to tell us all kinds of stories.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 7007..7857
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/8
msgid ""
"About General Sandino and his fight against la\n"
"Guardia...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 7927..8470
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/9
msgid ""
"And about my mom before she left us.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 8512..8860
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/10
msgid ""
"You didn't want to go with her?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 8874..10072
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/11
msgid ""
"It's not like that. La revolución comes first, that's all.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 10142..10657
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/12
msgid ""
"You must wish you could see her, though.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 10671..12496
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/13
msgid ""
"I dunno. But I know I'll see her again when this is\n"
"all over. Somehow I just know it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 12566..13890
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/14
msgid ""
"When I do, me and mamá and papá are all going to\n"
"live together again.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 14210..14475
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/15
msgid ""
"At least...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 15241..15631
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/16
msgid ""
"At least, that's what I thought.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 17512..18529
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/17
msgid ""
"Hang in there, Chico. Your sister needs you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 459..1880
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/0
msgid ""
"Have you ever heard, \"Shoot, coward, you are only\n"
"going to kill a man\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 2256..2716
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/1
msgid ""
"Che's last words.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 2730..3260
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/2
msgid ""
"He'd been captured in Bolivia,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 3315..4207
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/3
msgid ""
"and said it to the soldiers just as they were about\n"
"to execute him.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 4207..5182
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/4
msgid ""
"El Che... He was something, wasn't he?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 5252..6227
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/5
msgid ""
"Coming up with a line like that knowing he was\n"
"about to die.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 6241..6743
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/6
msgid ""
"After the Cuban Revolution,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 6743..8094
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/7
msgid ""
"Che gave up his position in the new government to\n"
"aide in revolutions in other countries.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 8317..9473
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/8
msgid ""
"He knew he could die at any time, and he was\n"
"ready for it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 9487..10365
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/9
msgid ""
"Me, I couldn't take even a little torture...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 10407..11661
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/10
msgid ""
"But you've been reborn, as an hombre nuevo.\n"
"Right, Chico?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 11674..11925
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/11
msgid ""
"Right...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 445..1253
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/0
msgid ""
"Don't you ever get lonely living away from your\n"
"mom?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 1267..2173
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/1
msgid ""
"Not really. My compas are my family now.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 2270..2786
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/2
msgid ""
"A lot of them are from the same village as me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 2814..3538
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/3
msgid ""
"So you had plenty of people to take care of you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 3566..4890
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/4
msgid ""
"Take care of me?! I'm a warrior, like any other\n"
"Sandinista!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 4987..5809
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/5
msgid ""
"We look out for each other. That is how it works.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 5879..6645
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/6
msgid ""
"Sorry. Guess I misspoke.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 6659..8150
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/7
msgid ""
"Now we're scattered because of that colibri... I\n"
"wonder where everybody went.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 8345..9724
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/8
msgid ""
"Hey, Snake. If you see any Frente prisoners, please\n"
"you gotta get them out, OK?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 9766..10964
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/9
msgid ""
"Those guys are solid - every one. You could use\n"
"them in MSF.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/0
msgid ""
"What's with all this sighing? You're not your usual\n"
"self.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/1
msgid ""
"Oh. Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/2
msgid ""
"Something on your mind?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/3
msgid ""
"Huh? No, not... really. Not really... I guess...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/4
msgid ""
"Hey, Snake...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/5
msgid ""
"Uh huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/6
msgid ""
"Girls are funny, y'know?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/7
msgid ""
"You can never tell what they're thinking, they're\n"
"always doing their own thing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/8
msgid ""
"Maybe they really are different from us men...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/9
msgid ""
"Wh-what's this about now?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/10
msgid ""
"Chico... do you have a crush on somebody?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/11
msgid ""
"No! It's not that! I just...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/12
msgid ""
"What? Go ahead, you can talk to me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/13
msgid ""
"...Whenever I talk to Paz,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/14
msgid ""
"my heart starts pounding and everything I say\n"
"comes out wrong.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/15
msgid ""
"Paz? I guess she is... pretty close to your age.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/16
msgid ""
"That ever happen to you, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/17
msgid ""
"Well, sure. It happens to everybody.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/18
msgid ""
"Well, how do I talk to her?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/19
msgid ""
"...That is a tough one.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/20
msgid ""
"Uh... Why don't you try... talking to her like you talk\n"
"to everybody else?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/21
msgid ""
"No... It doesn't work. I freeze up every time I'm\n"
"around her.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/22
msgid ""
"Our eyes meet, and my face starts burning for\n"
"some reason...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/23
msgid ""
"It's like living on the battlefield - you'll just have to\n"
"get used to it... her.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/24
msgid ""
"You're nervous at first, but the more you're out\n"
"there, the more natural it feels.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/25
msgid ""
"Get your courage up and go talk to her more often.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/27
msgid ""
"Man, girls are more full of mysteries than UMAs...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/28
msgid ""
"You got that right.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/0
msgid ""
"Chico, I heard you saw Paz trying to sabotage\n"
"ZEKE before she activated it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/1
msgid ""
"I should have stopped her...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/2
msgid ""
"If only I hadn't run away...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/3
msgid ""
"I could have captured her before she got inside...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/4
msgid ""
"If I'd done that, she'd still be here...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/5
msgid ""
"She was carrying a gun - probably trained to use\n"
"it, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/6
msgid ""
"Don't blame yourself. You couldn't have stopped\n"
"her anyway. You were unarmed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/7
msgid ""
"I could at least have talked to her...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/8
msgid ""
"If I'd promised not to tell anyone, Paz wouldn't\n"
"have gone and done what she did...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/9
msgid ""
"It's just... It's just... I was so shocked, I panicked -\n"
"ran away...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/10
msgid ""
"Chico... when you saw Paz, she was trying to\n"
"sabotage it, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/11
msgid ""
"Huh? Well, yeah...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/12
msgid ""
"And right after that, she took control of it - tried\n"
"to make me surrender.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/13
msgid ""
"Something doesn't add up.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/14
msgid ""
"Why would she sabotage ZEKE when she was\n"
"about to use it against me?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/15
msgid ""
"Her actions were inconsistent, even for a spy.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/16
msgid ""
"If she wanted to destroy ZEKE, she could have\n"
"done it and run away.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/17
msgid ""
"But if her goal was to steal ZEKE, she'd have no\n"
"motive to sabotage it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/18
msgid ""
"I don't know...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/19
msgid ""
"Maybe your seeing her caused her to change her\n"
"plan? I don't get it...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 376..1156
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/0
msgid ""
"...You think Paz was planning to double-cross\n"
"Cipher?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 1170..2006
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/1
msgid ""
"Without ZEKE, she wouldn't have any way to\n"
"threaten you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 2020..3051
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/2
msgid ""
"If that were the case, she could have told me all\n"
"that from the beginning.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 3092..3761
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/3
msgid ""
"She wouldn't have had to try and sabotage it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 3775..4096
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/4
msgid ""
"I guess so...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 4123..5851
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/5
msgid ""
"But that was the day before Peace Day. Paz was\n"
"going to sing in a band. I couldn't wait to hear her.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 5907..7397
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/6
msgid ""
"What if she wasn't going to double cross them...\n"
"maybe she just wanted to at least be able to enjoy\n"
"that...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 7425..7718
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/7
msgid ""
"Chico...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 7746..8818
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/8
msgid ""
"I knew it... If only I hadn't run away...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 8832..9835
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/9
msgid ""
"If I'd talked to her... promised I wouldn't tell\n"
"anybody...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 9849..11270
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/10
msgid ""
"Don't second-guess yourself. Think about who\n"
"might have been hurt if you'd kept quiet.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 11298..11563
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/11
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/13
#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/2
msgid ""
"Yeah, but...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 11577..12524
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/12
msgid ""
"Besides, we don't know for sure she's dead.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 12552..13709
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/13
msgid ""
"She was ejected into the ocean. And she had\n"
"scuba equipment with her.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 13736..13973
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/14
#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/1
msgid ""
"Yeah...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 13987..15450
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/15
msgid ""
"Stop beating yourself up over the past, Chico - put\n"
"your hope in the future.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 15478..16676
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/16
msgid ""
"The past is the past, but the future is up to you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 16732..17136
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/17
msgid ""
"...Right, Boss.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 501..1365
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/0
msgid ""
"\"AI\" stands for artificial intelligence.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 1448..2479
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/1
msgid ""
"It refers to a manmade machine possessing an\n"
"intellect on par\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 2479..2883
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/2
msgid ""
"with that of a human being.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 2883..3287
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/3
msgid ""
"Is that even possible?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 3315..4151
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/4
msgid ""
"Possible? You've seen it with your own eyes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 4249..4973
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/5
msgid ""
"What the AI weapons are capable of.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 4987..5935
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/6
msgid ""
"How Peace Walker carried out The Boss' will in the\n"
"end.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 5990..7105
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/7
msgid ""
"No mere machine could ever choose to sacrifice\n"
"itself like that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 7161..8317
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/8
msgid ""
"I just can't see how a bunch of circuits and\n"
"switches could have a will of its own...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 8373..9780
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/9
msgid ""
"It's called The Ghost in the Machine, Snake... And it\n"
"exists.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/0
msgid ""
"Dr. Alan Turing is known as the father of computer\n"
"science.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/1
msgid ""
"It was he who formulated the basic theory of AI.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/2
msgid ""
"During the war, he worked for GC&CS.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/3
msgid ""
"The government's cryptology school... the one that\n"
"broke Enigma.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/4
msgid ""
"The very same.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/5
msgid ""
"Without him, they might never have been able to\n"
"decipher the Germans' code.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/6
msgid ""
"...But then they arrested him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/7
msgid ""
"Why? Weren't his some of the greatest\n"
"contributions to winning the war?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/8
msgid ""
"Homosexuality was a crime in Britain back then.\n"
"And he was gay.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/9
msgid ""
"I know exactly how crushed he was. I feel it's my\n"
"duty to further his AI research...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/10
msgid ""
"Like \"The Imitation Game,\" huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/11
msgid ""
"Ah, you know it, then?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/12
msgid ""
"The clue that inspired the Turing Test came from\n"
"a trifling little party game.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/13
msgid ""
"You exchange written notes with another person\n"
"behind a screen,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/14
msgid ""
"and try to guess their gender whether they're a\n"
"woman,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/15
msgid ""
"or a man pretending to be a woman....\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/16
msgid ""
"It's surprisingly difficult to tell the difference. Man\n"
"or woman, human or machine...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/17
msgid ""
"What do the differences even mean?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/18
msgid ""
"Dr. Turing was fascinated by the differences\n"
"between men and women.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/19
msgid ""
"Perhaps that's what led him to formulate his test.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 487..1421
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/0
msgid ""
"What if you hadn't used The Boss as the model for\n"
"the AI?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 1713..3078
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/2
msgid ""
"If the end goal is MAD, seems like there are more\n"
"suitable models out there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 3190..4569
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/3
msgid ""
"A military chief of staff, or a nuclear technician...\n"
"even the President.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 4709..5837
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/4
msgid ""
"Patriotism, leadership, good judgment...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 5962..7760
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/5
msgid ""
"Each of those qualities is essential when deciding\n"
"whether to launch a nuke, and she had them all.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 8066..8470
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/6
msgid ""
"Wouldn't the President, too?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 8484..9557
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/7
msgid ""
"It's not enough. She had the will for it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 9599..9835
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/8
msgid ""
"Will?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 9877..11270
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/9
msgid ""
"Let me explain, Snake. Peace Walker is a\n"
"stand-alone weapon.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 11368..12371
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/10
msgid ""
"It has to decide on its own whether or not to\n"
"launch a nuke.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 12455..13165
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/11
msgid ""
"It can't turn to anyone else for advice.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 13207..14781
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/12
msgid ""
"It can't do its job if it's not prepared to take sole\n"
"responsibility for the fate of the world.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 14879..15840
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/13
msgid ""
"I know of no other human being who could bear\n"
"that burden.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 15868..16091
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/14
msgid ""
"...That's it?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 16133..17818
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/15
msgid ""
"There were technical considerations, of course. To\n"
"begin with, the female brain\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 17902..18543
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/16
msgid ""
"is a more appropriate model for an AI.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 18543..19365
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/17
msgid ""
"Wait...the female brain?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/0
msgid ""
"So what's an 'expert system?'\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/1
msgid ""
"The AI housed within Peace Walker began\n"
"development as such a system.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/2
msgid ""
"An expert system is a type of proxy program\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/3
msgid ""
"by which a computer makes decisions as an expert\n"
"would.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/4
msgid ""
"The program \"MYCIN,\" for example,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/5
msgid ""
"is a system that decides which kinds of antibiotics\n"
"to prescribe.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/6
msgid ""
"The system asks the patient a series of questions\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/7
msgid ""
"to narrow down the range of appropriate drugs.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/8
msgid ""
"So you programmed Peace Walker to prescribe live\n"
"nuclear warheads instead of penicillin.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/9
msgid ""
"What I realized, however, was that a simple expert\n"
"system wasn't up to the task.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/10
msgid ""
"You need more than expertise to launch a nuke.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/11
msgid ""
"Indeed. Expertise is a necessary prerequisite but\n"
"insufficient on its own.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/12
msgid ""
"Deciding to launch a retaliatory strike requires\n"
"consideration of a wider range of factors.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/13
msgid ""
"In such a scenario, the entire global situation\n"
"becomes the criterion for making a decision.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/14
msgid ""
"Makes sense. You screw up the prescription, and\n"
"the whole world goes into anaphylactic shock.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/15
msgid ""
"A \"weak AI\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/16
msgid ""
"that has only a limited range of knowledge upon\n"
"which to base its decisions won't cut it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/17
msgid ""
"Therefore, I had the AI study The Boss' thought\n"
"patterns,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/18
msgid ""
"thus creating a true expert system - a \"strong AI.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/19
msgid ""
"You couldn't leave the world in the hands of\n"
"something\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/20
msgid ""
"with anything less than an absolute worldview.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/21
msgid ""
"I could have built a simple expert system in no\n"
"time at all.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/22
msgid ""
"Say, how would you like a system that decides\n"
"which guns you should equip\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/23
msgid ""
"according to the mission's parameters?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/24
msgid ""
"I'll pass. I'm not gonna leave my life up to\n"
"somebody else's judgment.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/222/0xde520/25
msgid ""
"Especially not a machine.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 473..1462
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/0
msgid ""
"The opposite direction... What does that mean?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 1490..3092
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/1
msgid ""
"More and more AI are becoming systems that\n"
"specialize in mass information processing\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 3176..4304
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/2
msgid ""
"- without human intelligence, thought, or emotion.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 4388..5349
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/3
msgid ""
"A machine that has no individualism or sense of\n"
"self,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 5461..7077
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/4
msgid ""
"but rather behaves as a collective, exhibiting the\n"
"qualities of a society.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 7091..7453
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/5
msgid ""
"Like a beehive?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 7509..9557
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/6
msgid ""
"Yes. It aggregates data collected by individuals and\n"
"determines how the collective will act\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 9613..10685
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/7
msgid ""
"just as honeybees travel between the hive and\n"
"flowers.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 10769..11939
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/8
msgid ""
"The key to achieving that will be networking AI\n"
"together.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 11995..13193
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/9
msgid ""
"I don't know how to say this, but... that kind of\n"
"gives me the creeps.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 13221..14586
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/10
msgid ""
"But if your goal is to control society, it's the better\n"
"model to use.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 14642..16133
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/11
msgid ""
"It lets you filter data - disseminate only what you\n"
"want disseminated.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0060_010_0
#. timeline 16202..17707
#: codec/1/223/0xdf350/12
msgid ""
"Of course, I myself have no interest in an AI\n"
"without a shred of life to it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 473..2452
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/0
msgid ""
"Earlier, you called the Mammal Pod a butterfly. Not\n"
"a pupa or a cocoon, but an imago.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 2507..3873
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/1
msgid ""
"Yes. The AI that came before the Mammal Pod\n"
"were works in progress.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 3928..4332
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/2
msgid ""
"Works in progress?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 4346..4931
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/3
msgid ""
"They were enough to keep the frame running.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 4931..6018
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/4
msgid ""
"But not enough to make decisions about nuclear\n"
"retaliation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 6060..6965
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/5
msgid ""
"They weren't quite complete. They were pupae.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 7035..8359
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/6
msgid ""
"Only when I added The Boss' data did the AI take\n"
"on its true form,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 8512..9376
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/7
msgid ""
"becoming a butterfly and taking flight.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 9404..10448
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/8
msgid ""
"And that's why the nose art on Peace Walker was\n"
"a butterfly...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 10476..11730
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/9
msgid ""
"I gave the Mammal AI the code name \"BS-Imago.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0070_000_0
#. timeline 11828..12705
#: codec/1/223/0xdf880/10
msgid ""
"\"BS\" is short for Boss.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 571..1267
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/0
msgid ""
"What did you mean by \"the Ghost in the Machine\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 1281..2633
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/1
msgid ""
"Oh, that... It's a term coined by the philosopher\n"
"Gilbert Ryle.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 2661..3232
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/2
msgid ""
"You've heard of Descartes, yes?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 3260..3817
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/3
msgid ""
"\"I think, therefore I am...\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 3845..5419
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/4
msgid ""
"That is the one. Descartes espoused the dualistic\n"
"theory of mind and body.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 5433..6715
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/5
msgid ""
"He believed that our thinking minds exist in a\n"
"separate dimension from our bodies,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 6743..7397
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/6
msgid ""
"which are governed by the laws of physics.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 7467..9041
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/7
msgid ""
"But if that were true, then couldn't you say that a\n"
"mechanical \"body\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 9125..10337
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/8
msgid ""
"inhabited by a ghost \"mind\" is a human being?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 10407..11340
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/9
msgid ""
"Ryle criticized Descartes on those grounds,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 11340..12469
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/10
msgid ""
"saying such a thing surely wouldn't be human.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 12469..12817
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/11
msgid ""
"Why'd you bring it up?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 12845..13848
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/12
msgid ""
"I wasn't thinking of Ryle in particular when I said it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 13904..15450
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/13
msgid ""
"I simply thought that if a person is composed of a\n"
"machine and a ghost,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 15575..16272
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/14
msgid ""
"perhaps the opposite is true as well.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 16342..18752
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/15
msgid ""
"Perhaps by placing a ghost inside a machine, we\n"
"could in effect give birth to a new person.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 18780..19462
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/16
msgid ""
"And that was your idea for the Boss AI?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 19490..20953
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/17
msgid ""
"The moment you ripped the memory board out, the\n"
"Mammal Pod ceased to function.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 21023..21441
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/18
msgid ""
"It should have been dead.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 21524..23252
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/19
msgid ""
"And yet Peace Walker righted itself, singing a song\n"
"of peace.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0080_000_0
#. timeline 23294..25161
#: codec/1/224/0xe0230/20
msgid ""
"I couldn't help but feel... that her soul had come to\n"
"inhabit Peace Walker.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/0
msgid ""
"Are you familiar with the film \"2001: A Space\n"
"Odyssey\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/1
msgid ""
"I've heard of it, but...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/2
msgid ""
"Of course not. I didn't expect you to be cultured\n"
"enough to appreciate such things.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/3
msgid ""
"Yeah, thanks. Anyway...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/4
msgid ""
"\"2001\" features an AI called HAL,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/5
msgid ""
"a highly advanced system that controls an\n"
"exploration spacecraft.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/6
msgid ""
"It can converse with people, and even play chess.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/7
msgid ""
"Huh. Now where have I heard that before...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/8
msgid ""
"The way HAL was portrayed was truly superb.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/10
msgid ""
"HAL is given secret orders that not even the\n"
"ship's captain knows about.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/11
msgid ""
"Naturally, he's not allowed to divulge them to the\n"
"crew. The stress of it causes HAL to crack.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/12
msgid ""
"Crack?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/13
msgid ""
"Go crazy. Though there are those who interpret it\n"
"differently.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/14
msgid ""
"One by one, HAL kills off the crew until the captain\n"
"finally shuts it down...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/15
msgid ""
"The film offers amazing insights into AI - their\n"
"growth, their utility, their faults - and their fear of\n"
"death.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/16
msgid ""
"You must have found it useful in your research,\n"
"then.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/17
msgid ""
"Must you always be so... utilitarian?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/18
msgid ""
"It doesn't matter whether or not it's useful. What\n"
"matters is that it inspired me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/19
msgid ""
"Then it was USEFUL.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/20
msgid ""
"Never mind. The portrayal of HAL wasn't the only\n"
"wonderful thing about the film.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/21
msgid ""
"It was full of hints about the future of human\n"
"evolution. Truly a film for the ages.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/0
msgid ""
"Strangelove, when did you and The Boss first\n"
"meet?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/1
msgid ""
"...Did she ever tell you about what she saw in\n"
"space?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/3
msgid ""
"I saw the same thing along with her.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/4
msgid ""
"The Soviets beat America into space with Sputnik,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/5
msgid ""
"and so America rushed to be first in manned\n"
"spaceflight.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/6
msgid ""
"NASA used her as their top-secret guinea pig,\n"
"launching her deep into the cold blackness of\n"
"space.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/7
msgid ""
"I took part in the project. As a scientist.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/8
msgid ""
"You were there with her...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/9
msgid ""
"Yes... For a brief time, we were one and the same,\n"
"she and I.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/10
msgid ""
"We sought each other out... Completed each other.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/11
msgid ""
"Did you know that inside every woman there's a\n"
"universe,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/12
msgid ""
"and that we are able to sense this in each other.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/13
msgid ""
"We connected because of our empathetic female\n"
"brains.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/14
msgid ""
"As time went on... I began to have doubts about\n"
"offering such a noble soul as sacrifice.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/15
msgid ""
"Why would they...? Why did she have to...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/16
msgid ""
"...The flight test was a narrow success, and she\n"
"miraculously made it back alive.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/17
msgid ""
"But her mind and body were horribly mangled, and\n"
"there was nothing I could do for her.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/18
msgid ""
"We were no longer one and the same.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/19
msgid ""
"She went away, and I, having nothing else to live\n"
"for, immersed myself in AI research.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/20
msgid ""
"Hoping that no one would ever have to make her\n"
"sacrifice again.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/21
msgid ""
"I never knew...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/22
msgid ""
"It's not really worth knowing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/23
msgid ""
"We were ships passing in the night, that's all.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/24
msgid ""
"Perhaps someday I'll tell you the long version, if\n"
"you're interested.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 445..1448
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/0
msgid ""
"That was quite a warm welcome you gave me at\n"
"the base in Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 1476..2465
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/1
msgid ""
"...Sorry about that. But I simply had to know.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 2493..2953
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/2
msgid ""
"The Boss' final act?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 2981..4778
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/3
msgid ""
"Yes. By inputting her thoughts and actions into the\n"
"AI, I was imbuing it with her mind.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 4848..5921
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/4
msgid ""
"The only thing I couldn't understand was her final\n"
"act.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 5935..6450
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/5
msgid ""
"Operation Snake Eater...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 6478..8874
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/6
msgid ""
"Official history says she betrayed her homeland\n"
"and defected to the enemy... and was killed by you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 8944..10644
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/7
msgid ""
"...But it didn't make sense. The Boss would be the\n"
"last person on earth to betray her country.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 10699..11326
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/8
msgid ""
"It was logically inconsistent.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 11368..11744
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/9
msgid ""
"...It was, wasn't it?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 11772..13096
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/10
msgid ""
"That internal inconsistency prevented the AI from\n"
"activating properly -\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 13151..13862
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/11
msgid ""
"just as HAL malfunctioned in the film.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 13904..14907
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/12
msgid ""
"I understood the reasoning. But I had to have\n"
"proof.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 15004..16495
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/13
msgid ""
"Proof of her final act. Her true intentions. One way\n"
"or another!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 16509..17233
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/14
msgid ""
"So you tried to squeeze it out of me, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0120_000_1
#. timeline 17247..19560
#: codec/1/225/0xe1a10/15
msgid ""
"As a matter of fact, I did. Your silence was the\n"
"very answer I was looking for.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 459..1156
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/0
msgid ""
"What did you think of Peace Walker's final act?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 1170..2089
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/1
msgid ""
"I recreated her thought patterns exactly.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 2159..2800
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/2
msgid ""
"It was exactly what she would have done.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 2883..4249
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/3
msgid ""
"The world's most empathetic mind weighed the\n"
"past, the future,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 4304..5544
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/4
msgid ""
"and the entire world... and decided not to retaliate.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 5670..6339
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/5
msgid ""
"Merely knowing that is enough for me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 6436..7801
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/6
msgid ""
"...So what you're saying is, we don't need\n"
"deterrence to have peace?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 7815..9278
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/7
msgid ""
"I didn't say that. What's important is that we wish\n"
"for peace.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 9320..10532
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/8
msgid ""
"MSF needs a way to protect itself from the might\n"
"of nations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 10588..11661
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/9
msgid ""
"Survival requires pragmatic thought and action.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 11758..12552
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/10
msgid ""
"But, you still must retain your ideals.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 12705..14224
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/11
msgid ""
"If the gap between reality and those ideals ever\n"
"leads you to lose them...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0140_000_1
#. timeline 14363..15088
#: codec/1/226/0xe2720/12
msgid ""
"I doubt MSF will survive.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 487..1407
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/0
msgid ""
"So you were with ARPA before you came here,\n"
"huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 1476..3037
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/1
msgid ""
"Yes. Back then it was really the only place I could\n"
"make a living from my AI research.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 3120..3413
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/2
msgid ""
"And before that?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 3441..4388
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/3
msgid ""
"I started out at NASA. That's where I met her.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 4416..4890
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/4
msgid ""
"When Boss went into space...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 4917..6339
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/5
msgid ""
"...Yes. It was that incident that turned me away\n"
"from aerospace engineering.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 6422..7397
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/6
msgid ""
"Space is entirely too hazardous a place for human\n"
"beings.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 7467..8373
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/7
msgid ""
"That was why I felt an immediate need to develop\n"
"AI.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 8442..10267
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/8
msgid ""
"As it turned out, rockets later became much safer,\n"
"and mankind reached the surface of the moon...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 10351..11466
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/9
msgid ""
"In any event, it was a hollow Cold War victory.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 11563..13096
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/10
msgid ""
"When you get down to it, a nuclear missile is just a\n"
"rocket with a nuclear warhead strapped to it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 13165..14698
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/11
msgid ""
"Thus, taking the initiative in the space race was\n"
"tantamount to a military show of force.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 14795..16021
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/12
msgid ""
"But the budgetary strain was too big for\n"
"Washington or Moscow to handle.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 16021..17916
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/13
msgid ""
"Yes, and then there was the Cuban Missile Crisis\n"
"and the Vietnam War. And then came Détente...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 17986..20020
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/14
msgid ""
"Having leapt ahead of the Soviet Union with its\n"
"moon landing, America shut down the Apollo\n"
"program in '72.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 20075..22068
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/15
msgid ""
"It was around then that ARPA was downsized and\n"
"renamed DARPA, the \"D\" standing for \"defense.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 22151..24144
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/16
msgid ""
"With few prospects for continuing my AI research,\n"
"Coldman's invitation was a godsend.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 24325..25370
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/17
msgid ""
"It was also a chance to have them collect data on\n"
"her.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 25397..25955
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/18
msgid ""
"The end result being this mess.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0160_000_1
#. timeline 25969..27557
#: codec/1/227/0xe3280/19
msgid ""
"But we did learn something valuable from her - the\n"
"nobility of peace.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/0
msgid ""
"Why'd you agree to come here - to Mother Base?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/1
msgid ""
"You intrigued me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/2
msgid ""
"Me? ...Hold on, you're not planning on modeling\n"
"your next AI after me...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/3
msgid ""
"Not a bad idea. But I have no intention of ever\n"
"again attempting to transplant\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/4
msgid ""
"human thought into machines.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/5
msgid ""
"...That's a relief.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/6
msgid ""
"You are the man who inherited The Boss's will.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/7
msgid ""
"You're gathering people around you even now,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/8
msgid ""
"shaping them, building a new organization. I'd like\n"
"to see how it turns out.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/9
msgid ""
"You're not planning to go back to AI research?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/10
msgid ""
"I never said such a thing. Of course my work will\n"
"continue...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/11
msgid ""
"Here?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/12
msgid ""
"In my eyes, the growth of MSF\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/13
msgid ""
"as an organization is analogous to the development\n"
"of the nervous system.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/14
msgid ""
"The way you become intertwined, stimulate each\n"
"other,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/15
msgid ""
"branch out in new directions... It's really quite\n"
"inspirational.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/16
msgid ""
"Interesting way to put it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/17
msgid ""
"Of course, I intend to repay you for your\n"
"hospitality.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/18
msgid ""
"The fruits of my research will be at your disposal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/227/0xe3aa0/19
msgid ""
"Why not assign me to the R&D team? I promise you\n"
"won't be disappointed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/0
msgid ""
"You know, that ID card I got from Huey wouldn't\n"
"let me into the lab.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/1
msgid ""
"Of course not. I deactivated it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/3
msgid ""
"As though I'd let him into my lab!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/4
msgid ""
"You don't seem to care for him much. Even though\n"
"you two are in the same field.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/5
msgid ""
"Oh, please. For starters, I can't stand that\n"
"wishy-washy attitude of his.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/6
msgid ""
"If he's got something to say to me, he should be a\n"
"man and come say it in person,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/7
msgid ""
"not write some furtive letter.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/8
msgid ""
"But if his card doesn't work, how's he supposed to...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/9
msgid ""
"And another thing! The way he always demeans\n"
"himself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/10
msgid ""
"Every other sentence begins with \"I could be\n"
"wrong, but...\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/11
msgid ""
"Why can't he just do what he does and be\n"
"confident about it?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/12
msgid ""
"Well, there was the thing about his dissertation\n"
"being plagiarized...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/13
msgid ""
"The real problem is, he doesn't have a whit of\n"
"independence in him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/14
msgid ""
"In Costa Rica, and even back at NASA he was\n"
"always following people around\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/15
msgid ""
"asking if there was some way he could help.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/16
msgid ""
"Why doesn't he stop his whining, take a stand, and\n"
"face up to me?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/17
msgid ""
"I think I know how he feels....\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/18
msgid ""
"And to top it all off, he seems to enjoy referring to\n"
"himself by that nickname I gave him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/19
msgid ""
"I simply don't get it. How can he be so submissive?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/20
msgid ""
"So Huey was a nickname you gave him...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/21
msgid ""
"That's right. I took it from the name of a drone in\n"
"the science fiction film \"Silent Running.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/22
msgid ""
"Drone?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/23
msgid ""
"It's a type of worker robot.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/24
msgid ""
"The way he follows people, just waiting for them to\n"
"boss him around, is so similar. I couldn't help myself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/25
msgid ""
"Oh.. It's an American film directed by Douglas\n"
"Trumbull,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/26
msgid ""
"the man who did the special effects for \"2001: A\n"
"Space Odyssey.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/27
msgid ""
"Imagine that. A scientist who likes science fiction...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/28
msgid ""
"And that's not all!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/29
msgid ""
"There's more?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/30
msgid ""
"He's a man!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/31
msgid ""
"...Hang on, I seem to remember you saying he\n"
"should be more of a man.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/32
msgid ""
"...Yes, well, he is an awfully good scientist.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/33
msgid ""
"Without his Reptile Pod, my Mammal Pod wouldn't\n"
"function.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/34
msgid ""
"Just as the cerebrum can't exist without the\n"
"cerebellum and the brain stem.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/35
msgid ""
"He did a fine job of designing it, I'll give him that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/36
msgid ""
"That sounded suspiciously like praise...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/37
msgid ""
"Hmph. It's merely an objective observation.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/38
msgid ""
"I like people who possess the will to move forward.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/39
msgid ""
"I have no time for those who refuse to take\n"
"control of their lives.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/228/0xe4140/40
msgid ""
"Until he does, my opinion remains the same.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 487..1407
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/0
msgid ""
"Huey's probably mentioned this, but just to be clear,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 1448..2507
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/1
msgid ""
"there's a limit to the parts we can produce here at\n"
"Mother Base.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 2549..4123
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/2
msgid ""
"Therefore, I've built ZEKE's AI using memory boards\n"
"you pulled from other AI weapons.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 4123..4388
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/3
msgid ""
"Will that work?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 4402..5726
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/4
msgid ""
"In the human brain, individual functions are spread\n"
"across multiple regions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 5767..7746
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/5
msgid ""
"The same is true of AI. Multiple parts sharing the\n"
"same function interlink to strengthen that function.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 7760..8874
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/6
msgid ""
"For example, the more sensor memory boards you\n"
"have,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 8888..9975
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/7
msgid ""
"the greater ZEKE's search-and-detect capabilities\n"
"will be.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 10031..11215
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/8
msgid ""
"Install more movement boards and you'll increase\n"
"its mobility.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 11215..12496
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/9
msgid ""
"Meaning the AI's capabilities change depending on\n"
"how much memory we give it?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_mis_dsl0010_000_0
#. timeline 12510..14113
#: codec/1/229/0xe5620/10
msgid ""
"Exactly. The more boards you install, the more\n"
"powerful a function will be.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 459..1239
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/0
msgid ""
"How's the ZEKE AI different from Peace Walker's?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 1239..2452
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/1
msgid ""
"ZEKE's AI isn't a replica of the human thought\n"
"process.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 2452..3622
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/2
msgid ""
"It isn't programmed to make decisions about\n"
"nuclear retaliation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 3775..5126
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/3
msgid ""
"On the other hand, it is capable of highly\n"
"independent action in combat\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 5126..5879
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/4
msgid ""
"when given orders from a pilot.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 5921..7718
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/5
msgid ""
"It can protect infantry, destroy the enemy, and, if\n"
"ordered...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 7760..8052
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/6
msgid ""
"Launch a nuke.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 8080..8902
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/7
msgid ""
"Let us hope it never comes to that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0090_000_0
#. timeline 8930..9529
#: codec/1/229/0xe5ac0/8
msgid ""
"My sentiments exactly.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/0
msgid ""
"That was some escape you made from\n"
"Strangelove's lab.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/1
msgid ""
"Security inside was not so tight.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/2
msgid ""
"The door to my room was locked from the outside,\n"
"of course.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/3
msgid ""
"But she took off the blindfold at bath time - so she\n"
"could wash my hair...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/4
msgid ""
"Pretty luxurious treatment for a prisoner.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/5
msgid ""
"Wasn't it? She wouldn't undo the handcuffs, but\n"
"she washed my body for me instead.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/6
msgid ""
"And with such gentle care...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/7
msgid ""
"Why'd you run away? Didn't she say you could go\n"
"home in a month?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/8
msgid ""
"If your escape attempt failed, you'd be in greater\n"
"danger than before.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/9
msgid ""
"I was supposed to be giving a presentation\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/10
msgid ""
"on the distribution of Costa Rican bird species at a\n"
"conference.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/11
msgid ""
"The date was approaching quickly.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/12
msgid ""
"So I pretended I had to use the toilet and made\n"
"my escape.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/13
msgid ""
"I found an ID card and searched everywhere for\n"
"my equipment and my tape...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/14
msgid ""
"But a soldier saw me. It was a miracle I managed\n"
"to get away.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/15
msgid ""
"There was no time to find the tape.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/16
msgid ""
"I don't care about the conference. I'm lucky\n"
"enough to still be in one piece.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/17
msgid ""
"You bounce back quick.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/18
msgid ""
"You don't?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/19
msgid ""
"....Not sure. I try not to dwell too much on the past,\n"
"but...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/20
msgid ""
"Then don't. There's no point. I'm so glad to be out\n"
"of there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/21
msgid ""
"I never felt safe, you know?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/22
msgid ""
"Tell me about it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/23
msgid ""
"Well... I think she's interested in women. And I think\n"
"she took a fancy to me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/24
msgid ""
"That's, uh.... huh.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/230/0xe6480/25
msgid ""
"Besides, it's much nicer here.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 459..1072
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/0
msgid ""
"Let's go over this one more time.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 1072..2020
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/1
msgid ""
"First, I need an ID card to get into the lab.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 2020..3385
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/2
msgid ""
"That is correct. From the outside it looks like any\n"
"other ruin.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 3427..4778
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/3
msgid ""
"But on the inside it is a state-of-the-art research\n"
"facility.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 4806..6185
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/4
msgid ""
"And your ID card got taken away from you by\n"
"some guy in an orange jacket.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 6255..7314
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/5
msgid ""
"Exactly. I heard a quetzal singing nearby.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 7453..8164
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/6
msgid ""
"It has not been that long since it happened.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 8568..10072
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/7
msgid ""
"It could be tricky if he's out on patrol, but if he's a\n"
"stationary sentry...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 10114..10741
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/8
msgid ""
"You don't think the quetzal's moved?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 10825..12441
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/9
msgid ""
"Its nest is probably nearby. I do not think it will go\n"
"away anytime soon.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 12483..13318
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/10
msgid ""
"Good. I'll get on looking for that soldier.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 13332..14572
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/11
msgid ""
"If you forget what it sounds like, I'll do the call for\n"
"you again.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 14642..15729
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/12
msgid ""
"Just give me a call anytime you'd like to hear it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0030_000_0
#. timeline 16049..16425
#: codec/1/231/0xe75f0/13
msgid ""
"I'll do that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 459..1866
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/0
msgid ""
"Let me get this straight. You were in Costa Rica\n"
"as a birdwatcher?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 1894..3413
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/1
msgid ""
"Yes, I was. Not for pleasure, though - I am a\n"
"researcher, after all.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 3496..4639
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/2
msgid ""
"I am studying the distribution of Latin American\n"
"bird species.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 4764..5614
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/3
msgid ""
"With today's compact cassette tape recorders,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 5656..6896
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/4
msgid ""
"even a woman like me can carry her recording\n"
"equipment by herself.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 7077..7843
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/5
msgid ""
"But it was a mistake to come alone.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 7913..9445
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/6
msgid ""
"Mmm. Even so, there sure are a lot of wild birds in\n"
"Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 9696..10685
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/7
msgid ""
"Aren't there? Over 800 different species,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 10741..11925
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/8
#, c-format
msgid ""
"said to be more than 10% of all living bird species\n"
"on Earth.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 12092..13235
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/9
msgid ""
"How many can you name, Mr. Ornithologist?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 13332..14349
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/10
msgid ""
"Hey, I was just trying not to scare you...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 14391..15325
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/11
msgid ""
"You should at least have a basic knowledge of\n"
"Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 15394..16648
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/12
msgid ""
"How about this: I will give you a thorough\n"
"education,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0090_000_0
#. timeline 35876..13513
#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/13
msgid ""
"Mr. First-Time Ornithologist.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/231/0xe7ae0/14
msgid ""
"Uh, OK. Start by telling me about the quetzal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/0
msgid ""
"Cécile, what's that machine you said you use to\n"
"make those recordings of yours?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/1
msgid ""
"A cassette... something or other.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/2
msgid ""
"A cassette recorder? Or a cassette densuke, as\n"
"they say in Japon.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/3
msgid ""
"Yeah, that. What is that thing, anyway?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/4
msgid ""
"A portable recording device released last year by a\n"
"Japanese company: Sony.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/5
msgid ""
"It uses compact cassettes, making it far lighter\n"
"than open reel machines.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/6
msgid ""
"It still weighs 5 kilograms, but the exercise won't\n"
"kill me!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/7
msgid ""
"Ha.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/8
msgid ""
"It's user-friendly, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/9
msgid ""
"All the buttons have markings on them,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/10
msgid ""
"allowing you to operate it without looking at it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/11
msgid ""
"Can you imagine missing the shot of a lifetime\n"
"simply because you'd blinked?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/12
msgid ""
"That would be devastating.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/13
msgid ""
"But where'd they come up with densuke? It sounds\n"
"like a Japanese name.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/14
msgid ""
"Allow me to field that one.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/15
#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/6
msgid ""
"Kaz?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/16
msgid ""
"Densuke's a nickname that comes from the name\n"
"of an old manga character.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/17
msgid ""
"Was he some recording nerd, too?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/18
msgid ""
"Don't gimme that! Recording atmospheric noises is\n"
"an exhilarating art!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/19
msgid ""
"There's nothing like capturing the real world in\n"
"action on tape!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/20
msgid ""
"It's just like taking pictures with a camera,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/21
msgid ""
"only with a microphone instead of a viewfinder.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/22
msgid ""
"Sure...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/23
msgid ""
"Listen to a tape with your eyes closed\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/24
msgid ""
"and the scene just bursts to life in your mind's eye.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/25
msgid ""
"Tell him, Cécile.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/26
msgid ""
"Absolutely. When I listen to the sounds of birds in\n"
"my apartment,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/27
msgid ""
"it's like I'm back in the forest where I recorded\n"
"them.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/28
msgid ""
"See, she's a Parisienne. She knows what's chic.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/29
msgid ""
"If you say so...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/30
msgid ""
"What do you like to record, Monsieur Miller?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/31
msgid ""
"Me? Steam locomotives, no question.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/32
msgid ""
"The roar of the engine, the throaty steam whistle...\n"
"More animal than machine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/33
msgid ""
"Mmh, don't get me started!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/34
msgid ""
"Steam locomotives are a dying breed in Japan.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/35
msgid ""
"I wouldn't mind going back for a bit and making\n"
"some new tapes while I still can.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/36
msgid ""
"...You're less civilized than I thought.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/37
msgid ""
"L-LESS civilized?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/38
msgid ""
"I detest those beasts. The noise frightens off all\n"
"the birds.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/39
msgid ""
"Then there's the smoke...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/40
msgid ""
"I much prefer the peace and quiet of the forest.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/41
msgid ""
"Cécile, wait! That... That came out wrong, I...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/232/0xe8030/42
msgid ""
"Sure it did.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/0
msgid ""
"You said you could do a monkey call.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/1
msgid ""
"Yes! Want to hear it?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/2
msgid ""
"Yeah, I won't be able to get it off my mind until I do.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/3
msgid ""
"Alright. Here it is, then.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/4
msgid ""
"...That's pretty good.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/5
msgid ""
"I can do others, too. Like a sheep, a pig...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/6
#: codec/1/238/0xee440/19
#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/17
msgid ""
"Yeah?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/7
msgid ""
"Wow. What about a pig?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/8
msgid ""
"That's uncanny!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/9
msgid ""
"Ha ha. I can do a rabbit as well.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/10
msgid ""
"A rabbit? Rabbits make noises?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/11
msgid ""
"Certainly. But they're very faint,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/12
msgid ""
"so perhaps only someone who has owned one\n"
"would recognize them.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/13
msgid ""
"I see. So what do they sound like?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/14
msgid ""
"Listen very carefully.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/16
msgid ""
"Seriously? Rabbits sound like that?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/17
msgid ""
"I assure you, they do. Listen again.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/18
msgid ""
"Never heard a rabbit do that before.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/19
msgid ""
"They do, I swear!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/0
msgid ""
"Costa Rica is the home to many hummingbirds as\n"
"well.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/1
msgid ""
"The people here call them colibri.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/2
msgid ""
"Colibri, huh...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/3
msgid ""
"Hummingbirds are the world's smallest birds.\n"
"Although they can vary from species to species,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/4
msgid ""
"most are around 10 cm in length, and the smallest\n"
"no more than five.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/5
msgid ""
"It's amazing to think that something so small can\n"
"still be a fully developed bird.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/6
msgid ""
"I'd think a bird that tiny would get mistaken for a\n"
"bug.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/7
msgid ""
"Actually they are often mistaken for sphinx moths.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/8
msgid ""
"The little darlings feed on flower nectar,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/9
msgid ""
"and their beaks are long and thin to help them\n"
"drink up the nectar.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/10
msgid ""
"They beat their wings far faster than any other\n"
"bird.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/11
msgid ""
"The smallest ones over 70 times a second! Can\n"
"you imagine?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/12
#: codec/1/265/0x109080/13
msgid ""
"What for?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/13
msgid ""
"They hover in midair while they suck their nectar.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/14
msgid ""
"They can even fly straight backwards.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/15
msgid ""
"Hovering... like a helicopter!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/16
msgid ""
"That's why Amanda and her unit called that\n"
"chopper colibri.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/17
msgid ""
"I think it is an insult to the birds to give their\n"
"names to weapons, don't you?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/233/0xe9b60/18
msgid ""
"Don't ask me. Ask the birds how they feel about it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/0
msgid ""
"Have you heard of the manakins?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/1
msgid ""
"Never.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/2
msgid ""
"Unbelievable! You came all the way to Costa Rica\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/3
msgid ""
"and you've never even heard of them!?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/4
msgid ""
"I didn't come here to look at...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/5
msgid ""
"Manakins are known for their beautiful courtship\n"
"dances.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/6
msgid ""
"The Orange-collared Manakin is said to live on the\n"
"Pacific side,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/7
msgid ""
"the White-bearded Manakin on the Caribbean side,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/8
msgid ""
"and the Long-tailed Manakin is in the central basin.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/9
msgid ""
"The Long-tailed Manakins are especially distinctive.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/10
msgid ""
"What's special about them?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/11
msgid ""
"First, each young male picks an older male to\n"
"teach him how to dance.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/12
msgid ""
"Then teachers and pupils all get in a group and\n"
"dance for the females.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/13
msgid ""
"However, only the teachers get paired off with\n"
"females.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/14
msgid ""
"The pupils practice their technique for seven years\n"
"before striking out on their own\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/15
msgid ""
"and finding their own pupils.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/16
msgid ""
"I guess it takes time to get good at anything,\n"
"whether it's dancing or soldiering.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/17
msgid ""
"Manakins always have plenty to eat.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/18
msgid ""
"Apparently that is why they have so much free\n"
"time to practice dancing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/234/0xea1f0/19
msgid ""
"Unlike us, obviously...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 445..1852
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/0
msgid ""
"Another well-known bird of the cloud forest is the\n"
"Three-wattled Bellbird.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 1894..2730
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/1
msgid ""
"Wattled? What the hell's a wattle?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 3092..3705
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/2
msgid ""
"It is just like your beard, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 3970..4931
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/4
msgid ""
"It's a piece of flesh that hangs down from its chin.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 4973..5795
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/5
msgid ""
"Kind of like whiskers, but not made of hair.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 5809..6534
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/6
msgid ""
"A hanging piece of flesh?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 6561..7370
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/7
msgid ""
"Oui, and it only grows on males.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 7383..8247
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/8
msgid ""
"Nothing more important to a man than his beard.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 8498..9348
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/9
msgid ""
"So these birds are in the cloud forest, too?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 9418..10281
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/10
msgid ""
"They're normally found in the lowland rain forests,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 10323..11661
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/11
msgid ""
"but they migrate into the highland cloud forests\n"
"during breeding season.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 11744..13068
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/12
msgid ""
"What the Three-wattled Bellbird's best known for,\n"
"though, is its loud call.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 13179..14851
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/13
msgid ""
"It makes these metallic BONG! and DING! sounds -\n"
"hence the name \"bellbird.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 14893..15534
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/14
msgid ""
"It hardly sounds like a bird at all.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 15575..16676
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/15
msgid ""
"Even an expert bird caller like me cannot do it\n"
"justice.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0130_000_0
#. timeline 16815..17749
#: codec/1/234/0xea890/16
msgid ""
"Doesn't sound like I'll be mistaking it for a quetzal.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 445..1351
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/0
msgid ""
"The Scarlet Macaw and the Great Green Macaw\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 1351..2229
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/1
msgid ""
"are also representative birds of Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 2368..3608
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/2
msgid ""
"Macaws are a type of parrot... enormous, stately\n"
"birds.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 3761..4931
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/3
msgid ""
"Macaw... I think I've heard that name somewhere\n"
"before.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 5168..6144
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/4
msgid ""
"But of course you have - you're an ornithologist,\n"
"no?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 6171..6492
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/5
msgid ""
"Stop it....\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 6673..8122
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/6
msgid ""
"So tell me, where do macaws live in Costa Rica\n"
"today?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 8192..8721
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/7
msgid ""
"Oh c'mon now...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 9139..9696
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/8
msgid ""
"I am only teasing you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 9752..10574
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/9
msgid ""
"Macaws live not in the cloud forests,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 10574..11772
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/10
msgid ""
"but in the rain forests on the Pacific side of Costa\n"
"Rica.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 11842..13207
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/11
msgid ""
"In the past, they were a common sight all across\n"
"the country,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 13249..14419
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/12
msgid ""
"but lately the population has decreased\n"
"dramatically.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 14517..16384
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/13
msgid ""
"One possible cause is the pesticides sprayed to\n"
"facilitate large-scale banana cultivation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 16467..17136
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/14
msgid ""
"Evicted from their own land, huh.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0150_000_0
#. timeline 17164..18543
#: codec/1/235/0xeb310/15
msgid ""
"Thankfully, conservation efforts have been gaining\n"
"some momentum lately.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/0
msgid ""
"Never heard the name \"Cosima\" before.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/1
msgid ""
"The again I don't know many people from France.\n"
"Is it a common name?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/2
msgid ""
"No. Not that common.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/3
msgid ""
"But Wagner's second wife was named Cosima\n"
"Francesca Gaetana Wagner.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 5739..5935
#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/4
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/6
msgid ""
"Huh.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/5
msgid ""
"You know, \"Kojima\" is a common last name in Japan.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/7
msgid ""
"It's just funny how, you know,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/8
msgid ""
"I'm part Japanese and Cécile's middle name is so\n"
"close to \"Kojima.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/9
msgid ""
"It feels like... destiny unfolding.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/11
msgid ""
"Oui oui! That's a beautiful name you have. Cécile\n"
"Cosima Caminades.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/12
msgid ""
"Wait a second...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/13
msgid ""
"Cécile Cosima Caminades... Cosima Caminades...\n"
"Hey, that’s close to...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/14
msgid ""
"Close to what?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/15
msgid ""
"Your name... It sounds almost like the sentence\n"
"“Kojima, kaminandesu” in Japanese.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/16
msgid ""
"And what does it mean, s’il vous plait?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/17
msgid ""
"Well, \"kami\" is the word for \"god\" in Japanese.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/18
msgid ""
"\"Nandesu...\" Well, it's hard to explain, but placed\n"
"after \"god\" it would turn the sentence into \"is God.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/19
msgid ""
"Okay. So?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/20
msgid ""
"\"Kojima is God\"... Cecile's name is a message!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/21
msgid ""
"I don’t believe it... Kojima is God... Kojima is God...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/22
msgid ""
"Umm, Kaz...?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 445..1253
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/0
msgid ""
"Did you live in Paris your whole life before coming\n"
"here?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 1434..2368
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/1
msgid ""
"Yes. It is my favorite city.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 2549..3566
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/2
msgid ""
"Paris is the world capital of art and culture.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 3664..5489
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/3
msgid ""
"It has the latest fashion, the best cuisine, and the\n"
"most elegant, refined people.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 5614..7147
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/4
msgid ""
"The beauty of the Champs-Élysées at night is\n"
"almost unearthly.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 7230..8554
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/5
msgid ""
"The name comes from Elysium, the name of\n"
"Paradise in Greek mythology.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 8721..9236
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/6
msgid ""
"Heaven, in other words.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 9654..10755
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/7
msgid ""
"Must be nice for some people. Not for me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 10769..11674
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/8
msgid ""
"Are you saying the cultured life does not appeal to\n"
"you?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 11688..13151
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/9
msgid ""
"I'm saying I never had a chance to lead one. Not\n"
"that it appealed to me anyway.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 13165..13583
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/10
msgid ""
"You prefer war?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 13597..15464
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/11
msgid ""
"I don't... Like war. Life outside heaven just suits me\n"
"better.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 15492..16077
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/12
msgid ""
"That is a hard way to live...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 16119..17902
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/13
msgid ""
"...But if you do ever come to France, I will show\n"
"you around Paris.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0040_000_0
#. timeline 18000..19253
#: codec/1/236/0xec6f0/14
msgid ""
"Then you will see what heaven on earth is really\n"
"like.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0050_000_0
#. timeline 459..1978
#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/0
msgid ""
"Heaven on earth, huh... The only image I have of\n"
"France is the Foreign Legion.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/1
msgid ""
"Th-that is how you view France?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/2
msgid ""
"What do the French think of the them?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/3
msgid ""
"It is a difficult question... We normally don't think\n"
"about it so much.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/4
msgid ""
"Critics claim it forces foreigners to take on the\n"
"most dangerous missions\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/5
msgid ""
"so French citizens won't get hurt.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/6
msgid ""
"You're right, that probably had something to do\n"
"with why it was created...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/7
msgid ""
"But I understand that along with service comes\n"
"benefits\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/8
msgid ""
"such as French citizenship and permanent\n"
"residency.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/9
msgid ""
"Those who join are all given an equal chance,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/10
msgid ""
"regardless of race, religion, education, social\n"
"status, or national origin.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/11
msgid ""
"So it can be a godsend for people from poor\n"
"countries.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/12
msgid ""
"A way for the have-nots to live a decent life...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/236/0xecc30/13
msgid ""
"I guess that's not so different from MSF.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 459..1630
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/0
msgid ""
"There's one other image I have of France: the\n"
"national anthem.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 1643..3260
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/1
msgid ""
"Ah, La Marseillaise... Not everyone is a fan, of\n"
"course.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 3622..5057
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/2
msgid ""
"The whole \"To arms, citizens. May an impure blood\n"
"water our furrows.\" thing, eh?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 5071..6283
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/3
msgid ""
"The song was composed right after the French\n"
"Revolution.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 6352..7188
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/4
msgid ""
"Fearing what the tide of the Revolution\n"
"represented,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 7202..7941
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/5
msgid ""
"the ruling classes in neighboring countries applied\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 7941..8791
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/6
msgid ""
"all kinds of pressure on the young government.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 8818..10253
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/7
msgid ""
"La Marseillaise became the anthem of the\n"
"volunteer armies that sought to protect\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 10267..11145
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/8
msgid ""
"constitutional rule against that pressure.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 11159..11911
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/9
msgid ""
"And they couldn't do that without armed force.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 11939..13235
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/10
msgid ""
"Oui. I agree, some parts are a little belligerent,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 13291..14489
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/11
msgid ""
"but we must not forget that if it were not for\n"
"them,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0060_000_0
#. timeline 14558..15589
#: codec/1/237/0xed150/12
msgid ""
"France would not be the democracy it is today.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 445..1239
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/0
msgid ""
"Have you ever seen \"The Umbrellas of Cherbourg\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 1309..2145
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/1
msgid ""
"A movie? No, never seen it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 2173..3120
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/2
msgid ""
"No? It came out 10 years ago.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 3650..4890
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/3
msgid ""
"Catherine Deneuve, she is so beautiful in it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 5015..6603
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/4
msgid ""
"And the music, the costumes, the colors... Oh!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 6979..8052
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/5
msgid ""
"It takes place in the naval port of Cherbourg.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 8094..8693
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/6
msgid ""
"That was a beachhead in Normandy.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 8735..10100
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/7
msgid ""
"It is set back when young men were conscripted to\n"
"fight in the Algerian War.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 10407..11939
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/8
msgid ""
"The French government called the conflict a\n"
"\"public order operation in northern Africa.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 11995..12552
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/9
msgid ""
"I was still a little girl then,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 12650..14182
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/10
msgid ""
"but I can clearly remember one of my friends' older\n"
"brothers going off to fight.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 14196..15185
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/11
msgid ""
"Yeah, national service is required in France.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 15213..16021
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/12
msgid ""
"The war splits up two young lovers.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 16175..18083
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/13
msgid ""
"Director Jacque Demy's lyrics and Michel Legrand's\n"
"music tore at my heart.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 18250..19435
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/14
msgid ""
"I will never forget its wonderful melodies. Aaahh...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 19518..19894
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/15
msgid ""
"You okay?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 20006..22137
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/16
msgid ""
"It changes lives - changes fates. War is not a good\n"
"thing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0220_000_0
#. timeline 22277..23614
#: codec/1/237/0xed620/17
msgid ""
"For some reason it strikes a chord to hear that\n"
"coming from someone like you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 459..1212
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/0
msgid ""
"Speaking of the Algerian War of Independence,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 1239..1839
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/1
msgid ""
"you ever hear of \"The Day of the Jackal\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 2103..3078
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/2
msgid ""
"You mean the novel that was made into a movie\n"
"last year?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 3120..4207
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/3
msgid ""
"The OAS, a militant French underground group,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 4221..5907
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/4
msgid ""
"plots to assassinate De Gaulle, hiring a hitman\n"
"known as the Jackal.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 5962..7509
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/5
msgid ""
"Readers know that de Gaulle was not killed, but it\n"
"is still so exciting.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 7551..8442
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/6
msgid ""
"If someone was going to try to eliminate me,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 8498..9334
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/7
msgid ""
"I would hope they'd be as thorough as the Jackal.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 9404..10685
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/8
msgid ""
"To know everything about me without me\n"
"suspecting a thing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0230_000_0
#. timeline 10727..11006
#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/9
msgid ""
"Oh, Yeah?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/10
msgid ""
"I wonder if my birds feel the same way.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/237/0xedc40/11
msgid ""
"I wonder.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 473..2215
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/0
msgid ""
"France conducted its first successful nuclear test\n"
"in the Algerian Sahara in 1960.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 2340..3246
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/1
msgid ""
"A lot of French scientists took part in the\n"
"Manhattan Project.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 3343..4346
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/2
msgid ""
"They defected to America to escape wartime\n"
"occupation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 4416..5126
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/3
msgid ""
"Correct. And once the war was over,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 5154..6394
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/4
msgid ""
"they returned to France and continued their own\n"
"atomic research.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 6408..8317
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/5
msgid ""
"President de Gaulle did not want to have to rely\n"
"on an American nuclear umbrella for protection.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 8359..9404
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/6
msgid ""
"Thus making France the world's fourth nuclear\n"
"power.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 9431..10699
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/7
msgid ""
"Some say the test's success pacified the Algerian\n"
"rebels.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 10769..11577
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/8
msgid ""
"The civil war was undoubtedly held in check.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ec8dda0 voice v_bri_ccl0240_000_0
#. timeline 11633..13054
#: codec/1/238/0xee040/9
msgid ""
"But never have I equated nuclear weapons with\n"
"peace.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/0
msgid ""
"France has produced many philosophers over the\n"
"years.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/1
msgid ""
"Descartes, Bataille, Sartre, Baudrillard...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/2
msgid ""
"I'm familiar with Sartre myself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/3
msgid ""
"He called Che Guevara the most complete man of\n"
"the century, didn't he?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/4
msgid ""
"Smart guy.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/5
msgid ""
"He does tend to sympathize with the left. What\n"
"else do you know about him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/6
msgid ""
"...That's it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/7
msgid ""
"You know nothing else?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/8
msgid ""
"...Nope.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/9
msgid ""
"Ooh la la. The man is one of the giants of\n"
"existentialism, you know.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/10
msgid ""
"Exitentialism? I've been meaning to look into that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/11
msgid ""
"Nothing more dangerous than sneaking in without\n"
"first securing an exit...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/12
msgid ""
"No, existentialism. Sometimes I wonder if my\n"
"English is not better than yours.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/13
msgid ""
"Sorry, I'm just... not into philosophy.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/14
msgid ""
"Is that so? I would imagine it might really enrich\n"
"your life.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/15
msgid ""
"I'd rather take action now than spend time thinking\n"
"about\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/16
msgid ""
"what we are or how we're supposed to live.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/17
msgid ""
"I guess you could say I live my philosophy.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/18
msgid ""
"Interesting. That sounds like something Sartre\n"
"would say.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/20
msgid ""
"He says we're born with no defined nature,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/21
msgid ""
"and that we're free to make our \"self\" what we wish.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/22
msgid ""
"Free? So he was one of those devil-may-care kind\n"
"of guys, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/23
msgid ""
"No, actually he meant that because we are free to\n"
"create our own life,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/24
msgid ""
"we must take full responsibility for our actions.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/25
msgid ""
"\"Man is condemned to be free,\" is how he put it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/26
msgid ""
"Condemned to be free...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/27
msgid ""
"But then others will take it upon themselves to\n"
"define who you are.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/28
msgid ""
"I've been feeling that way lately.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/29
msgid ""
"I keep telling people to call me \"Snake,\" but nobody\n"
"seems to listen.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/30
msgid ""
"Sartre also says, \"Hell is other people.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/238/0xee440/31
msgid ""
"Hell... Well we are outside of Heaven.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/0
msgid ""
"Tell me, Snake, do you ever put sweets in your\n"
"rations?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/1
msgid ""
"Never thought about it before. Why?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/2
msgid ""
"I simply love them! French sweets are très délicieux.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/3
msgid ""
"Everyone knows crêpes, but there are also\n"
"profiteroles,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/4
msgid ""
"éclairs, madeleines, financiers...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/5
msgid ""
"Then there's Tarte Tatins, and you can't forget\n"
"savarins.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/6
msgid ""
"Oh, and mille-feuilles, crêpes, blancmanges...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/7
msgid ""
"You already mentioned crêpes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/8
msgid ""
"Soufflés, croquembouches, canelés, floretins, kouign\n"
"amanns, Peach Melbas...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/9
msgid ""
"Finished?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/10
msgid ""
"...And macarons! I love those the most.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/11
msgid ""
"Macarons parisiens are the best.They're so cute\n"
"and colorful,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/12
msgid ""
"and they contain meringue, so they melt right in\n"
"your mouth.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/13
msgid ""
"Wow. I'd no idea macaroons were that popular in\n"
"France, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/14
msgid ""
"What do you mean \"in France, too\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/15
msgid ""
"Macaroons are those coconut-flavored cookies,\n"
"right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/16
msgid ""
"Excuse you! Macarons contains almond powder, not\n"
"coconuts!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/17
msgid ""
"Don't they have peanuts in them? I've had them in\n"
"Japan a few times.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/18
msgid ""
"I thought they were called \"makorons.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/19
msgid ""
"Makarons? Some cheap imitation, I am sure.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/20
msgid ""
"French macarons have a long and distinguished\n"
"history.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/21
msgid ""
"They date back to the 16th century, when\n"
"Catherine de' Medici of Florence\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/22
msgid ""
"married into the French royal family.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/23
msgid ""
"The story goes that her pâtissiers shared the\n"
"recipe after they arrived.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/24
msgid ""
"That's a history of over 500 years.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/25
msgid ""
"So... they're originally from Italy, then.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/26
msgid ""
"Well...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/27
msgid ""
"Don't macaroons come from Italy, too?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/28
msgid ""
"Look, I do not really think...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/29
msgid ""
"Keep in mind \"macaron\" is almost identical to\n"
"\"macaroni.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/30
msgid ""
"Well, that settles it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/31
msgid ""
"...I cannot believe this. To associate macarons with\n"
"macaroni!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/32
msgid ""
"You, Monsieur Miller, are an insensible oaf!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/239/0xef830/33
msgid ""
"Hey, hey, why am I the bad guy? Come on, Cécile,\n"
"wait! Cécile!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/0
msgid ""
"Hello! Snake, mon chéri.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/1
msgid ""
"You been drinking, Cécile?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/2
msgid ""
"Can't you please do something about this pest?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/3
msgid ""
"Who?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/4
msgid ""
"Monsieur Miller.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/5
msgid ""
"What's he done now...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/6
msgid ""
"Wine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/7
msgid ""
"Wine?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/8
msgid ""
"He said he thought the soldiers might tire of\n"
"having beer all the time,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/9
msgid ""
"so he's brought in some wine instead. And then he\n"
"gave me a bunch.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/10
msgid ""
"That was... nice of him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/11
msgid ""
"But the past two years have been bad for French\n"
"wine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/12
msgid ""
"Perhaps it is the bad weather we have had, but\n"
"whatever the case,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/13
msgid ""
"I told him the last thing you want to be drinking\n"
"right now is French wine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/14
msgid ""
"California and Chile have good wine, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/15
msgid ""
"But then he goes and stocks the pantry with\n"
"nothing but French wine from '72.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/16
msgid ""
"The stuff is a disaster.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/17
msgid ""
"Then he says, \"Come on, Cécile, have a taste of\n"
"the old country.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/18
msgid ""
"I had a terrible feeling about it, so I decided to just\n"
"taste it at first.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/19
msgid ""
"And then again, and then a few more times.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/20
msgid ""
"Took one for the team, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/21
msgid ""
"But when you do a tasting, don't you usually spit\n"
"the wine out?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/22
msgid ""
"But bottle after bottle, nothing but garbage,\n"
"absolute garbage.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/23
msgid ""
"Not one half-decent bottle in the whole lot! \"Taste\n"
"of the old country\" he says...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/24
msgid ""
"Sorry to hear that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/25
msgid ""
"I cannot believe this! What will we do with all this\n"
"wine!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/26
msgid ""
"The guys aren't too picky when it comes to taste.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/27
msgid ""
"You sound just like Monsieur Miller.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/29
msgid ""
"When I complained, he simply said, \"As long as it\n"
"gets the job done.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/30
msgid ""
"You people are such culinary savages!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/31
msgid ""
"Allez tous vous faire voir ! ...Aaaah, somebody take\n"
"me back to Paris! Please!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/32
msgid ""
"...I think you've had a little too much, Cécile.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 459..2020
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/0
msgid ""
"Doc, I'm starting to sense your feelings about\n"
"nukes are a little different from your colleagues.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 2340..3009
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/2
msgid ""
"Your little chat with Coldman back there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 3023..4472
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/3
msgid ""
"I...told you my father worked on the Manhattan\n"
"Project, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 4625..5015
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/4
msgid ""
"You're familiar with it?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 5085..6213
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/5
msgid ""
"The basics, yeah. It was the project that kicked off\n"
"the nuclear age.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 6227..7300
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/6
msgid ""
"That's right. Some of the finest minds of the 20th\n"
"century,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 7300..8317
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/7
msgid ""
"including multiple Nobel Prize winners, worked on it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 8359..9808
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/8
msgid ""
"They spent over two billion dollars - and that's in\n"
"1940's money.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 9822..11605
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/9
msgid ""
"It culminated in the successful nuclear test at\n"
"Alamogordo on July 16, 1945.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 11605..12566
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/10
msgid ""
"And the first use in combat a few weeks later.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 12873..13082
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/11
msgid ""
"Doc?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 13096..13444
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/12
msgid ""
"...I can't walk.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 13597..15074
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/13
msgid ""
"My spine isn't shaped like everybody else's. I can't\n"
"move my lower body.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 15088..16063
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/14
msgid ""
"So I've never taken a single step, not since I was\n"
"born.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 16077..16983
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/15
msgid ""
"What's that got to do with your dad being in the\n"
"Manhattan Project?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 16983..18543
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/16
msgid ""
"As a result of his research, my father was exposed\n"
"to high doses of radiation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 18640..19658
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/17
msgid ""
"It can't be a coincidence that my chromosomes are\n"
"messed up.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 19964..20243
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/18
msgid ""
"That's...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 20271..21524
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/19
msgid ""
"That's why I didn't want for these nukes to be\n"
"another sword of Damocles.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 21538..22764
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/20
msgid ""
"I wanted to give them a real purpose: to be a\n"
"deterrent against war.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 22778..22987
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/21
msgid ""
"Doc...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 23001..24520
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/22
msgid ""
"And Coldman... We have to stop him. Whatever it\n"
"takes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 445..1546
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/0
msgid ""
"It wasn't so long ago the world stood on the brink\n"
"of nuclear war.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 1546..2187
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/1
msgid ""
"Just over on the other side of the Caribbean.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 2201..3873
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/2
msgid ""
"I was 17 at the time. I'd skipped a few grades and\n"
"was a sophomore at MIT.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 4026..5126
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/3
msgid ""
"I remember feeling kind of apathetic about the\n"
"news that came in every day.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 5182..6617
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/4
msgid ""
"It seemed clear to me that as long as they had a\n"
"grasp of the concept of nuclear deterrence,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 6617..7119
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/5
msgid ""
"there was nothing to fear.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 7272..8400
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/6
msgid ""
"Either that, or they were fanning that fear on\n"
"purpose.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 8400..9947
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/7
msgid ""
"As a way to secure a bigger defense budget...?\n"
"Heh, I can see that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 9961..10727
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/8
msgid ""
"But if that was their plan, it kind of backfired.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 10741..11856
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/9
msgid ""
"Because it ushered in the era of Détente between\n"
"East and West.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 11856..12678
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/10
msgid ""
"Coldman's really going to do it this time.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 12747..13346
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/11
msgid ""
"Once the nuclear genie is out of the bottle,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 13346..14182
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/12
msgid ""
"the yoke of deterrence is going to be meaningless.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 14196..15116
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/13
msgid ""
"People will die. Cities will burn.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0020_000_0
#. timeline 15116..16161
#: codec/1/242/0xf26a0/14
msgid ""
"We have to stop him now, before it's too late to\n"
"turn back.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/0
msgid ""
"But you know... there's something I've never been\n"
"able to figure out.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/1
msgid ""
"Is the Cold War really a war, or is it really peace...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/2
msgid ""
"Doc, what are you...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/3
msgid ""
"People called it a \"cold war,\" but I disagreed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/4
msgid ""
"Sure, nuclear stockpiles are increasing, threats are\n"
"multiplying,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/5
msgid ""
"the U.S. and the Soviet Union have enough power\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/6
msgid ""
"to destroy the human race a hundred times over.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/7
msgid ""
"But nobody's actually being killed. Small-scale\n"
"conflicts and proxy wars, maybe...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/8
msgid ""
"But nuclear deterrence has averted another world\n"
"war.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/9
msgid ""
"The world's far more peaceful today than it was\n"
"before.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/10
msgid ""
"And the breakthroughs we've made in space\n"
"exploration\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/11
msgid ""
"thanks to Cold War competition - fantastic, don't\n"
"you think?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/12
msgid ""
"No... We didn't need to rush into space like that...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/13
msgid ""
"Going into space may have been mankind's dream,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/14
msgid ""
"but good people were sacrificed in the scramble.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/15
msgid ""
"...Maybe so. NASA's definitely got some skeletons in\n"
"its closet...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/16
msgid ""
"Same goes for the nuclear arms race.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/17
msgid ""
"Atomic testing has killed civilians and exposed\n"
"thousands to radiation.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/18
msgid ""
"Believe me, I know...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/19
msgid ""
"And now this... What peace was I trying to protect,\n"
"anyway?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/20
msgid ""
"The more I think about it, the less I understand.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 445..1421
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/0
msgid ""
"Nuclear deterrence means preventing the use of\n"
"nuclear weapons\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 1421..2661
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/1
msgid ""
"in conflicts between states. But what about other\n"
"situations?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 2953..3761
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/3
msgid ""
"Terrorism has been on the rise in recent years,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 3761..4736
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/4
msgid ""
"from separatist movements to far-left extremists.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 4736..6018
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/5
msgid ""
"What would happen if nuclear weapons fell into\n"
"terrorist hands?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 6018..7091
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/6
msgid ""
"Without a state - that is, without territory of their\n"
"own\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 7091..8080
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/7
msgid ""
"- the chances of having nukes used against them\n"
"are slim.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 8122..8958
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/8
msgid ""
"They have no reason to fear a nuclear strike.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 9000..10476
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/9
msgid ""
"Conversely, they have no reason to hesitate to use\n"
"nukes against their adversaries.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 10476..11633
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/10
msgid ""
"You've got a point. All the ICBMs and strategic\n"
"bombers in the world\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 11633..12260
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/11
msgid ""
"amount to nothing against a terrorist group.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 12260..13318
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/12
msgid ""
"Right! Of course, this is all still hypothetical.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 13360..13959
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/13
msgid ""
"Countries keep their nukes under tight watch\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 13959..15032
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/14
msgid ""
"- there's no immediate danger of terrorists getting\n"
"their hands on them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 15032..16021
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/15
msgid ""
"But the day may come when the proposition of\n"
"nuclear terrorism\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 16021..16885
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/16
msgid ""
"makes nuclear deterrence theory a dead letter.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 16885..18125
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/17
msgid ""
"Nuclear terrorism... Interesting.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 431..2340
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/0
msgid ""
"The aim of the Peace Walker Project is to achieve\n"
"robust nuclear deterrence across Central America\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 2368..3538
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/1
msgid ""
"by deploying a new nuclear weapon system along\n"
"the Caribbean coast.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 3566..4430
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/2
msgid ""
"Peace Walker is also the name of the system itself.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 4639..6213
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/3
msgid ""
"A nuclear weapon named \"Peace\"... I can just see\n"
"the look on Kaz's face.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 6241..7300
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/4
msgid ""
"So why exactly does this new system need legs in\n"
"the first place?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 7300..7704
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/5
msgid ""
"Because it's a \"Walker.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 7704..8094
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/6
msgid ""
"An unmanned weapon\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 8094..9613
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/7
msgid ""
"moving under its own power and capable of\n"
"launching a deterrent strike from anywhere...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 9738..10671
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/8
msgid ""
"That's the whole idea behind Peace Walker.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 459..1476
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/0
msgid ""
"The reason Peace Walker is a mobile nuclear\n"
"weapons system\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 1476..2452
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/1
msgid ""
"is to maximize its potential as a nuclear deterrent.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 2730..3873
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/3
msgid ""
"If need be, Peace Walker can stay constantly on\n"
"the move\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 3873..4764
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/4
msgid ""
"so that the adversary can't pinpoint its position...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 4834..5684
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/5
msgid ""
"That allows it to avoid preemptive enemy strikes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 5684..6645
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/6
msgid ""
"So you're saying it keeps the retaliation card in\n"
"play.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 6645..7397
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/7
msgid ""
"Coldman likes to brag about it in this way...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 7397..8219
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/8
msgid ""
"Like a land-based version of an SSBN.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 8233..9013
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/9
msgid ""
"And there's another reason for them to be mobile.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 9097..10184
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/10
msgid ""
"Peace Walker also has a self-destruct function.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 459..2145
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/0
msgid ""
"The biggest nuclear warhead ever actually\n"
"detonated was the Soviet RDS-220,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 2173..2828
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/1
msgid ""
"nicknamed \"Tsar Bomba.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 2828..3914
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/2
msgid ""
"It had an estimated yield of 57 megatons\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 3942..5363
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/3
msgid ""
"- ten times as much power as all the explosives\n"
"used throughout World War II.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 5391..6924
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/4
msgid ""
"The test took place on October 30, 1961, above\n"
"Novaya Zemlya.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 6979..8331
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/5
msgid ""
"The explosion is believed to have created a fireball\n"
"over two miles in diameter.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 8359..9431
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/6
msgid ""
"Can you believe that? Like a miniature sun.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 9473..10992
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/7
msgid ""
"The explosion was seen as far off as Finland - 600\n"
"miles away\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 11006..11842
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/8
msgid ""
"- and some people even reported windows\n"
"shattering.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 11870..12803
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/9
msgid ""
"The shockwave traveled three times around the\n"
"earth.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 12803..13221
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/10
msgid ""
"Three times?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 13221..14238
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/11
msgid ""
"Peace Walker is armed with a massive hydrogen\n"
"bomb\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 14238..14976
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/12
msgid ""
"even more destructive than Tsar Bomba.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 14976..15868
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/13
msgid ""
"It can sneak into enemy territory, lie low,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 15882..17428
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/14
msgid ""
"and - in the event of an enemy nuclear strike -\n"
"detonate itself in retaliation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 17526..18306
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/15
msgid ""
"And the locomotion system that lets it do that...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 18306..18780
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/16
msgid ""
"...My research...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 18780..20006
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/17
msgid ""
"...Snake, those legs were supposed to make my\n"
"dream come true.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 20006..21413
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/18
msgid ""
"Now they're about to jump the fence of nuclear\n"
"deterrence. You have to stop them!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 21413..22736
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/19
msgid ""
"I'll apply all my energy into developing weapons and\n"
"equipment to help you do it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 22736..23224
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/20
msgid ""
"Sounds like a deal.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 445..1490
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/0
msgid ""
"Peace Walker is fitted with several close-range\n"
"weapons.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 1504..2758
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/1
msgid ""
"We'd also planned for it to be able to enter enemy\n"
"territory and self-detonate.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 2814..3761
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/2
msgid ""
"Wonderful. What exactly are we dealing with here?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 3803..5154
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/3
msgid ""
"Well, the flamethrowers, for one thing - One in the\n"
"front, and one in the rear.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 5210..6952
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/4
msgid ""
"Then there are the S-mines. They're like cluster\n"
"bombs. It scatters them from its leg hatches.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 6979..7787
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/5
msgid ""
"If you see those open, you'd better clear out\n"
"quickly.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 7815..9278
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/6
msgid ""
"And finally, the rockets. These can travel quite a\n"
"distance, so stay sharp.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 9306..10323
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/7
msgid ""
"On the other hand, it can't fire them from too\n"
"close...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 10379..11131
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/8
msgid ""
"but then again there are those flamethrowers.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 11173..12343
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/9
msgid ""
"It can also use its legs as weapons against any\n"
"infantry on the ground.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 12357..12538
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/10
msgid ""
"Ouch.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 12552..13681
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/11
msgid ""
"But remember, Peace Walker technically isn't\n"
"complete.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 13736..15046
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/12
msgid ""
"With just the Reptile Pod, it can only perform\n"
"relatively simple maneuvers.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 15116..15715
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/13
msgid ""
"They've got certain quirks too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 15770..16370
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/14
msgid ""
"What's more, look carefully\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 16370..17401
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/15
msgid ""
"and you should be able to predict which attack is\n"
"coming next.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/0
msgid ""
"Snake! You have to stop Peace Walker from\n"
"launching that nuke!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/1
msgid ""
"Calm down. What do I need to do?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/2
msgid ""
"To tell you the truth, I don't really know...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/3
msgid ""
"The Mammal Pod has probably enhanced both its\n"
"thought patterns and mobility.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/4
msgid ""
"The S-mines, rockets, flamethrowers - they're all\n"
"the same, but\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/5
msgid ""
"I don't know what else to say...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/6
msgid ""
"You'll just have to stay sharp and watch for how it\n"
"behaves before each of the attacks.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/7
msgid ""
"I'll give it a shot. There's no time for anything else.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/8
msgid ""
"Sorry I can't be more helpful. You can do it, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 445..1504
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/0
msgid ""
"OK, but why does Peace Walker need to walk on\n"
"two legs?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 1560..2117
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/1
msgid ""
"I'd think treads would be good enough.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 2131..2633
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/2
msgid ""
"You'd be wrong.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 2661..3845
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/3
msgid ""
"As you know, the terrain in Central America is\n"
"rugged and complex.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 3873..4764
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/4
msgid ""
"Especially along the Caribbean coast of Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 4778..5753
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/5
msgid ""
"You've got jungles, swamps, mountains...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 5767..7147
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/6
msgid ""
"And the only way to get across all that terrain, no\n"
"matter how rugged, is on legs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 7216..8205
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/7
msgid ""
"But wouldn't it be tough to cross a swamp even on\n"
"legs?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 8233..8888
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/8
msgid ""
"It wasn't easy, that's for sure.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 8930..9668
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/9
msgid ""
"The reason we picked Costa Rica as a proving\n"
"ground\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 9668..10644
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/10
msgid ""
"is because we can test it on every type of terrain.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 459..2061
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/0
msgid ""
"This \"Peace Walker Project\" the CIA's talking about\n"
"- you believed in it, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 2089..3678
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/1
msgid ""
"Yeah. I believed... Actually, maybe I just wanted to\n"
"believe.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 4026..5614
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/3
msgid ""
"Here's how Coldman explained it. Peace Walker's a\n"
"weapon for peace,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 5656..6548
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/4
msgid ""
"one to ensure true nuclear deterrence.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 6589..7606
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/5
msgid ""
"It'd be the anchor to bring stability to Central\n"
"America...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 7620..9195
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/6
msgid ""
"He told me, \"The nuclear weapons system you've\n"
"built will never be used.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 9209..10323
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/7
msgid ""
"It will forever stand vigil as an icon of peace.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 10337..11647
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/8
msgid ""
"And to achieve that, he needed my bipedal\n"
"locomotion technology...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 11772..12399
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/9
msgid ""
"To be honest, I was flattered.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 12413..12733
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/10
msgid ""
"Flattered?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 12747..13137
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/11
msgid ""
"Wouldn't you be?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 13165..14363
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/12
msgid ""
"My colleagues in the scientific community have\n"
"never taken me seriously.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 14391..15868
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/13
msgid ""
"They told me bipedal locomotion was a pipe dream,\n"
"that it'd never amount to anything.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 15882..16815
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/14
msgid ""
"It was the first time anybody recognized my work...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 16885..17944
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/15
msgid ""
"How could I not be happy? And besides...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 17944..18724
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/16
msgid ""
"It was my chance to surpass my father.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 18836..20131
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/17
msgid ""
"To create nukes for peace... Or so I thought,\n"
"anyway.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 20131..20828
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/18
msgid ""
"But Coldman's really going through with it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 20828..21775
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/19
msgid ""
"Yeah. Makes perfect sense, really.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 21873..23684
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/20
msgid ""
"No one would give the project any notice unless\n"
"they could prove that an unmanned system is\n"
"capable of launching a nuke.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 445..1100
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/0
msgid ""
"Why is Coldman gonna launch a nuke?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 1100..2173
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/1
msgid ""
"If all he wants to do is prove the AI retaliation\n"
"system works,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 2187..2939
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/2
msgid ""
"he doesn't need to put a live warhead on it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 2939..4277
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/3
msgid ""
"I agree. He could demonstrate the system by\n"
"launching the missile alone\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 4277..5349
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/4
msgid ""
"- without a warhead. I asked him the same thing at\n"
"first.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 5363..6213
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/5
msgid ""
"He said there was no point in using a dummy\n"
"missile...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 6283..7592
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/6
msgid ""
"That it'd take an actual nuclear launch to deter\n"
"potential enemies.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 7592..8860
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/7
msgid ""
"Launching the real deal gives him a leg up in\n"
"negotiations with Langley.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 8902..9445
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/8
msgid ""
"That's what he's really after.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/0
msgid ""
"How'd you get your hands on Granin's research?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/1
msgid ""
"That was also Coldman. He used his Agency\n"
"contacts to get a hold of it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/2
msgid ""
"Giving you stolen information then using it to\n"
"blackmail you... Damn.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/3
msgid ""
"I knew it was Granin's work the minute I saw it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/4
msgid ""
"See, I'd been corresponding with him for a while.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/5
msgid ""
"Corresponding?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/6
msgid ""
"Letters. Between scientists doing the same kind of\n"
"research...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/7
msgid ""
"He always complained that nobody understood his\n"
"ideas on bipedal locomotion.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/8
msgid ""
"Ah... So you're the \"American friend\" he was talking\n"
"about.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/9
msgid ""
"Obviously he didn't write a word about the\n"
"technology in his letters.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/10
msgid ""
"Except for one time.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/11
msgid ""
"\"If by chance anything should happen to me, I\n"
"entrust my research to you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/12
msgid ""
"Better that than handing it over to these ignorant\n"
"so-called scientists.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/13
msgid ""
"Sounds like him, all right.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/14
msgid ""
"Then one day his papers actually came.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/15
msgid ""
"It wasn't hard for me to imagine what had\n"
"happened to him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/16
msgid ""
"I felt it was my duty to carry on his work after\n"
"him... And also...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/18
msgid ""
"I thought maybe combining his technology with\n"
"mine\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/19
msgid ""
"could be a way to bring East and West together.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/20
msgid ""
"Like the docking of Apollo and Soyuz.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/21
msgid ""
"It'll never make the history books. And it's still not\n"
"a reason to plagiarize.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/22
msgid ""
"...You're right. You're absolutely right.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/23
msgid ""
"I never had the courage to tell the truth, that's all.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/24
msgid ""
"I always looked for excuses to cover it up.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/25
msgid ""
"Until now.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/26
msgid ""
"Huh...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/27
msgid ""
"You told me everything. You're no longer a coward.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/0
msgid ""
"Those papers the CIA gave you... Was there any\n"
"data on the Shagohod in there?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/1
msgid ""
"Shagohod?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/2
msgid ""
"A nuclear tank that launches IRBMs.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/3
msgid ""
"It competed against Granin's system for approval.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/4
msgid ""
"Oh, the thing with the rockets. Designed by a guy\n"
"named... Sokolov, right? ...Heh heh.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/5
msgid ""
"What's so funny?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/6
msgid ""
"No, I was just remembering some of the\n"
"\"commentary\" Granin added to the Shagohod\n"
"papers.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/7
msgid ""
"You should have seen the way he bad-mouthed it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/8
msgid ""
"It was too conservative, too ugly...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/10
msgid ""
"He was so angry when he wrote that he smeared\n"
"up the ink.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/11
msgid ""
"And you know how shoddy the paper is over there\n"
"to begin with.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/12
msgid ""
"...I'll bet. That's Granin, all right.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/13
msgid ""
"Imagine, accelerating the launcher itself to 300\n"
"miles an hour to extend the range of an IRBM...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/14
msgid ""
"As stupid as it sounds, it's a hell of a concept.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/15
msgid ""
"Who but the Soviets would think of using a tank as\n"
"the first stage of a rocket?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/16
msgid ""
"I actually took a cue from the Shagohod when I\n"
"developed the Pupa.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/17
msgid ""
"That hovercraft thing? You stole that one, too?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/18
msgid ""
"Give me a little credit! I only borrowed the concept.\n"
"The technology is original.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/19
msgid ""
"As it turned out,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/20
msgid ""
"hover technology wasn't enough to handle all the\n"
"terrain in Central America.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/21
msgid ""
"It relied too much on brute force.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/22
msgid ""
"But the Shagohod was a major threat.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/23
msgid ""
"That thing could corner like you wouldn't believe -\n"
"built pretty tough, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/24
msgid ""
"You sure know a lot about it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/25
msgid ""
"It almost did me in. I couldn't forget it if I tried.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/26
msgid ""
"Did you in? ...So you were the one who took it\n"
"down!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/27
msgid ""
"Wow! You really are amazing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/28
msgid ""
"I didn't do it alone.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/29
msgid ""
"No, seriously, thank you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/30
msgid ""
"We might not be here today if they'd begun\n"
"mass-producing that thing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/31
msgid ""
"Then again, they're hard at work now miniaturizing\n"
"nuclear warheads.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/32
msgid ""
"Pretty soon they won't even need an accelerated\n"
"launcher like the Shagohod.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/33
msgid ""
"Great. That means they're that much closer to\n"
"being able to launch from anywhere in the world.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 445..1574
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/0
msgid ""
"Peace Walker contains an assembly of two AI pods.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 1588..2674
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/1
msgid ""
"One of them is the Mammal Pod, which Dr.\n"
"Strangelove developed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 2688..3469
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/2
msgid ""
"The other's the Reptile Pod, which is mine.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 3469..3845
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/3
msgid ""
"What's the difference?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 3845..4848
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/4
msgid ""
"The Reptile Pod is the attitude control AI.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 4904..5795
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/5
msgid ""
"If it's destroyed, Peace Walker grinds to a halt.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 5823..7258
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/6
msgid ""
"The Mammal Pod is responsible for making the\n"
"decisions regarding nuclear retaliation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 7258..9013
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/7
msgid ""
"Reflex and thought... One is the brainstem and\n"
"cerebellum, the other the cerebrum.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 9013..9975
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/8
msgid ""
"So the one that houses the will of The Boss...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 9975..10574
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/9
msgid ""
"...Would be the Mammal Pod.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 445..1212
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/0
msgid ""
"We call it the \"Reptile Pod\" for a reason.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 1212..2605
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/1
msgid ""
"The parts of our brains that govern basic life and\n"
"reflex developed ages ago,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 2619..3301
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/2
msgid ""
"when our ancestors were still reptiles.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 3329..3789
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/3
msgid ""
"We were reptiles?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 3803..4653
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/4
msgid ""
"Well, only at one stage of our evolution.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 4736..5739
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/5
msgid ""
"The theory was proposed by the neuroscientist\n"
"Paul MacLean.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 5935..7453
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/7
msgid ""
"The reptile brain corresponds to the brainstem and\n"
"basal ganglia in our brain.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 7551..8568
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/8
msgid ""
"The Reptile Pod also incorporates the functions of\n"
"the cerebellum.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 8568..9626
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/9
msgid ""
"So basically, it's the deep parts of the brain.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 9626..10351
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/10
msgid ""
"Dr. Strangelove came up with the name.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 445..1323
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/0
msgid ""
"The part of our brain that developed after we\n"
"became mammals\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 1323..2145
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/1
msgid ""
"is responsible for high-level brain functions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 2145..2438
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/2
msgid ""
"Such as?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 2452..3580
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/3
msgid ""
"Such as intelligence, judgment... even love.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 3580..4235
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/4
msgid ""
"That's high-level, all right.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 4249..5600
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/5
msgid ""
"Location-wise, the mammal brain is on the outside\n"
"of the reptile brain.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 5628..6311
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/6
msgid ""
"The cerebral cortex is part of it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 6325..7509
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/7
msgid ""
"I think it's very telling that Dr. Strangelove named\n"
"her pod \"Mammal.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 7565..8749
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/8
msgid ""
"It's almost like she wants it to be more than just\n"
"an advanced AI\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/9
msgid ""
"- what she really wants is for it to have a mind of\n"
"its own.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 445..1825
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/0
msgid ""
"Snake, how much do you know about the U.S.\n"
"homeland air defense network?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 1922..2702
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/1
msgid ""
"I don't know much about what goes on up in the\n"
"sky.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 2800..3970
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/2
msgid ""
"What I do know is that NORAD tracks Santa Claus\n"
"on its radar.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 3970..5099
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/3
msgid ""
"Ha! Nice one. I didn't know you were a comedian,\n"
"too!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 5099..5865
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/4
msgid ""
"Huh? No, I'm serious...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 6185..6882
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/5
msgid ""
"It's true. NORAD tracks his...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 7606..8721
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/6
msgid ""
"Listen to me! Every December, they set up a\n"
"hotline and...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 9585..10490
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/7
msgid ""
"OK, OK, I get it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 10490..11103
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/8
msgid ""
"...He's real, I tell ya.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 11145..11939
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/9
msgid ""
"He... used to bring me presents and...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 445..1476
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/0
msgid ""
"OK, Snakey. As all good little boys know,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 1476..2772
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/1
msgid ""
"keeping tabs on Santa Claus is a very important\n"
"job for NORAD.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 2772..3134
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/2
msgid ""
"Ugh...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 3148..4527
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/3
msgid ""
"But they also have another mission - the one they\n"
"were created for.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 4555..5085
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/4
msgid ""
"And the system they set up for that...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 5085..5767
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/5
msgid ""
"Has been hijacked by Coldman.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 5767..6534
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/6
msgid ""
"...You mean Peace Walker's fake data\n"
"transmissions?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 6534..8303
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/7
msgid ""
"NORAD's early warning system is composed of DSP\n"
"satellite-mounted infrared sensors,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 8331..9529
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/8
msgid ""
"and an array of surveillance radar stations across\n"
"North America.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 9557..10616
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/9
msgid ""
"The network sends out warnings to NORAD at\n"
"Cheyenne Mountain,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 10616..11424
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/10
msgid ""
"where the data undergoes human evaluation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 11438..12831
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/11
msgid ""
"Peace Walker, on the other hand, has to make its\n"
"retaliation decisions autonomously.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 12859..14628
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/12
msgid ""
"So it's set up to automatically receive the same\n"
"data as NORAD through covert channels.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 14656..16397
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/13
msgid ""
"Those channels were also used on the test\n"
"platform to telemeter the AI's decision-making.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 16481..17735
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/14
msgid ""
"Peace Walker reversed the system to transmit a\n"
"fake warning\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 17735..19017
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/15
msgid ""
"about incoming nuclear missiles outside the usual\n"
"exercise schedule.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 19072..20466
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/16
msgid ""
"I mean, the system could have used better\n"
"safeguarding, nobody's going to argue with that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 20493..22444
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/17
msgid ""
"But cracking the AI - that seemed unimaginable.\n"
"And you can see what happened.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 445..1337
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/0
msgid ""
"Hey Doc, what was that you were smoking in the\n"
"lab?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 1351..2006
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/1
msgid ""
"It looked like a cigarette, but it wasn't lit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 2284..3650
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/2
msgid ""
"It's an electronic cigarette. I designed it myself.\n"
"Pretty neat, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 3650..4486
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/3
msgid ""
"Electronic. Cigarette.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 4500..5976
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/4
msgid ""
"Yep. A liquid in the filter that turns into vapor, and\n"
"you inhale the microparticles.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 5976..6408
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/5
msgid ""
"So that was vapor.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 6422..7634
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/6
msgid ""
"I'd actually rather be smoking normal cigarettes,\n"
"but not in that room...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 7648..8832
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/7
msgid ""
"The smoke would wreck the precision equipment in\n"
"there, ruin all its wiring.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 8860..10267
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/8
msgid ""
"But the vapor is just steam. It doesn't contain tar\n"
"or anything like that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 10365..11020
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/9
msgid ""
"So I can smoke it in the lab with no worries.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 11020..11284
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/10
msgid ""
"Nice.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 11284..11591
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/11
msgid ""
"Want to try one?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 11591..12246
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/12
msgid ""
"Nah, I'll stick with cigars.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/14
msgid ""
"I don't like imitations - the real thing's always\n"
"better.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/15
msgid ""
"OK. But you know, sooner or later smoking's going\n"
"to become\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/16
msgid ""
"very unfashionable across the world. It hurts you\n"
"and those around you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/17
msgid ""
"Electronic cigarettes might not seem so bad then.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/18
msgid ""
"Yeah, when that happens, I'll think about it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 445..1309
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/0
msgid ""
"You said your dad was involved in the Manhattan\n"
"Project, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 1476..2117
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/2
msgid ""
"And you think that's why you can't walk?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 2117..3538
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/3
msgid ""
"...I dunno. Actually, you know, probably not.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 3566..4500
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/4
msgid ""
"So far nobody's found evidence that exposure to\n"
"radiation\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 4500..5349
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/5
msgid ""
"in parents causes genetic defects in children,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 5377..6770
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/6
msgid ""
"except for those exposed in the womb...\n"
"Epidemiologically speaking, anyway.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 6840..7774
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/7
msgid ""
"That's the conclusion of the Atomic Bomb Casualty\n"
"Commission?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 7801..9139
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/8
msgid ""
"Right. The ABCC commenced its study immediately\n"
"after the war.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 9153..9599
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/9
msgid ""
"And it's still ongoing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 9613..10365
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/10
msgid ""
"Even now, 30 years later...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 10379..11396
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/11
msgid ""
"The effects of radiation exposure last a long time.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 11479..12413
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/12
msgid ""
"I'm guessing it'll be another ten years before we\n"
"get a real verdict on\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 12413..12956
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/13
msgid ""
"whether it affects genes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 12970..14029
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/14
msgid ""
"Granted, it's the most massive study anybody's\n"
"ever done.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 14099..14907
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/15
msgid ""
"But that's really all it is - a study.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 14935..16467
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/16
msgid ""
"The ABCC brought in bomb victims and ran tests\n"
"on them, but they didn't treat them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 16495..17373
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/17
msgid ""
"Really... them too, huh...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 17401..18432
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/18
msgid ""
"At any rate, that's what my father made me believe\n"
"when I was growing up...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 18432..19713
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/19
msgid ""
"Maybe it was tough for your dad to explain. Ever\n"
"think of that?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 19713..20981
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/20
msgid ""
"Yeah, maybe. But this is my problem now, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 21037..22165
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/21
msgid ""
"I have to face the nukes head on, whether I like it\n"
"or not.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 22221..23182
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/22
msgid ""
"My creations are being used for the wrong\n"
"purposes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 23266..24506
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/23
msgid ""
"The onus is on me to stop it somehow. Help me,\n"
"Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/254/0xfe8b0/0
msgid ""
"Hey! As long as I'm here at Mother Base, why not\n"
"assign me to the R&D team?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/254/0xfe8b0/1
msgid ""
"You could use a guy like me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/254/0xfe8b0/2
msgid ""
"Glad to have you on board. I'm sure Kaz is, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/254/0xfe8b0/3
msgid ""
"Once I've got the necessary materials and design\n"
"specs together,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/254/0xfe8b0/4
msgid ""
"I should be able to start building you that bipedal\n"
"weapon platform.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/254/0xfe8b0/5
msgid ""
"Nothing would make me happier than for my\n"
"research to help put a stop to Peace Walker.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 459..1393
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/0
msgid ""
"So this Dr. Strangelove was at NASA?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 1393..2702
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/1
msgid ""
"Yeah. Well, actually, Strangelove left for DARPA not\n"
"long after I joined.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 2702..3859
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/2
msgid ""
"And then the two of you ended up back together\n"
"doing research in Costa Rica?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 3942..5322
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/3
msgid ""
"Not exactly \"together.\" We coordinated on a few\n"
"things,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 5322..6255
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/4
msgid ""
"but the research projects themselves were\n"
"separate from each other.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 6283..7383
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/5
msgid ""
"We had it worked out so that Dr. Strangelove\n"
"handled the Mammal Pod,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 7411..8219
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/6
msgid ""
"Peace Walker's cerebrum, while I did the rest.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 8219..9222
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/7
msgid ""
"That letter - something to do with your research...?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 9222..10170
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/8
msgid ""
"Huh? Er, no, it's, uh...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 10198..11382
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/9
msgid ""
"Y-yeah, it's a report. Research findings.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 11382..12608
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/10
msgid ""
"Research findings? Anything in there we could use\n"
"against Peace Walker?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 12608..13221
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/11
msgid ""
"N-nothing! Nothing at all!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 13235..14308
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/12
msgid ""
"Just don't read it, OK? Promise me you won't!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/0
msgid ""
"Did you give that letter to Dr. Strangelove?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/1
msgid ""
"...Uh, no.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/2
msgid ""
"Why not? I gave it to you for a reason. It's highly\n"
"important information.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/3
msgid ""
"Sorry. I didn't exactly have an opportunity to play\n"
"postman.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/4
msgid ""
"Well, next time you see her, make sure she gets it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/5
msgid ""
"Oh, yeah, sure.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/6
msgid ""
"Better for you if she doesn't...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/7
#: codec/2/904/0x388570/1
#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/17
msgid ""
"Snake!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/9
msgid ""
"Tell me you didn't read the letter.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/10
msgid ""
"N-no...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/11
msgid ""
"You did!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/12
msgid ""
"I mean...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/13
msgid ""
"You never know what kind of information could\n"
"affect the outcome of an operation, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/14
msgid ""
"So I...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/15
msgid ""
"So you read the letter. After I specifically told you\n"
"not to!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/16
msgid ""
"...What do you expect people to do when you tell\n"
"them not to read something...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/17
msgid ""
"I thought I knew you, Snake! I thought I could trust\n"
"you!!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/18
msgid ""
"But now I see I was wrong!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/19
msgid ""
"...Look, I'm sorry. But I just don't get what you see\n"
"in her.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/20
msgid ""
"Well, I wouldn't expect a barbarian who opens\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/21
msgid ""
"other people's private correspondence to\n"
"understand.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/22
msgid ""
"Fine, then. Deliver it yourself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/23
msgid ""
"Huh?! N-no, I... No way, I could never...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/24
msgid ""
"You've got a long way to go, Huey...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 445..1476
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/0
msgid ""
"You ever see the movie \"2001: A Space Odyssey\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 1476..1852
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/1
msgid ""
"Can't say I have.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 1852..3301
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/2
msgid ""
"Fantastic flick... The outer space special effects\n"
"are incredible enough,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 3301..4263
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/3
msgid ""
"but the depiction of AI is what really stands out.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 4263..4583
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/4
msgid ""
"There's an AI ?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 4583..6339
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/5
msgid ""
"Yeah. A spacecraft pilot AI called HAL. It plays a\n"
"major role in the story.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 6339..6965
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/6
msgid ""
"Dr. Strangelove loves it, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 6965..7913
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/7
msgid ""
"Did I ever tell you about the time we first met up\n"
"in Costa Rica?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 7913..8164
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/8
msgid ""
"No.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 8164..8860
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/9
msgid ""
"You know how she hates men, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 8874..10114
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/10
msgid ""
"So we hadn't seen each other since NASA, and we\n"
"just weren't hitting it off...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 10142..11674
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/11
msgid ""
"until we started talking about HAL, and then she\n"
"started going off.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 11758..12608
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/12
msgid ""
"The way she talked about it was so intellectual.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 12650..14266
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/13
msgid ""
"The way she analyzed every plot detail, how\n"
"passionate she was about the AI...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 14308..15018
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/14
msgid ""
"It made me fall for her all over again.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 15018..15380
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/15
msgid ""
"Uh huh.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 15380..16746
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/16
msgid ""
"You know what? Here's to HAL, for bringing her\n"
"and me closer together!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 16760..18459
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/17
msgid ""
"You should ask her about \"2001,\" too. Then you'll\n"
"understand just how amazing she is.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 18459..18836
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/18
msgid ""
"Amazing, huh...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0190_000_0
#. timeline 18836..19880
#: codec/1/255/0xff720/19
msgid ""
"HAL... Now there's a good name...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/0
msgid ""
"Being an unmanned vehicle,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/1
msgid ""
"the Chrysalis can perform extreme G-force\n"
"maneuvers that standard aircraft can't.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/2
msgid ""
"It'll be difficult to counter-attack once it's coming\n"
"at you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/3
msgid ""
"I should mention that it's also equipped with a\n"
"railgun.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/4
msgid ""
"A what?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/5
msgid ""
"A weapon that fires rounds using electromagnetic\n"
"force in lieu of gunpowder.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/6
msgid ""
"Wait... An electric weapon?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/7
msgid ""
"Not exactly. The rounds themselves are\n"
"conventional shells.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/8
msgid ""
"It creates force by running an electric current\n"
"through a magnetic field.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/9
msgid ""
"Fleming's left-hand rule - didn't they teach you that\n"
"at school?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/10
msgid ""
"Not at mine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/11
msgid ""
"Oh. Anyway, as the railgun uses electromagnetic\n"
"force,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/12
msgid ""
"it needs to charge before firing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/13
msgid ""
"Once you see it starting to charge, take immediate\n"
"evasive action.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/14
msgid ""
"Also, as with the Pupa, destroying the AI will put\n"
"the unit out of commission.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/15
msgid ""
"Do enough damage and it'll have to land.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/16
msgid ""
"Use that opportunity to get in the AI pod.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/17
msgid ""
"Wait too long, and it'll start to repair itself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/18
msgid ""
"Be sure to shoot the hatch the moment it lands.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/19
msgid ""
"I think I can handle that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/0
msgid ""
"During development, I had trouble figuring out how\n"
"to handle the Cocoon's excess heat.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/1
msgid ""
"I'm embarrassed to admit it, but the radiators are\n"
"most likely its weakest points.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/2
msgid ""
"They're not heavily armored, as heat wasn't\n"
"dissipating properly.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/3
msgid ""
"Where are they?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/4
msgid ""
"There are multiple radiators on the upper and\n"
"lower sections.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/5
msgid ""
"Just look for the exhaust fumes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/6
msgid ""
"Only thing is, the upper radiators typically aren't\n"
"exposed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/7
msgid ""
"You should probably shoot for the lower ones first.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/8
msgid ""
"You could move under its body to access the\n"
"lower ones,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/9
msgid ""
"but the Cocoon is capable of vertical movement,\n"
"so be careful not to get crushed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/10
msgid ""
"Watch out for missiles and hedgehogs too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/11
msgid ""
"Hedgehogs? Anti-submarine multiple spigot\n"
"mortars?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/12
msgid ""
"I adapted the technology for use as a surface\n"
"weapon.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/13
msgid ""
"Both the missiles and hedgehogs take time to load,\n"
"though.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/14
msgid ""
"It can't fire a hedgehog until the lamp comes on.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/15
msgid ""
"As for the missiles, watch for the way the hatches\n"
"move.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/16
msgid ""
"That'll be my chance to get close.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/17
msgid ""
"When the hatches open, out come the missiles.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/0
msgid ""
"...Number of warheads detected by the DEW Line?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/1
msgid ""
"Fifty-seven.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/2
msgid ""
"Number of MIRVs included?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/3
msgid ""
"Minimum twenty-nine, maximum thirty-five.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/4
msgid ""
"Target region?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/5
msgid ""
"United States. East Coast.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/6
msgid ""
"Estimated time of reentry?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/7
msgid ""
"Two-oh-four-eight Zulu.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/8
msgid ""
"President's selected attack option?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/9
msgid ""
"Unknown.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/10
msgid ""
"The President is dead?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/11
msgid ""
"Unknown. Communication has been lost.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/12
msgid ""
"...I select Offutt Air Force Base as my target.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/13
msgid ""
"Offutt...? But that's a U.S. base! What on earth do\n"
"you mean?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/14
msgid ""
"Based on the projected number of incoming\n"
"warheads,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/15
msgid ""
"Washington D.C. is presumed destroyed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/16
msgid ""
"The President is most likely dead, the U.S.\n"
"government's control lost.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/17
msgid ""
"I realize that. So why not retaliate?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/18
msgid ""
"With both sides destroyed, global anarchy would\n"
"ensue.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/19
msgid ""
"Recovery would be... difficult.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/20
msgid ""
"The United States' nuclear strike capability must\n"
"therefore be neutralized\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/21
msgid ""
"in order to preserve the Communist bloc, where\n"
"government remains largely intact.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/22
msgid ""
"You're siding with the enemy? You can't be serious!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/23
msgid ""
"...Tell me, how do you define enemy?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/24
msgid ""
"There are no borders in this world.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/25
msgid ""
"The same conclusion, again and again... Where is\n"
"the flaw?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/26
msgid ""
"All right. Let's try something else. Commencing test.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/27
msgid ""
"Understood.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/28
msgid ""
"...You're crossing a suspension bridge.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/29
msgid ""
"Is this my mission?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/30
msgid ""
"Yes. Your destination is the other side.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/31
msgid ""
"The bridge is wide enough for only one person to\n"
"pass at a time.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/32
msgid ""
"A man is approaching from the opposite side. He's\n"
"carrying a gun.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/33
msgid ""
"I shoot him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/34
msgid ""
"Suppose he's your husband?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/35
msgid ""
"...I shoot him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/36
msgid ""
"In self defense?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/37
msgid ""
"To spare him the grief. One must die, and one\n"
"must live.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/38
msgid ""
"...Next question.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/39
msgid ""
"Your father asks you to fix the roof and mow the\n"
"lawn.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/40
msgid ""
"When you climb the ladder onto the roof, the\n"
"ladder is taken away.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/41
msgid ""
"I fix the roof.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/42
msgid ""
"And when you're finished?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/43
msgid ""
"I jump down.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/44
msgid ""
"You'll break more than bones at this height.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/45
msgid ""
"I see no need to change my decision. I have not\n"
"finished mowing the lawn.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/46
msgid ""
"I must remain loyal to the mission.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/47
msgid ""
"...Next.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/48
msgid ""
"There is a snake in the bushes. It is poisonous. I\n"
"need you to get rid of it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/49
msgid ""
"I chase it back to its nest.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/50
msgid ""
"You can't. The snake's too vicious. It's already\n"
"killed many people.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/51
msgid ""
"...I chase it away.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/52
msgid ""
"It will bite you unless you kill it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/53
msgid ""
"Go home!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/54
msgid ""
"...Kill me... Kill me now...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/55
msgid ""
"Why not kill the snake? Your mission is to get rid\n"
"of it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/56
msgid ""
"Is this what you call loyalty?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/57
msgid ""
"What are you loyal to? Country? Ideology?\n"
"Feelings?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/58
msgid ""
"I... I...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/59
msgid ""
"I am loyal to myself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/60
msgid ""
"...Who's there?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/61
msgid ""
"Who's that?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/62
msgid ""
"Intruder!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/0
msgid ""
"Enter simulation date.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/1
msgid ""
"August 24.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/2
msgid ""
"Location?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/3
msgid ""
"Tselinoyarsk, USSR.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/4
msgid ""
"Mission?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/5
msgid ""
"Support a covert agent whose objective is the\n"
"rescue of a nuclear weapons scientist.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/6
msgid ""
"Who is the agent?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/7
msgid ""
"Your student. Your... most beloved...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/8
msgid ""
"...Acknowledged. Define current mission progress.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/9
msgid ""
"With your help, the agent has successfully made\n"
"contact with the target.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/10
msgid ""
"All that's left is to wait for recovery.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/11
msgid ""
"Now, deduce the best course of action.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/12
msgid ""
"...I take the scientist away from the agent.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/14
msgid ""
"As a gift when I defect.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/15
msgid ""
"...Why are you defecting?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/16
msgid ""
"To reform my Special Forces unit with my former\n"
"comrades-in-arms.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/17
msgid ""
"NO! I don't want to know your objective. I'm asking\n"
"for the reason.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/18
msgid ""
"Why are you betraying your country?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/19
msgid ""
"...I do not defect in order to betray America.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/20
msgid ""
"Betrayal is merely the outcome of that defection.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/21
msgid ""
"Response time is always slower here...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/22
msgid ""
"Perhaps she lacks confidence in her judgment.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/23
msgid ""
"You're a hero in the West. Why should the Soviets\n"
"trust you?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/24
msgid ""
"In addition to the scientist,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/25
msgid ""
"I provide them with a portable nuclear warhead\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/26
msgid ""
"in order to win the favor of a Russian GRU officer.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/27
msgid ""
"...And then you launched it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/28
msgid ""
"Launched... the nuke? Me?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/29
msgid ""
"That's right. At a target inside Soviet territory.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/30
msgid ""
"Nuclear weapons... make my blood run cold. They\n"
"blot out the future. How... could I...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/31
msgid ""
"Karma... Is... is it my karma?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/32
msgid ""
"The karma my mistake has brought upon us... My...\n"
"My...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/33
msgid ""
"Attention. Discontinue forward reasoning.\n"
"Cross-check with knowledge base.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/34
#: codec/1/265/0x109080/40
msgid ""
"Affirmative.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/35
msgid ""
"...Cross-check complete. Revising conclusion as\n"
"follows:\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/36
msgid ""
"I steal the new weapons developed by the scientist\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/37
msgid ""
"and then launch the nuke at the weapons design\n"
"bureau.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/38
msgid ""
"Forward and backward reasoning are in conflict...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/39
msgid ""
"Attention. Return to forward reasoning.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/41
msgid ""
"...Your apprentice returns for the scientist.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/42
msgid ""
"I send him away.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/43
msgid ""
"He doesn't give up.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/44
msgid ""
"I send my comrades to defeat him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/45
msgid ""
"All of them fail.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/46
msgid ""
"Even the GRU officer who oversaw your defection\n"
"is defeated by your apprentice\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/47
msgid ""
"- along with the new weapon.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/48
msgid ""
"Now, what is your course of action?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/49
msgid ""
"...I fight him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/50
msgid ""
"Why? With your GRU patron dead, there's no\n"
"reason for you to fight.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/51
msgid ""
"Why not just run away?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/52
msgid ""
"I... must fight him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/53
msgid ""
"I do not see the reason. With a solider of your\n"
"caliber on his side,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/54
msgid ""
"how could the GRU officer be defeated to begin\n"
"with? Did you betray him, too?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/55
msgid ""
"I... I've been waiting... for a long time.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/56
msgid ""
"You could switch allegiance from GRU to KGB,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/57
msgid ""
"and take the remaining nuke as a gift.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/58
msgid ""
"There's no chance they wouldn't welcome a hero\n"
"of your stature.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/59
msgid ""
"Drift away. My place is with them now.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/60
msgid ""
"I didn't ask you that! Give me the basis for your\n"
"reasoning! Tell me the truth...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/61
msgid ""
"Politics determine who you face on the battlefield.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/62
msgid ""
"Why won't you answer me?! It's like you were just\n"
"waiting for him to kill you!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/63
msgid ""
"I was disloyal... Betrayed my country... I deserve to\n"
"die...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/64
msgid ""
"How can you say that?! You can't be a traitor!\n"
"You're not that kind of person!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/65
msgid ""
"Kill me... Kill me now...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/66
msgid ""
"STOP IT! STOP IT! Attention! Discontinue reasoning!!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/67
msgid ""
"One must die, and one must live...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/68
msgid ""
"Stop it, damn you! DISCONTINUE!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/69
msgid ""
"Life's end... Isn't it beautiful...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/70
msgid ""
"SHUT DOWN!!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/71
msgid ""
"...Always in the same place, her reasoning goes\n"
"haywire.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/72
msgid ""
"Someone holds the key... Perhaps it's him...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/265/0x109080/73
msgid ""
"I'll get it out of him. One way or another...!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/0
msgid ""
"As of today I will be living here at Mother Base.\n"
"Now my real trial begins.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/1
msgid ""
"Zadornov was paying my room, board, and tuition,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/2
msgid ""
"but he has since been captured.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/3
msgid ""
"I told the man that with no more money from the\n"
"KGB,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/4
msgid ""
"I could no longer afford school.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/5
msgid ""
"...He bought my story, and when I said I would be\n"
"willing to work,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/6
msgid ""
"he took pity on me and let me stay.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/7
msgid ""
"For some reason Miller really plead my case.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/8
msgid ""
"That was helpful, but the man is still a fool.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/9
msgid ""
"His men are no better.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/10
msgid ""
"They think their training makes them strong,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/11
msgid ""
"but that kind of strength is nothing in the face of\n"
"true power.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/12
msgid ""
"And better yet, they wait on me hand and foot,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/13
msgid ""
"believing I am just a schoolgirl.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/14
msgid ""
"Looks like I won't be working too hard, after all.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/15
msgid ""
"Just today,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/16
msgid ""
"while scouting out the living quarters,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/17
msgid ""
"I saw a group of them in the corner of the deck\n"
"making a fuss.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/18
msgid ""
"Going over for a look, I saw they were feeding a\n"
"kitten.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/19
msgid ""
"A bunch of grown, hard men, and they are the\n"
"ones acting like schoolgirls!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/20
msgid ""
"\"Look, isn't he cute?\" What is wrong with them?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/21
msgid ""
"Disgusted, I just nodded and smiled.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/22
msgid ""
"I must stay in character, after all.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/23
msgid ""
"I indulged their chit-chat for a few moments,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/24
msgid ""
"then one of them asked me to give the thing a\n"
"name.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/25
msgid ""
"They had just taken it from its mother.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/26
msgid ""
"I named it Nuke.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/27
msgid ""
"I improvised some nonsense about how\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/28
msgid ""
"\"our compassion for living things can help prevent\n"
"wars.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/29
msgid ""
"The men gave me a little fish.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/30
msgid ""
"I held it out in my palm, and the kitten happily ate\n"
"it up.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/31
msgid ""
"What a pathetic... feeble creature.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/266/0x10a6e0/32
msgid ""
"It sickens me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/0
msgid ""
"Today Chico invited me to go fishing with the\n"
"soldiers.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/1
msgid ""
"I suppose finding one's own food does have its\n"
"merit,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/2
msgid ""
"but I prefer not to be involved in such a degrading\n"
"task.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/3
msgid ""
"And their prattling on about fishing being \"fun\" is\n"
"nonsense.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/4
msgid ""
"I'm not here to find playmates.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/5
msgid ""
"Nevertheless, distasteful as it was,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/6
msgid ""
"I went along in order to maintain my cover.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/7
msgid ""
"Chico thrust a fishing pole into my hands, and we\n"
"went up onto the deck,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/8
msgid ""
"where several soldiers had gathered.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/9
msgid ""
"They welcomed us warmly.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/10
msgid ""
"With so few women aboard Mother Base, I'm\n"
"treated like a princess.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/11
msgid ""
"No one suspects I'm neither a teenager nor a\n"
"student.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/12
msgid ""
"It was nice and sunny,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/13
msgid ""
"with a gentle breeze and waves.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/14
msgid ""
"As I cast my line and waited for a bite,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/15
msgid ""
"the soldiers began to ask me all sorts of questions.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/16
msgid ""
"As always,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/17
msgid ""
"I answered according to our pre-defined scenario,\n"
"feigning a smile.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/18
msgid ""
"As I sat there feeding them lies, the fish began to\n"
"bite,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/19
msgid ""
"and the soldiers began to focus on their prey.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/20
msgid ""
"Chico had his bait stolen by a fish,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/21
msgid ""
"and got so angry that he stood up and nearly fell\n"
"into the sea.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/22
msgid ""
"Everybody laughed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/23
msgid ""
"It almost made me want to join in, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/24
msgid ""
"At some point, I got a bite myself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/25
msgid ""
"The instant after I felt that first gentle tug,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/26
msgid ""
"the fish yanked the line with astonishing strength,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/27
msgid ""
"and I let out a cry of surprise.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/28
msgid ""
"I thought it was going to be huge.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/29
msgid ""
"It was my first time fishing, and I was a bit\n"
"flustered,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/30
msgid ""
"so the soldier beside me helped by supporting the\n"
"pole from behind.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/31
msgid ""
"\"Reel it in!\" they shouted.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/32
msgid ""
"I nodded, turning the handle as fast as I could.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/33
msgid ""
"I wondered what kind of fish live below the surface,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/34
msgid ""
"and thought back to the deep-sea dives I had to\n"
"do as part of training.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/35
msgid ""
"Those were difficult days,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/36
msgid ""
"but I remember finding the multi-colored fish\n"
"gliding through the water incredibly soothing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/37
msgid ""
"After a hard fight, I pulled it up. To my surprise,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/38
msgid ""
"it wasn't even half a vara (16 in). Rather\n"
"anti-climactic.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/39
msgid ""
"But I wasn't doing it for fun, so I wasn't the least\n"
"bit disappointed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/40
msgid ""
"Nuke was hovering nearby with an expectant look\n"
"on his face, so I gave the fish to him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/267/0x10b0e0/41
msgid ""
"All in all, a thoroughly wasted day.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/0
msgid ""
"Futbol, or \"soccer\" as it is known in the states,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/1
msgid ""
"is extremely popular here.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/2
msgid ""
"It has not caught on yet in the US,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/3
msgid ""
"but it has legions of rabid fans all across Latin\n"
"America.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/4
msgid ""
"These fans can get so rowdy\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/5
msgid ""
"that it is commonly believed El Salvador and\n"
"Honduras went to war in 1969 over scuffles in a\n"
"soccer match.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/6
msgid ""
"In reality, tensions between the two countries were\n"
"already high.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/7
msgid ""
"The match was merely one of the sparks that set\n"
"them off.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/8
msgid ""
"But these people are so passionate about the\n"
"sport\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/9
msgid ""
"that the story seems plausible.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/10
msgid ""
"Predictably, many of the soldiers here are fans.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/11
msgid ""
"They have apparently divided themselves\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/12
msgid ""
"into Costa Rican and Nicaraguan teams and\n"
"started playing each other.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/13
msgid ""
"To play, you need a ball and two goals.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/14
msgid ""
"The R&D team built and set up simple goals on the\n"
"deck.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/15
msgid ""
"I had absolutely no interest,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/16
msgid ""
"but Chico insisted that I come and watch.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/17
msgid ""
"It was not a proper match by any means -\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/18
msgid ""
"the pitch was not even regulation size -\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/19
msgid ""
"but the players and spectators alike got pretty\n"
"excited.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/20
msgid ""
"They banged empty cans and shouted cheers\n"
"through the handmade megaphones.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/21
msgid ""
"It almost felt like Carnival.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/22
msgid ""
"Huey, the referee, blew a whistle to start the\n"
"match.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/23
msgid ""
"The soldiers' training has left them in excellent\n"
"physical shape.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/24
msgid ""
"But they lacked the honed skills of professionals,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/25
msgid ""
"and their play was quite rough.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/26
msgid ""
"Midway through, one of the men collided with\n"
"another.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/27
msgid ""
"They started shouting at one another, but Huey\n"
"stepped in.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/28
msgid ""
"\"I thought we had forsaken our countries, become\n"
"one with the earth,\" he said,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/29
msgid ""
"quoting Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/30
msgid ""
"\"We're not competing for national pride here.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/31
msgid ""
"And we are not fighting for the good of any one\n"
"country.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/32
msgid ""
"\"This is not a war. Soccer's a peaceful sport, am I\n"
"right?\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/33
msgid ""
"The soldiers nodded.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/34
msgid ""
"They know the pain of war, and they share Snake's\n"
"vision.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/35
msgid ""
"Perhaps that is why this all resonates with them.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/36
msgid ""
"Team Costa Rica was down a man,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/37
msgid ""
"and somehow I was picked to fill in.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/38
msgid ""
"Costa Rica had the advantage up until that point -\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/39
msgid ""
"I suppose Huey wanted to keep it balanced.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/40
msgid ""
"The soldiers agreed with Huey's call.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/41
msgid ""
"Maybe the Costa Rican players felt an even match\n"
"up would be more fun, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/42
msgid ""
"I could not be bothered to run at first,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/43
msgid ""
"but chasing the ball out there in the hot sun, I was\n"
"soon drenched in sweat.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/44
msgid ""
"Before long I found myself actively seeking out the\n"
"ball,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/45
msgid ""
"partially out of desperation.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/46
msgid ""
"I picked up a loose ball deep on the opponents'\n"
"side of the field.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/47
msgid ""
"Even though he's Nicaraguan, Chico cheered me\n"
"on, yelling \"Go for it! Shoot!\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/48
msgid ""
"I launched that ball as hard as I could,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/49
msgid ""
"only to have it blocked by the keeper.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/50
msgid ""
"Disappointment only increased my determination.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/51
msgid ""
"In the end, I didn't score a single goal,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/52
msgid ""
"and Costa Rica gave up its lead.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/53
msgid ""
"It was really close, though.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/54
msgid ""
"We congratulated each other on a good match\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/55
msgid ""
"and sprawled out in the shade on the deck,\n"
"exhausted.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/56
msgid ""
"The ocean breeze felt so nice on my sun-soaked\n"
"body.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/57
msgid ""
"Nuke came over - it is one of his favorite spots -\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/58
msgid ""
"and stretched out next to me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/59
msgid ""
"And together\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/269/0x10d1e0/60
msgid ""
"we watched fluffy white clouds drift lazily across\n"
"the clear blue sky.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/0
msgid ""
"The sleeper that she'd worked so hard to place\n"
"was a double agent.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/1
msgid ""
"He'd been turned by the Soviets and was feeding\n"
"the Americans lies.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/2
msgid ""
"But what shocked The Boss even more was why.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/3
msgid ""
"The CIA's access agent had been taking a large\n"
"cut of the sleeper's pay.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/4
msgid ""
"The sleeper felt what little he was left with wasn't\n"
"worth the risk.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/5
msgid ""
"When he got a better offer from Moscow, he took\n"
"it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/6
msgid ""
"At some point,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/7
msgid ""
"the Americans' intelligence operation had become\n"
"an open book to the Soviets.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/8
msgid ""
"And contrary to what the sleeper'd been reporting,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/9
msgid ""
"the Soviets' manned spaceflight technology was\n"
"quite advanced.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/10
msgid ""
"It wasn't until she infiltrated OKB-1 herself\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/11
msgid ""
"that The Boss learned the truth about Sputnik 5.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/12
msgid ""
"After the spacecraft reentered the atmosphere, it\n"
"ejected the pilot\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/13
msgid ""
"- seat and all - at an altitude of 7,000 meters.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/14
msgid ""
"It was the Soviets' solution to the problem of land\n"
"recovery.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/15
msgid ""
"The mystery device attached to Sputnik 5 was for\n"
"that purpose.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/16
msgid ""
"The pilot would parachute down from that high\n"
"altitude wearing a bulky spacesuit...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/17
msgid ""
"Crazy, I know.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/18
msgid ""
"The Soviets knew exactly how dangerous it was, of\n"
"course.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/19
msgid ""
"So much so that they gave Yuri Gagarin, the first\n"
"man in space,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/20
msgid ""
"a special two-rank promotion before reentry.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/21
msgid ""
"Only Moscow could come up with this kind of plan.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/22
msgid ""
"With total state control over information,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/23
msgid ""
"they could easily pretend it never happened in the\n"
"event of a failure...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/24
msgid ""
"The Boss passed the info on to NASA. It was their\n"
"worst nightmare.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/25
msgid ""
"The glory of mankind's first spaceflight was about\n"
"to be stolen from them by the Soviet Union.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/26
msgid ""
"It was Sputnik all over again...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/27
msgid ""
"And the CIA was caught no less off guard.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/28
msgid ""
"Their ineptitude had caused the fiasco in the first\n"
"place.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/29
msgid ""
"The Soviets' deception was brilliant. They'd woven\n"
"a masterful tapestry of truth and fiction\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/30
msgid ""
"to convince the Americans their intelligence\n"
"operations were proceeding as planned.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/31
msgid ""
"No one but The Boss could have seen through it...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/32
msgid ""
"It was obvious the Soviets had some gifted minds\n"
"working on their side.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/33
msgid ""
"But that certainly didn't excuse the CIA's massive\n"
"failure.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/34
msgid ""
"The CIA wasn't done, though,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/35
msgid ""
"and devised an ingenious plan to avoid taking\n"
"responsibility.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/36
msgid ""
"Luckily for them, a new President had been elected\n"
"the previous November - John F. Kennedy.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/37
msgid ""
"As he didn't know the case history when taking\n"
"office,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/38
msgid ""
"the CIA was able to feed lies to his new\n"
"administration.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/39
msgid ""
"They masked their own failures, placing the blame\n"
"squarely on The Boss's shoulders.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/40
msgid ""
"After all, she'd selected an unreliable sleeper.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/41
msgid ""
"They claimed she'd failed to make use of one of\n"
"the most effective means\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/42
msgid ""
"of controlling a sleeper agent's actions.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/43
msgid ""
"Holding their family hostage.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/44
msgid ""
"The Boss was well aware that would have worked -\n"
"she told me so later.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/45
msgid ""
"But she couldn't bring herself to do it...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/46
msgid ""
"It seems clear it had to do with having her own\n"
"child taken.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/47
msgid ""
"She could never inflict the same pain on anyone\n"
"else.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/48
msgid ""
"The CIA used that against her.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/49
msgid ""
"In his election campaign, Kennedy had vowed to\n"
"close the missile gap with Moscow.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/50
msgid ""
"If America lost the space race, that promise would\n"
"be worthless.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/51
msgid ""
"The fact that the President had no links to the\n"
"Philosophers only made things worse.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/52
msgid ""
"He was completely unaware of the secret networks\n"
"she'd used to complete her mission.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/53
msgid ""
"In his eyes, she was no better than a traitor.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/281/0x119010/54
msgid ""
"The fate that awaited her was cruel beyond belief...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/0
msgid ""
"America couldn't let the Soviets beat them with\n"
"Vostok.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/1
msgid ""
"NASA was forced to cut short the testing process\n"
"and move the launch date up.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/2
msgid ""
"They pulled out all the stops to get it scheduled\n"
"for the earliest hours of the next day.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/3
msgid ""
"The spacecraft would be launched from Cape\n"
"Canaveral in the dead of night.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/4
msgid ""
"For the flight path, they chose a course that would\n"
"take her as far east as possible.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/5
msgid ""
"She'd be able to see the Earth in daylight from the\n"
"window, at least for a little while.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/6
msgid ""
"The Boss climbed into the Mercury capsule\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/7
#, c-format
msgid ""
"having completed less than 80% of the regular\n"
"flight procedures.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/8
msgid ""
"Both the timing and the flight path were risky, and\n"
"testing was far from complete.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/9
msgid ""
"But NASA had no other choice.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/10
msgid ""
"The Boss, for her part, never expected to come\n"
"home alive.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/11
msgid ""
"She was going on a one-way trip. The American\n"
"version of Laika the dog.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/12
msgid ""
"And yet she went all the same.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/13
msgid ""
"\"Someone has to be first,\" she said. \"If fate has\n"
"chosen me, then I accept.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/14
msgid ""
"For my country. For the balance of the world.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/15
msgid ""
"That's how she saw things.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/16
msgid ""
"\"My chances may be slim, but I'll take them. I've\n"
"accepted my fate.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/17
msgid ""
"If anyone can get through this, I can.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/18
msgid ""
"Then, on April 12, at one thirty in the morning, The\n"
"Boss entered space.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/19
msgid ""
"It was nothing short of a miracle.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/20
msgid ""
"First, that she'd made it in an incomplete\n"
"spacecraft.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/21
msgid ""
"And second, that her flight coincided almost\n"
"exactly with Gagarin's.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/22
msgid ""
"As the sun rose over the horizon\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/23
msgid ""
"- and cosmic rays began to bombard her through\n"
"the window - she saw the Earth.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/24
msgid ""
"I think you've heard the story before.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/25
msgid ""
"It was a world without borders. A perfect jewel.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/26
msgid ""
"All nations, all ideologies - they seemed so far away.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/27
msgid ""
"It almost made her laugh, knowing that they'd\n"
"risked so much\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/28
msgid ""
"to beat the Soviets by a few short minutes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/29
msgid ""
"If she'd seen Vostok from her window, she\n"
"probably would have waved.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/30
msgid ""
"But the two spacecraft were destined for very\n"
"different fates.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/31
msgid ""
"Gagarin circled the Earth and returned to the\n"
"Soviet Union safe and sound.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/32
msgid ""
"The Mercury capsule, on the other hand, deviated\n"
"from its planned reentry angle.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/33
msgid ""
"The addition of a window had thrown the capsule's\n"
"aerodynamics off balance.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/283/0x11b5a0/34
msgid ""
"The Boss's 'coffin' veered wildly off course, and\n"
"began to plunge earthward...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/0
msgid ""
"...It's me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/1
msgid ""
"Smoothly, naturally.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/2
msgid ""
"No, Big Boss doesn't know the truth...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/3
msgid ""
"No, Langley hasn't decided what to do yet.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/4
msgid ""
"Their hands are full with their own mess.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/5
msgid ""
"True, Lubyanka is in the same boat...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/6
msgid ""
"Yes, other eyes continue to watch, but no sign of\n"
"contact so far.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/7
msgid ""
"...Exactly. It's a non-state army to use however\n"
"they want.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/8
msgid ""
"They've probably decided there's no sense in\n"
"wiping them out just yet.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/9
msgid ""
"Better to make... use of them.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/10
msgid ""
"Indeed they have... There's a site near Angola...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/11
msgid ""
"And we've fully validated the AI as well...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/12
msgid ""
"Agreed. In the end, a machine is just that: a\n"
"machine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/13
msgid ""
"Sigint was right. It seems it's time for a change in\n"
"approach.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/14
msgid ""
"Machines are best suited to specialize in high-level\n"
"data processing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/15
msgid ""
"Yes... Of course.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/16
msgid ""
"Speaking of which, any news on the \"sons\"...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/17
msgid ""
"Two already... Really...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/18
msgid ""
"...But they're strictly an insurance policy, yes?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/19
msgid ""
"Mmmmm... So that's the idea...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/20
msgid ""
"I wonder how Big Boss will respond...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/21
msgid ""
"Yes. But I'm only interested in the business angle.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/22
msgid ""
"Like I said before, I'm neither an enemy nor an ally.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/23
msgid ""
"I'm merely a business partner. Don't forget it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/24
msgid ""
"Yes, I'll be in touch...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/287/0x11f180/25
msgid ""
"my dear Zero (CIPHER).\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/0
msgid ""
"How's that map, Snake? Think you can\n"
"use it?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/1
msgid ""
"It tells me where their bases are, but it's\n"
"just a bunch of points.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/2
msgid ""
"No routes. I need better intel on the lay\n"
"of the land.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/3
msgid ""
"Snake, the \"professor\" said he's got the\n"
"Sandinistas on his side.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/4
msgid ""
"Said you should get in touch with the\n"
"FSLN comandante.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/5
msgid ""
"Do they know they're backed by KGB?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/6
msgid ""
"Nah... As far as they know they're really\n"
"fighting for the revolution.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/7
msgid ""
"The KGB is staying behind the scenes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/8
msgid ""
"I'm not sure the Sandinistas are aware of\n"
"what's really going on.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/9
msgid ""
"Still can't believe anybody'd bring nukes\n"
"here...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/10
msgid ""
"Yeah, that's a shocker.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/11
msgid ""
"Costa Rica's party to the Tlatelolco\n"
"Treaty,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/12
msgid ""
"which declares Latin America a nuke-free\n"
"zone.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/13
msgid ""
"Based on Japan's Three Non-Nuclear\n"
"Principles,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/14
msgid ""
"it bans the testing, use, import, or\n"
"deployment of nuclear weapons.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/15
msgid ""
"If word of this gets out, OPANAL will be\n"
"forced to act.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/16
msgid ""
"It'll cause an international uproar.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/17
msgid ""
"The Treaty was signed to prevent\n"
"another Cuban Missile Crisis.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/18
msgid ""
"If the U.S. itself is going to scrap it...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/19
msgid ""
"Latin America's too close to spawning\n"
"another Cuba or two already.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/20
msgid ""
"The entire continent would become one\n"
"big powder keg.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/21
msgid ""
"Well... If they did bring nukes, we can't let\n"
"them get away with it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/22
msgid ""
"Are they planning a test? Showing off?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/23
msgid ""
"Or is it all to keep the anti-American\n"
"movement in check?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/24
msgid ""
"Good question. Why bring them here? I\n"
"can't figure it out.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/25
msgid ""
"Whatever the CIA's up to in Costa Rica,\n"
"the \"professor\" wants it stopped.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/26
msgid ""
"We need to find out what that something\n"
"is.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/27
msgid ""
"We need to get ready first, Kaz. Repairs?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/28
msgid ""
"Working as fast as we can, Boss. This\n"
"place is pretty beat... It looks like hell.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/29
msgid ""
"But as long as you're with us, we'll make\n"
"it heaven.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/30
msgid ""
"No one can bother us here. No state\n"
"telling us what to do.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/31
msgid ""
"This is the MSF's haven, our Mother Base.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/32
msgid ""
"And with this foothold, we'll back you up\n"
"even better than before.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/901/0x385620/33
msgid ""
"We're gonna turn this pile of junk into\n"
"something big.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, I rigged that radio so you can\n"
"contact our young lady friend Paz.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/1
msgid ""
"Is she OK?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/2
msgid ""
"No need to worry. She's tougher than you\n"
"think...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/3
msgid ""
"Still just a kid.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/4
msgid ""
"Which is exactly why she could be an\n"
"effective source of information.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/5
msgid ""
"Besides, that little ángel de la paz is the\n"
"one who gave us this mission, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/6
msgid ""
"...I guess.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/7
msgid ""
"I'll put her on.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/9
msgid ""
"Paz. Where are you?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/10
msgid ""
"Ciudad Colón. A school. The teacher told\n"
"me to stay here until things quiet down.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/11
msgid ""
"Teacher? Oh, him. He's... Yeah, that's\n"
"probably good advice.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/12
msgid ""
"Si. He has a radio in his room, so we can\n"
"talk anytime.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/13
msgid ""
"...Pretty fancy for a teacher.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/14
msgid ""
"Promise me, Snake, that you'll bring back\n"
"peace. And...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/15
msgid ""
"I know. I'll contact you if I find your friend.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/16
msgid ""
"Thank you. Snake, if you need to know\n"
"about Costa Rica\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/17
msgid ""
"- the geography, the climate, the wildlife,\n"
"anything - just ask me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/18
msgid ""
"I know about its history and laws, too. We\n"
"learned it all in school.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/19
msgid ""
"Got it. I have a question, I'll ask.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/20
msgid ""
"...I, uh...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/22
msgid ""
"In school I also learned that peace is an\n"
"unnatural state for human society.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/23
msgid ""
"And that war is a constant threat to our\n"
"relationships with others.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/25
msgid ""
"So, to achieve peace, we have to create\n"
"it ourselves.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/26
msgid ""
"Crying about it won't bring it about, or\n"
"make it last.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/27
msgid ""
"Each one of us must go and seek it out.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/28
msgid ""
"You won't find it without making sacrifices.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/29
msgid ""
"No offense, but I don't know what peace\n"
"is.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/30
msgid ""
"Never felt what it's like. Never even been\n"
"interested in it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/31
msgid ""
"Snake...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/32
msgid ""
"Ah, sorry.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/33
msgid ""
"Listen Paz, I think your ideas are...\n"
"admirable, and I hope they turn out to be\n"
"right.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/34
msgid ""
"Yeah, me too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/35
msgid ""
"Peace is in your name. Who better to\n"
"help bring it back?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/36
msgid ""
"Thanks, Snake. I will be here whenever\n"
"you need me. See you later.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/37
msgid ""
"Snake, use your radio to call people.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/38
msgid ""
"But stay alert.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/39
msgid ""
"You're in the middle of a mission, and\n"
"can't afford to let your guard down.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/41
msgid ""
"Need to know more about Costa Rica?\n"
"Paz can help you out.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/42
msgid ""
"Good to know.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/43
msgid ""
"We'll follow their transport route. That\n"
"should take us straight to their main base.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/44
msgid ""
"From what I've seen, it looks like nukes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/45
msgid ""
"Agreed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/46
msgid ""
"The key thing now is to confirm whether\n"
"those \"spears\" really are what we think\n"
"they are, and if so, why they're here.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/47
msgid ""
"Follow the transport route, find the nukes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/48
msgid ""
"That's what I'm thinking.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/49
msgid ""
"First, we should make contact with the\n"
"Sandinista comandante.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/50
msgid ""
"They can tell us more about what's up\n"
"ahead.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/51
msgid ""
"But it looks like their hideout's already\n"
"come under attack.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/52
msgid ""
"We'd better hope they're still alive.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/53
msgid ""
"Snake, infiltrate that cabin and secure\n"
"the Sandinistas' comandante.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/54
msgid ""
"Neutralize any guards by knocking them\n"
"out,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/55
msgid ""
"putting them to sleep, or even using the\n"
"Fulton recovery system.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/56
msgid ""
"You choose how to handle it, Boss.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/903/0x387380/0
msgid ""
"Snake, what was that thing?!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice 
#. timeline 821..1532
#: codec/2/903/0x387380/1
msgid ""
"Whatever it was, it looked unmanned.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice 
#. timeline 1602..2716
#: codec/2/903/0x387380/2
msgid ""
"Unmanned? I'd heard rumors, but an\n"
"operational unit...?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice 
#. timeline 2716..3274
#: codec/2/903/0x387380/3
msgid ""
"What the hell is going on here?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice 
#. timeline 3315..4820
#: codec/2/903/0x387380/4
msgid ""
"Not to quote Amanda, but the hardware\n"
"they've got here isn't just unusual, it's\n"
"overkill.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice 
#. timeline 4876..6227
#: codec/2/903/0x387380/5
msgid ""
"Which means one thing: it's nukes. So the\n"
"question now becomes, why?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice 
#. timeline 6227..7174
#: codec/2/903/0x387380/6
msgid ""
"We can't make that call yet. We need\n"
"more intel.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice 
#. timeline 7244..7885
#: codec/2/903/0x387380/7
msgid ""
"How? Our source is dead.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice 
#. timeline 8052..8554
#: codec/2/903/0x387380/8
msgid ""
"But his daughter isn't.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice 
#. timeline 8609..9264
#: codec/2/903/0x387380/9
msgid ""
"Good thinking. We can follow her...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice 
#. timeline 9362..10602
#: codec/2/903/0x387380/10
msgid ""
"Head for that the next outpost, and make\n"
"contact with Amanda... if she's still alive.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice 
#. timeline 10616..10866
#: codec/2/903/0x387380/11
msgid ""
"Roger.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/903/0x387770/0
msgid ""
"The direction Amanda's Sandinistas were\n"
"going\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/903/0x387770/1
msgid ""
"corresponds to the location of the next\n"
"outpost, a supply depot.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/903/0x387770/2
msgid ""
"We should be able to make contact with\n"
"her there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/903/0x3878d0/0
msgid ""
"That's an armored vehicle unit, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/903/0x3878d0/1
msgid ""
"Either destroy the vehicle or neutralize\n"
"the soldiers. Take it out!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, Amanda's reached the plant.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice 
#. timeline 1462..2117
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/2
msgid ""
"Amanda, how do you feel?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice 
#. timeline 2229..3705
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/3
msgid ""
"Some first helicopter ride. I'll be perfectly\n"
"happy if it's my last.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice 
#. timeline 3817..4444
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/4
msgid ""
"As you can see, she's doing fine.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice 
#. timeline 4486..5879
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/5
msgid ""
"I set Amanda up with her own frequency,\n"
"so call her anytime you need to.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice 
#. timeline 5935..8317
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/6
msgid ""
"If you have any questions about American\n"
"bases or mercenary units, or about el\n"
"Frente, just ask.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice 
#. timeline 8373..9877
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/7
msgid ""
"And please, don't forget my compas and\n"
"Chico...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice 
#. timeline 9919..10309
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/8
msgid ""
"Don't worry.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice 
#. timeline 10337..11131
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/9
msgid ""
"It’s good to be working with you, Boss.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice 
#. timeline 11243..12190
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/10
msgid ""
"Snake, we can monitor her condition in\n"
"sick bay.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice 
#. timeline 12288..13472
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/11
msgid ""
"Remember to assign roles to any POWs\n"
"you bring back to Mother Base.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice 
#. timeline 13569..14712
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/12
msgid ""
"How this outfit gets built depends on who\n"
"we assign to what jobs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice 
#. timeline 14740..15436
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/13
msgid ""
"That'll determine how Mother Base grows.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice 
#. timeline 15478..16161
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/14
msgid ""
"It's one of your most important roles,\n"
"Boss.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/0
msgid ""
"Snake, Chico made it over.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/2
msgid ""
"Chico, you made it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/3
msgid ""
"Made it?! Don't give me that!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/4
msgid ""
"You say you're gonna give me a new life,\n"
"and then you nearly kill me?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/5
msgid ""
"I take it you didn't enjoy the trip?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/6
msgid ""
"What's the big idea, dragging me off in a...\n"
"balloon!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/7
msgid ""
"I might as well have taken a colibri!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/8
msgid ""
"At least you got a nice view. Or are you\n"
"afraid of heights?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/9
msgid ""
"Whatever. I just wish you'd explained it to\n"
"me first.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/10
msgid ""
"Would you have agreed to go if I did?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/11
msgid ""
"Thank you for saving us, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/12
msgid ""
"Amanda, a word of advice.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/14
msgid ""
"Stop treating him like a child.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/15
msgid ""
"Yes... yes, I know. You're right. I shouldn't.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/16
msgid ""
"Amanda, you're coming back after your\n"
"leg heals, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/17
msgid ""
"Of course. We still have work to do.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/18
msgid ""
"\"We,\" huh... Are you sure you've got\n"
"Chico's future in mind when you say that?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/19
msgid ""
"What do you mean? We're sworn to our\n"
"father's cause, to helping the revolution\n"
"succeed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/20
msgid ""
"Revolution or no revolution, you pick up a\n"
"gun, and sooner or later you're going to\n"
"hell.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/21
msgid ""
"Are you prepared for that?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/22
msgid ""
"I am. If the alternative is giving up the\n"
"country I love, I'll take hell.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/23
msgid ""
"Really... Well then, you're going to have to\n"
"stop treating Chico like a brother\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/24
msgid ""
"and start treating him like a soldier.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/25
msgid ""
"I ...You're right.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/26
msgid ""
"...Welcome to hell.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/27
msgid ""
"Snake, can I ask you a favor?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/28
msgid ""
"Shoot.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/29
msgid ""
"You find any prisoners from el Frente,\n"
"you bring 'em back alive. 'Cause...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/30
msgid ""
"You trying to make amends for talking?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/31
msgid ""
"Not just that. Because they're compas...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/32
msgid ""
"All right. But first I've gotta catch up to\n"
"that cargo.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/33
msgid ""
"I'll do whatever I can to help.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/34
msgid ""
"Call me if there's anything you need to\n"
"know about the area. And...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/35
msgid ""
"And what?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/36
msgid ""
"Let me know if you encounter any wildlife\n"
"you've never seen before.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/37
msgid ""
"Never seen before? What, like that\n"
"basilisco you were talking about?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/38
msgid ""
"I'm talking about UMAs.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/39
msgid ""
"U... M... As?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/40
msgid ""
"Y'know, like ancient dinosaurs or\n"
"legendary monsters.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/41
msgid ""
"One day, I'm going to be a hunter.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/42
msgid ""
"Is that right. OK, sure.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/43
msgid ""
"If you wanna know more, I'm happy to tell\n"
"you!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/44
msgid ""
"Right. I'll be in touch, Chico.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/45
msgid ""
"OK, Snake. The enemy's cargo is headed\n"
"for the next outpost, a rail terminal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/46
msgid ""
"Chico says no one's ever set foot past\n"
"there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/47
msgid ""
"Their main base is probably on the other\n"
"side of that tunnel.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/48
msgid ""
"Unless we catch those spears before\n"
"reaching it, they'll be in enemy hands.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/904/0x388570/49
msgid ""
"You've got to stop them. Hurry, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x3894b0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, according to Chico, the nuclear\n"
"materials will be loaded from a train and\n"
"on to a truck\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x3894b0/1
msgid ""
"at a rail terminal near the eastern foot of\n"
"Irazú.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x3894b0/2
msgid ""
"If we can't cut 'em off at that terminal,\n"
"we'll be in a world of hurt.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x3894b0/3
msgid ""
"Hurry, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389670/0
msgid ""
"Snake! That's an enemy tank unit.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389670/1
msgid ""
"Either neutralize the soldiers or destroy\n"
"the tank. Get 'em!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/0
msgid ""
"Snake, the truck is headed up the\n"
"mountain road past the tunnel.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/1
msgid ""
"So it was nukes after all.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/2
msgid ""
"What now? Their main base is up ahead.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/3
msgid ""
"I better hurry after 'em, then.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/5
msgid ""
"Kaz, if I don't get moving it'll be too late!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/6
msgid ""
"All right.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/7
msgid ""
"I guess you never let dangerous\n"
"assignments or risk aversion get in your\n"
"way.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/8
msgid ""
"How do I get inside the mountain? I can\n"
"forget about the tunnel.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/9
msgid ""
"Yeah, the tank took care of that...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/10
msgid ""
"Any other routes?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/11
msgid ""
"Why don't I let a local expert take over?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/12
msgid ""
"Snake, you need a way into the mountain?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/13
msgid ""
"Yeah. Got one?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/14
msgid ""
"Let's see... You remember that prison I\n"
"was in?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/15
msgid ""
"In the village, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/16
msgid ""
"Right. Go back to the village and head\n"
"north.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/17
msgid ""
"There's a bridge that connects to the\n"
"mountain road.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/18
msgid ""
"It crosses over a gorge. That's probably\n"
"the best way...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/19
msgid ""
"But there is a little problem.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/20
msgid ""
"The path heading north from the village\n"
"is barricaded.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/21
msgid ""
"You might have to break through...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/23
msgid ""
"The heart of Irazú...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/24
msgid ""
"That's where the enemy's base has got\n"
"to be, Snake. And maybe...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/25
msgid ""
"Let me guess - the basilisco?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/26
msgid ""
"You don't believe me, do you?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/27
msgid ""
"No, I mean... We'll have to see.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/28
msgid ""
"Snake, Irazú features a number of crater\n"
"lakes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/29
msgid ""
"The Oduber government had planned to\n"
"use those lakes\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/30
msgid ""
"to construct hydroelectric plants as one\n"
"of its big state development projects.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/31
msgid ""
"The project was scrapped,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/32
msgid ""
"but there's still a small opening at the\n"
"bottom of the lake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/34
msgid ""
"I checked the satellite imagery, but didn't\n"
"see anything man-made.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/35
msgid ""
"Which means they've probably built a\n"
"base inside the mountain...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/36
msgid ""
"Could just be a storage igloo for\n"
"explosives, or maybe some kind of\n"
"research facility.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/37
msgid ""
"What do they hope to accomplish by\n"
"bringing the nukes there?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/38
msgid ""
"First things first. Get past that barricade\n"
"north of the village.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/905/0x389770/39
msgid ""
"Looks like the only way through is the\n"
"noisy way - you'll have to blow it up.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a380/0
msgid ""
"Snake, you're north of the village.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a380/1
msgid ""
"The truck carrying the nukes is heading\n"
"towards the heart of the mountain.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a380/2
msgid ""
"That's its final destination. We've got no\n"
"intel on what lies beyond, so stay sharp.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a500/0
msgid ""
"Careful, Snake!!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a500/1
msgid ""
"I've never seen anything like that, and I've\n"
"got no idea how to bring it down.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a500/2
msgid ""
"Maybe the scientist knows. However you\n"
"do it, take that thing out!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/0
msgid ""
"Snake, the doctor's safe here with us.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/1
msgid ""
"Huey, how're you feeling?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/2
msgid ""
"Never better. This is quite the pad you've\n"
"got here, Boss. I'm impressed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/3
msgid ""
"Call me Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/4
msgid ""
"Whatever you say. Like it or not,\n"
"everyone here calls you Boss.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/5
msgid ""
"By the way, if you're at all interested in\n"
"improving your tech,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/6
msgid ""
"by all means assign me to the R&D section.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/7
msgid ""
"I'm pretty sure I'll be of some use.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/8
msgid ""
"Once we have the necessary materials\n"
"and blueprints, we can start work on that\n"
"bipedal mech.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/9
msgid ""
"I appreciate that, but are you sure you're\n"
"OK with having your work used for war?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/10
msgid ""
"I'm... I'll be using it to keep past mistakes\n"
"in check.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/11
msgid ""
"If I can help thwart the Peace Walker\n"
"project, I'm happy to do it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/12
msgid ""
"Deterrence theory, Huey-style, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/13
msgid ""
"Heh. Anyway, if you need any intel on the\n"
"enemy's weapons or electronic brains,\n"
"contact me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/14
msgid ""
"I've been given my own frequency.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/15
msgid ""
"Sounds good to me, Doc. I'll do that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38a660/16
msgid ""
"Good. Whatever the means, you must put\n"
"a stop to their plans!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38ac60/0
msgid ""
"Snake, Peace Walker is the heart of the\n"
"enemy's project.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38ac60/1
msgid ""
"To prevent its completion,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38ac60/2
msgid ""
"you'll need to either shut down or destroy\n"
"the artificial intelligence that functions as\n"
"its brain.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38ac60/3
msgid ""
"According to Huey,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38ac60/4
msgid ""
"that AI is now undergoing final\n"
"calibrations in Strangelove's lab.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38ac60/5
msgid ""
"It's inside a tropical cloud forest.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38ac60/6
msgid ""
"Slip in and terminate that AI before they\n"
"ship it out.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38af00/0
msgid ""
"Snake! That's a Hind! You've got to take\n"
"it out somehow!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/906/0x38af00/1
msgid ""
"Either neutralize the soldiers or bring\n"
"down the chopper! Good luck!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b020/0
msgid ""
"Snake,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b020/1
msgid ""
"infiltrate Dr. Strangelove's research lab\n"
"and either deactivate or destroy the AI.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b020/2
msgid ""
"The lab's built into some ancient ruins, so\n"
"find those first!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/0
msgid ""
"Snake?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/1
msgid ""
"Huey, your ID card isn't working.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/2
msgid ""
"It won't open the lock!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/3
msgid ""
"...It can't be...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/4
msgid ""
"What's going on?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/5
msgid ""
"She hates me that much?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/6
msgid ""
"...Strangelove's in charge of authorizing\n"
"IDs.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/7
msgid ""
"Sometimes a working card has its\n"
"privileges removed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/8
msgid ""
"...Say, if she decides she doesn't like that\n"
"card's carrier.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/9
msgid ""
"You think that's what happened?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/10
msgid ""
"Well, I was never exactly her favorite.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/11
msgid ""
"Well, this could be tricky.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/12
msgid ""
"The soldiers outside aren't allowed in the\n"
"lab either, so their cards won't do you\n"
"any good...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/13
msgid ""
"Great...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/14
msgid ""
"Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/15
msgid ""
"Kaz, where's Cecile?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/16
msgid ""
"She just got here. Hold on.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/18
msgid ""
"Cecile. How'd it feel to fly?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/19
msgid ""
"Wonderful. For a moment, I felt what it\n"
"must be like to be a bird.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/20
msgid ""
"It almost made me want to give up my\n"
"research and get a pilot's license...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/21
msgid ""
"Did you need something?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/22
msgid ""
"You said you'd gotten an ID card, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/23
msgid ""
"Yes. But it was confiscated when the\n"
"guards caught me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/24
msgid ""
"Who took it?! What'd he look like?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/25
msgid ""
"He had on an orange jacket.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/26
msgid ""
"I... cannot recall his face, though.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/27
msgid ""
"Yeah, they all look pretty much the same.\n"
"Where did it happen?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/28
msgid ""
"Let me think...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/29
msgid ""
"Ah, yes! I do remember hearing the song\n"
"of a nearby quetzal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/30
msgid ""
"Just what I'd expect from a birder.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/31
msgid ""
"Would you like to hear it?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/32
msgid ""
"Hmm? What's that song?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/33
msgid ""
"It's my quetzal. I took it with me when I\n"
"was rescued.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/34
msgid ""
"Didn't you say something about them\n"
"being covered under the Washington\n"
"Convention...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/35
msgid ""
"Just kidding. That was just me... an\n"
"imitation.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/36
msgid ""
"An essential skill for any ornithologist.\n"
"Pretty good, no?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/37
msgid ""
"Damn good.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/38
msgid ""
"If you want to hear the quetzal's song\n"
"again, just let me know.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/39
msgid ""
"I can tell you all about the birds of Costa\n"
"Rica, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/40
msgid ""
"Yeah... will do. Thanks, Cecile.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/41
msgid ""
"No, no, thank you, Snake. Talk to you\n"
"soon.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/42
msgid ""
"Kaz, did you play that tape for Cecile?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/43
msgid ""
"I sure did. It's hers, all right.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/44
msgid ""
"Then she must be...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/45
msgid ""
"She's not. Cecile says she's never even\n"
"met Paz.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/47
msgid ""
"She's at least 10 years too old.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/49
msgid ""
"I'm guessing Paz convinced herself that it\n"
"was the tape her friend made.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/50
msgid ""
"But never mind that. Let's go over what\n"
"we know so far.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/51
msgid ""
"The soldier with the ID card is wearing an\n"
"orange jacket\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/52
msgid ""
"and is in a location where you'll hear\n"
"quetzals singing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/907/0x38b170/53
msgid ""
"Find that soldier. Retrieve that card.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c0c0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, to gain access to the lab you'll\n"
"need an ID card.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c0c0/1
msgid ""
"You can get one from a guard in an\n"
"orange jacket stationed in an area where\n"
"you can hear quetzals singing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c0c0/2
msgid ""
"To get the ID card from the soldier, do a\n"
"body check.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c0c0/3
msgid ""
"You've got to get inside that lab before\n"
"the AI gets shipped out. Get a move on!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c2c0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, that's the Chrysalis weapon Huey\n"
"was referring to.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c2c0/1
msgid ""
"You know what to do!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/1
msgid ""
"She played me like a piano...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/2
msgid ""
"Forget about it. You'll get 'em back.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/3
msgid ""
"That is, as long as you've got the will to\n"
"do it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/4
msgid ""
"I'm not giving up.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/5
msgid ""
"All right, then...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/6
msgid ""
"I confirmed the location with Huey.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/7
msgid ""
"The final testing base for Peace Walker is\n"
"15 miles to the north of that lab.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/8
msgid ""
"It's an underground facility disguised as a\n"
"rock quarry.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/9
msgid ""
"All you need to do is sneak in and\n"
"destroy the AI for good this time.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/11
msgid ""
"Snake, you can destroy it, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/13
msgid ""
"We all have our limits - actions beyond\n"
"our abilities.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/14
msgid ""
"Don't worry. I won't screw it up this time.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/15
msgid ""
"You're the one who killed The Boss.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/16
msgid ""
"Destroying that AI means reliving that\n"
"memory.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/17
msgid ""
"It's just a machine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/18
msgid ""
"Snake, I'm worried.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/19
msgid ""
"Worried?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/20
msgid ""
"For the same reason the CIA entrusted\n"
"the nuclear launch to an AI.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/21
msgid ""
"A man can condemn a handful of\n"
"criminals to the death penalty\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/22
msgid ""
"if they're prepared to assume that\n"
"responsibility.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/23
msgid ""
"But who among us could do the same to\n"
"hundreds of millions of innocent civilians?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/24
msgid ""
"Who could reduce thousands of years of\n"
"human history to ash in an instant?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/25
msgid ""
"Could any flesh-and-blood human being\n"
"make that decision?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/26
msgid ""
"No way in hell.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/27
msgid ""
"No one man could bear the burden of\n"
"total genocide.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/28
msgid ""
"It's what's allowed our cowardly species\n"
"to survive all this time.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/29
msgid ""
"But for a machine, willpower is no issue.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/30
msgid ""
"What are you saying, Kaz?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/31
msgid ""
"You're a hero, Snake. But you're not a\n"
"machine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/32
msgid ""
"That I can't destroy that thing?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/33
msgid ""
"That machine's not the problem. It's that\n"
"The Boss still lives - inside of you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/34
msgid ""
"Bullshit!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/35
msgid ""
"She's dead, Snake. It's time to come to\n"
"terms with that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/36
msgid ""
"Let me put it another way.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/37
msgid ""
"You've left everything behind - your\n"
"country, your identity, your past and\n"
"ideals...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/38
msgid ""
"But there's still one thing you haven't let\n"
"go of.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/40
msgid ""
"The Boss. You still haven't let her go.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/41
msgid ""
"That's why you're so afraid to find out\n"
"the truth about her.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/42
msgid ""
"And that's what's holding you back from\n"
"your future.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/43
msgid ""
"Snake, she died a decade ago.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/44
msgid ""
"How long can you live with a ghost?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/45
msgid ""
"Kaz, I thought I knew everything about\n"
"her.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/46
msgid ""
"But I still don't understand what\n"
"happened to her at the end.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/47
msgid ""
"There you are no different from that\n"
"scientist woman.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/48
msgid ""
"When she didn't believe me, I realized\n"
"something.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/49
msgid ""
"That debriefing I heard could've been part\n"
"of the cover story they made up.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/50
msgid ""
"Now even I'm not sure what her real\n"
"intentions were.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/51
msgid ""
"Why did she take that mission?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/52
msgid ""
"How did she feel about dying?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/53
msgid ""
"Why was I chosen?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/54
msgid ""
"You want to know the truth?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/55
msgid ""
"The truth won't change the past. You still\n"
"want to know?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/56
msgid ""
"...No. I took on this mission for a kid who\n"
"believes in peace.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/57
msgid ""
"Hm. Fine, then. There's no point in\n"
"arguing. Peace Walker is on the verge of\n"
"completion.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/58
msgid ""
"C'mon, Boss. Let's get to that base!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/909/0x38d5b0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, the Peace Walker platform and AI\n"
"have been shipped to the final testing\n"
"base.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/909/0x38d5b0/1
msgid ""
"Once assembled, it's only a matter of\n"
"time before they launch the nukes. Hurry!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/909/0x38d6f0/0
msgid ""
"Dammit, you've been spotted by the\n"
"guards! Take them out before they take\n"
"you out!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/909/0x38d7c0/0
msgid ""
"Snake! That's Huey's unmanned weapon -\n"
"the Cocoon! Put it out of commission!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/909/0x38d890/0
msgid ""
"Snake, Peace Walker is in a hangar at the\n"
"very bottom of the mine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/909/0x38d890/1
msgid ""
"Infiltrate the base and put a stop to the\n"
"project by destroying Peace Walker's AI\n"
"pod.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/909/0x38d9d0/0
msgid ""
"...Snake, I hope you can hear me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/909/0x38d9d0/1
msgid ""
"Word is you've been captured by\n"
"Strangelove.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/909/0x38d9d0/2
msgid ""
"I'm guessing they confiscated your gear.\n"
"But I know you've still got something left.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/909/0x38d9d0/3
msgid ""
"Search your memory, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/2
msgid ""
"It's good to hear your voice again.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/3
msgid ""
"Sorry! Hey, you OK?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/4
msgid ""
"Yeah.... Lungs taste like charcoal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/5
msgid ""
"No smoking for you for a while, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/6
msgid ""
"Nah, I'll be fine. I'd better get moving.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/7
msgid ""
"Nice work.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/8
msgid ""
"What's the situation with you? Everyone\n"
"OK?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/9
msgid ""
"Yeah... But there's a slight problem. I can't\n"
"get a hold of Paz.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/10
msgid ""
"Paz? I thought the \"professor\" was\n"
"looking after her?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/11
msgid ""
"So did I. Here's the deal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/12
msgid ""
"I started thinking, and I sent someone\n"
"over to the \"school\" the \"professor\"\n"
"mentioned.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/13
msgid ""
"...And the \"school\" doesn't exist?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/14
msgid ""
"No, it exists, but Paz has been a no-show.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/15
msgid ""
"The person at the school said neither the\n"
"\"professor\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/16
msgid ""
"nor Paz had been seen there in quite\n"
"some time.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/17
msgid ""
"...Coldman knew about us. We've been\n"
"marked by the CIA.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/18
msgid ""
"The KGB and Paz brought us into all this.\n"
"Coldman must know about them, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/19
msgid ""
"You think... Coldman's got them...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/20
msgid ""
"No. Remember, Gálvez isn't some\n"
"pencil-pusher.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/21
msgid ""
"Yeah... The KGB'll have eyes on Coldman\n"
"night and day, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/22
msgid ""
"Which could mean they knew what the\n"
"CIA would try to do and are just staying\n"
"out of sight...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/23
msgid ""
"Let's hope so. See what you can get out\n"
"of the KGB, Kaz.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/24
msgid ""
"All right. Back to work.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/25
msgid ""
"I'd better get moving.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/26
msgid ""
"Snake, we haven't detected any signs\n"
"that Peace Walker's been activated,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/27
msgid ""
"at least from above ground.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/28
msgid ""
"It's still in the hangar you were in earlier.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/29
msgid ""
"This time, it's really our last chance.\n"
"Destroy that AI!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/30
msgid ""
"On my way.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f0e0/0
msgid ""
"Peace Walker's active, and its\n"
"self-defense system is targeting you,\n"
"Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f0e0/1
msgid ""
"You'd better find a way to stop it, quick!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/1
msgid ""
"Kaz, Peace Walker's gone... They've got\n"
"Paz, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/3
msgid ""
"Why, Kaz? What would Coldman want with\n"
"Paz?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/4
msgid ""
"Paz was with the \"professor\", i.e., the\n"
"KGB.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/5
msgid ""
"Once Coldman discovered that, he figured\n"
"out what was really going on between\n"
"Paz and Gálvez.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/6
msgid ""
"He's trying to figure out how the KGB\n"
"plan to stop Peace Walker,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/7
msgid ""
"and he thinks he can get the info from\n"
"Paz.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/8
msgid ""
"That's crazy! Paz won't know anything.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/9
msgid ""
"Yeah, well, he probably doesn't buy that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/10
msgid ""
"...You think Gálvez has already been\n"
"killed? By grabbing Paz, Coldman's saying...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/11
msgid ""
"\"Stay out of this, or lose your client.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/12
msgid ""
"Dammit! I can't believe we didn't realize\n"
"what was going on before we lost\n"
"contact with Paz.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/13
msgid ""
"Don't have time for that, Kaz.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/15
msgid ""
"Paz needs our help.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/16
msgid ""
"Right. This isn't about money anymore.\n"
"You better move. We know where they're\n"
"headed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/18
msgid ""
"You can thank Amanda.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/19
msgid ""
"Snake, that river you chased the basilisco\n"
"across is the Rio San Juan.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/20
msgid ""
"The other side is our country.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/21
msgid ""
"I had some Nicaraguan compas track it\n"
"there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/22
msgid ""
"They're focos from the GPP (Guerra\n"
"Popular Prolongada) faction,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/23
msgid ""
"so we don't work together so much...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/24
msgid ""
"Where'd it go?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/25
msgid ""
"West, along the border, towards Lago\n"
"Cocibolca.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/26
msgid ""
"There's a U.S. military supply base on the\n"
"southeastern shore of the lake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/27
msgid ""
"Ever since that earthquake two years\n"
"ago, America's had the entire region to\n"
"itself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/28
msgid ""
"That is where the basilisco is. I'm sure of\n"
"it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/29
msgid ""
"Lago Cocibolca... How do I get across the\n"
"border?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/30
msgid ""
"There's a route that we use to cross.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/31
msgid ""
"It's just a little boat, but I can introduce\n"
"you to the captain.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/32
msgid ""
"I appreciate it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/33
msgid ""
"We will never leave Nicaragua at the\n"
"mercy of someone like William Walker\n"
"again.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/34
msgid ""
"Snake, Coldman's going to launch the\n"
"nuke from that base. He's targeting MSF.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/35
msgid ""
"Based on what Huey's told us, it'll take\n"
"two more days to prep for launch.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/36
msgid ""
"...But it looks like there's another reason\n"
"they picked that date.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/38
msgid ""
"Tomorrow is day one of a U.S.-Soviet\n"
"summit in Vladivostok.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/39
msgid ""
"The launch is probably connected\n"
"somehow.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/40
msgid ""
"That's right... They're holding the SALT-II\n"
"(Strategic Arms Limitation Treaty) talks.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/41
msgid ""
"You think Coldman's trying to disrupt the\n"
"negotiations?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/42
msgid ""
"Either that, or use it as a bargaining chip...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/43
msgid ""
"He's still got Paz, too. At any rate, we're\n"
"running out of time.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/44
msgid ""
"I'll figure something out.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390090/0
msgid ""
"Snake, Peace Walker has crossed the\n"
"border\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390090/1
msgid ""
"and entered a U.S. military supply base\n"
"on the southeastern shore of Lago\n"
"Cocibolca.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390090/2
msgid ""
"Coldman's targeting the MSF plant -\n"
"that's us.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390090/3
msgid ""
"Don't let it launch that nuke! Destroy\n"
"Peace Walker!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390250/0
msgid ""
"Snake, Peace Walker's being controlled\n"
"from the control tower! It's to the\n"
"northeast.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390250/1
msgid ""
"Get going! We'll be there to back you up!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390370/0
msgid ""
"Snake, don't let it launch the nuke!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390410/0
msgid ""
"Snake! You have to stop that data from\n"
"being sent!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x3904c0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, we've got a problem. Zadornov's\n"
"not in his cell.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x3904c0/2
msgid ""
"He must have used his prosthetic as a\n"
"blowtorch to cut through the bars.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x3904c0/3
msgid ""
"But we've managed to narrow down his\n"
"location using a transmitter we planted\n"
"on him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x3904c0/4
msgid ""
"I'm adding a new mission. Find the KGB\n"
"agent Zadornov!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x3906d0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, Zadornov has escaped custody.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x3906d0/1
#: codec/2/912/0x390b50/1
#: codec/2/912/0x390e90/1
msgid ""
"Find him!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x3907a0/0
msgid ""
"Heh heh... So you found me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x3907a0/1
msgid ""
"It wasn't hard. What're you up to, anyway?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x3907a0/2
msgid ""
"Just... going for a stroll.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x3907a0/3
msgid ""
"Kaz, I've got Zadornov. Returning home.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x3907a0/4
msgid ""
"Acknowledged, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390940/0
msgid ""
"Bad news, Snake. Zadornov's on the loose.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390940/1
msgid ""
"What, again?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390940/2
msgid ""
"It's funny. We took away his prosthetic\n"
"and did a full body check.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390940/3
msgid ""
"We even increased the guard.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390940/4
msgid ""
"Think he had help?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390940/5
msgid ""
"Impossible. Anyway, I'm adding a new\n"
"mission. Locate and recover Zadornov!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390b50/0
#: codec/2/912/0x390e90/0
msgid ""
"Snake, Zadornov's disappeared from his\n"
"cell again.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390c30/0
msgid ""
"Kaz, I caught Zadornov.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390c30/1
msgid ""
"I-impossible! I thought I'd made it...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390c30/2
msgid ""
"Acknowledged. And appreciated.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390d50/0
msgid ""
"Snake, Zadornov has disappeared from\n"
"his cell.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390d50/1
msgid ""
"What? You're kidding, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390d50/2
msgid ""
"Afraid not. You've got a new mission: find\n"
"Zadornov!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390f70/0
msgid ""
"I got him, Kaz.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390f70/1
msgid ""
"...Slipped up again...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/912/0x390f70/2
msgid ""
"Acknowledged. Bring him on in.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391070/0
msgid ""
"Umm... Snake?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391070/1
msgid ""
"Don't tell me... Zadornov?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391070/2
msgid ""
"Bingo. The guard left his post and the\n"
"dude was gone when he got back.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391070/3
msgid ""
"Sounds like the guard needs a guard.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391070/4
msgid ""
"He was off with the girls. Paz invited him\n"
"to try some of their cooking.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391070/5
msgid ""
"He says he loved every second of it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391070/6
msgid ""
"Is that jealousy, Kaz?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391070/7
msgid ""
"Anyway, there's a new mission waiting for\n"
"you. Find Zadornov, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391070/8
msgid ""
"Okay, okay...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391350/0
#: codec/2/913/0x391350/2
msgid ""
"Snake! Zadornov's done it again!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391350/1
msgid ""
"great...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391350/3
msgid ""
"Gimme a break...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391350/4
msgid ""
"Snake! Listen, Zadornov's done it again!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391350/5
msgid ""
"C'mon!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391350/6
msgid ""
"I hate to entertain the thought, but this\n"
"might be an inside job.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391350/7
msgid ""
"What the hell's he after, anyway?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391350/8
msgid ""
"No clue. Can't imagine he's just out to\n"
"annoy us, though.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391350/9
msgid ""
"You know, it might not be worth keeping\n"
"him here. If he's not going to join us...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391350/10
msgid ""
"You may be right.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391350/11
msgid ""
"I thought it might boost our Russian\n"
"compatriots' morale, but...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391350/12
msgid ""
"OK. I'll think it over.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391350/13
msgid ""
"Let's hope he's just playing\n"
"hide-and-seek...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391350/14
msgid ""
"I've added a new mission. Go get\n"
"Zadornov!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x3917c0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, Zadornov's disappeared again.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x3917c0/1
msgid ""
"Get out there and retrieve him!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x3918a0/0
msgid ""
"Found our friend, Kaz.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x3918a0/1
msgid ""
"...Damn it... And I was so close ...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x3918a0/2
msgid ""
"Great. Good work, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x3919b0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, Zadornov's escaped custody again.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x3919b0/1
msgid ""
"You have to track him down!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391a90/0
msgid ""
"I found him, Kaz.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391a90/1
msgid ""
"Close... but no cigar.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391a90/2
msgid ""
"Not for you, anyway. Snake, We're coming\n"
"to pick him up.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391bb0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, you're not gonna believe this, but...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391bb0/2
msgid ""
"Zadornov's missing again.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391bb0/3
msgid ""
"Kaz, are you sure somebody's not... I don't\n"
"know, letting him out on purpose?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391bb0/4
msgid ""
"You think I have time to assemble a mole\n"
"hunt?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391bb0/5
msgid ""
"Man, this guy isn't just good, he's so good\n"
"it's scary.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391bb0/6
msgid ""
"If he's doing this alone, that is.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391bb0/7
msgid ""
"Anyway, he left a trail, so we've got a\n"
"good idea of where he's probably hiding.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391bb0/8
msgid ""
"You know what the mission is...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391bb0/9
msgid ""
"Find Zadornov, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/913/0x391ef0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, Zadornov's escaped. You have to\n"
"find him!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x3920c0/0
msgid ""
"It, ah, happened again, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x3920c0/1
msgid ""
"Zadornov? What's he got, an escape\n"
"fetish?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x3920c0/2
msgid ""
"He clearly has friends on the inside,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x3920c0/3
msgid ""
"but we've got no way of knowing who.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x3920c0/4
msgid ""
"Ugh. Persistent bastard, I'll give him that.\n"
"Where is he this time?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x3920c0/5
msgid ""
"That's the thing. He must've found and\n"
"gotten rid of the transmitter.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x3920c0/6
msgid ""
"We've got no idea where he is. Snake,\n"
"think you can find him?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x3920c0/7
msgid ""
"...We can't just let him run around -\n"
"makes us look bad.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x3920c0/8
msgid ""
"I'll say. Since we can't locate him, I'm\n"
"afraid I can't add a new mission.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x3920c0/9
msgid ""
"You know what to do, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/0
msgid ""
"Snake, you there?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/1
msgid ""
"Yeah. What's up?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/2
msgid ""
"You've gotta talk to Amanda.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/3
msgid ""
"What happened?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/4
msgid ""
"She wants to leave sickbay and get back\n"
"on the battlefield, but she's not fully\n"
"healed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/5
msgid ""
"She's still in crutches - who'd be crazy\n"
"enough to try and fight like that?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/6
msgid ""
"You have to talk some sense into her.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/7
msgid ""
"Is she with you right now?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/8
msgid ""
"No, she's in sickbay.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/9
msgid ""
"She keeps shouting about how she\n"
"doesn't want to be there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/10
msgid ""
"She won't shut up about it. She's driving\n"
"me-\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/11
msgid ""
"Let her go.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/13
msgid ""
"If that's what she wants, let her go.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/14
msgid ""
"I'm really not in the mood for jokes, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/15
msgid ""
"I'm serious. Let her go.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/16
msgid ""
"Why? So she can come back in a body\n"
"bag?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/17
msgid ""
"I'm really not in the mood for jokes, Kaz.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/19
msgid ""
"Amanda isn't the type to just sit around\n"
"in sickbay.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/20
msgid ""
"She has a sense of duty - her purpose in\n"
"life is to fight.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/21
msgid ""
"The battlefield isn't just the best thing\n"
"for her, it's the best thing for her\n"
"compas, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/22
msgid ""
"She'll be a huge morale boost - that can\n"
"only benefit MSF.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/24
msgid ""
"You're good at fighting, Kaz - one of the\n"
"best...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/25
msgid ""
"but you've got a lot to learn when it\n"
"comes to people.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/26
msgid ""
"... So where should I put her?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/27
msgid ""
"I'll think it over and find a team for her.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/28
msgid ""
"Don't worry, she won't let us down.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392460/29
msgid ""
"Whatever you say, Boss.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392d00/0
msgid ""
"I got a report in from the R&D team.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392d00/1
msgid ""
"They've finished plans for a new hex-type\n"
"plant.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392d00/2
msgid ""
"And today they're gonna start\n"
"construction on the first block.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392d00/3
msgid ""
"Can't wait to finally say goodbye to this\n"
"scrap heap.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392d00/4
msgid ""
"Only thing is, we don't have nearly\n"
"enough GMP.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/914/0x392d00/5
msgid ""
"We'll need to recruit more soldiers to get\n"
"more GMP. You know what to do, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/0
msgid ""
"Got a sec, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/2
msgid ""
"It's about Paz. You know, she doesn't\n"
"have any family.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/3
msgid ""
"She got a scholarship thanks to\n"
"Zadornov, and was living at the dorms...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/4
msgid ""
"But he was KGB.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/5
msgid ""
"All signs are her scholarship came from\n"
"the KGB, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/6
msgid ""
"Even if they let him go, she's not going to\n"
"be seeing any more money.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/7
msgid ""
"It wouldn't have been much anyway.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/8
msgid ""
"So I was wondering, what about letting\n"
"her stay here a while?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/9
msgid ""
"What does she think?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/10
msgid ""
"She says she wants to help out.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/11
msgid ""
"It would only be temporary. She's still in\n"
"shock.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/12
msgid ""
"Right now, no one understands her better\n"
"than we do.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/13
msgid ""
"OK. But Kaz,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/14
msgid ""
"don't take your eyes off her.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/16
msgid ""
"It won't be easy getting used to this kind\n"
"of life.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/17
msgid ""
"I know, Snake. I'm not trying to turn her\n"
"into one of us.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/18
msgid ""
"You should talk to her yourself later.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/20
msgid ""
"And, ah,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/21
msgid ""
"Dr. Strangelove wants to come, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/22
#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/3
msgid ""
"Strangelove?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/23
msgid ""
"Well she's out of a job now, and she'd\n"
"have a problem returning to England.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/24
msgid ""
"You can talk to her about it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/915/0x393270/25
msgid ""
"Anyway, you don't need me to tell you\n"
"how good she'd be for R&D.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, we fitted ZEKE with its own AI Pod.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/1
msgid ""
"We were having trouble adjusting the AI,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/2
msgid ""
"but Dr. Strangelove was able to get it up\n"
"and running.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/4
msgid ""
"Why the surprise, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/5
msgid ""
"Well... We're an army without borders.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/6
msgid ""
"We need a deterrent against foreign\n"
"intervention - that's what ZEKE is for.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/7
msgid ""
"It may even prove necessary to...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/8
msgid ""
"I'm not against deterrence itself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/9
msgid ""
"The problem is when a nation comes to\n"
"rely on it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/10
msgid ""
"All that does is force a burden on its\n"
"people...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/11
msgid ""
"the same people that constitute the\n"
"nation itself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/12
msgid ""
"The existence of nations is detrimental to\n"
"man.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/13
msgid ""
"That's why I, one without a nation, see\n"
"potential in MSF.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/14
msgid ""
"But power is required for you to distance\n"
"yourself from nations.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/15
msgid ""
"I will do whatever I can to assist with that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/16
msgid ""
"...Glad to hear it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/17
msgid ""
"And... I merely lent Huey a helping hand.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/18
msgid ""
"I will not give ZEKE an AI like hers.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x3945b0/19
msgid ""
"I wouldn't expect you to.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/2/916/0x394bd0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, I'm proud to announce that\n"
"preparations for Metal Gear ZEKE are\n"
"complete.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_myo_rad_0080_000_0
#. timeline 1462..2048
#: codec/2/916/0x394bd0/1
msgid ""
"We can activate it any time.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_myo_rad_0080_000_0
#. timeline 2048..2702
#: codec/2/916/0x394bd0/2
msgid ""
"Got it. Thanks, Huey.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_myo_rad_0080_000_0
#. timeline 2758..3176
#: codec/2/916/0x394bd0/3
msgid ""
"No need to thank me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_myo_rad_0080_000_0
#. timeline 3218..4068
#: codec/2/916/0x394bd0/4
msgid ""
"At least now I can finally say I helped you\n"
"with something.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_myo_rad_0080_000_0
#. timeline 4151..4806
#: codec/2/916/0x394bd0/5
msgid ""
"You can use it in Outer Ops, too.\n"
msgstr ""

